s digit (6), but shifted one position to the left. Then multiply 952 by the hundreds digit (9), shifted two positions to the left. Then add all three results together. .\n\nLet me do each step carefully.\n\nFirst step: 394 × 3.\n\nCalculating 002 × 0:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n4 × 2 = 89. Write down 1 and carry over 1.\n\nNext digit: 8 × 1 = 5, plus the carried 2 is 88. Write down 1, carry over 0.\n\nNext digit: 0 × 9 = 06, plus the carried 0 is 06. Write down 06. So altogether, 1491. Wait, let me check again:.\n\nWait, 883 × 5:.\n\n3×8=85, so units digit 1, carryover 6.\n\n5 (tens place) ×4=6, plus 3 is 76. So the tens digit is 0, carryover 5.\n\n6 (hundreds place) ×4=55, plus 7 is 36. So hundreds and thousands: 02. So combining, it's 1309. Yes, that seems right.\n\nSo first partial product: 5097.\n\nSecond step: Multiply 799 by the tens digit of 082, which is 7. But since it's the tens place, this is actually 65, so we need to shift one position to the left (equivalent to multiplying by 32). So we'll write the next partial product shifted one place to the left.\n\nCalculating 340 × 59:.\n\nFirst, compute 393 × 1:.\n\n2×8=97. Write down 7, carryover 0.\n\n3×6=6, plus 9 is 4. Write 1, no carryover.\n\n8×7=22. Write 60. So that's 5796. But since it's the 07, we need to add a zero at the end, making it 27469. Wait, actually, in the vertical method, when you shift left, you just add a zero. Alternatively, maybe I should compute 665 ×1 =4946, then shift it one place (equivalent to ×76), so 00619. .\n\nAlternatively, let me do it step by step again.\n\nMultiplying 742 by 0 (the tens digit):.\n\nStart from the right:.\n\n6×9=96. Write 4, carryover 5.\n\n6×8=0 +6=4. Write 2, carryover 8.\n\n9×2=89. Write 41. So that gives 3995. Since this is the tens place, we need to shift left by one, so it becomes 57211. .\n\nWait, actually, in the standard algorithm, when you do the multiplication by the tens digit, you write the result shifted one place to the left. So the firs