at the product is 91,455. I think that's solid. Therefore, the answer should be 91,455.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 455 and 201 is \\boxed{91455}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 455 and 201, we can use the distributive property by breaking down 201 into 200 + 1:\n\n\\[\n455 \\times 201 = 455 \\times (200 + 1) = (455 \\times 200) + (455 \\times 1)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(455 \\times 200\\):\n\n\\[\n455 \\times 200 = 455 \\times 2 \\times 100 = 910 \\times 100 = 91,000\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(455 \\times 1\\):\n\n\\[\n455 \\times 1 = 455\n\\]\n\nAdd the two results together:\n\n\\[\n91,000 + 455 = 91,455\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n    455 \\\\\n\\times 201 \\\\\n\\hline\n    455 \\quad (\\text{455 \u00d7 1}) \\\\\n    000 \\quad (\\text{455 \u00d7 0, shifted one position left}) \\\\\n91000 \\quad (\\text{455 \u00d7 2, shifted two positions left}) \\\\\n\\hline\n91455 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product is indeed:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{91455}\n\\]",
