n\nThen add 4,932: 120,560 +4,932 = 125,492.\n\nWait, but let me confirm with another method to be sure. Let's do the multiplication step by step:\n\n       548  \n     \u00d7229  \n     -------\n       548 \u00d79 = 4,932  \n      548 \u00d720 =10,960 (shifted one position to the left)  \n     548 \u00d7200 =109,600 (shifted two positions to the left)  \n     -------------------\n      Adding them up:\n\n           4,932  \n          10,960  \n        +109,600  \n        -----------\n          125,492\n\nYes, that seems consistent. Alternatively, using another method: (a + b)(c + d) etc.?\n\nAlternatively, 229 is 230 -1. So 548\u00d7(230 -1) =548\u00d7230 -548\u00d71.\n\nCompute 548\u00d7230 =548\u00d7200 +548\u00d730 =109,600 +16,440 =126,040.\n\nThen subtract 548: 126,040 -548 =126,040 -500 -48 =125,540 -48 =125,492. Same result.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer should be 125,492.\n\nWait, but earlier when I miscalculated with different numbers I got a different result, but after correcting, it's 125,492. Let me check with a calculator approach step by step:\n\nMultiply 548 \u00d7229:\n\nFirst, 548 \u00d7 200 = 109,600.\n\n548 \u00d720 =10,960.\n\n548 \u00d79 =4,932.\n\nAdding those together:\n\n109,600 +10,960 =120,560.\n\n120,560 +4,932 =125,492. Yep.\n\nAlternatively, compute 548\u00d7229:\n\nBreak it into (500 +48) \u00d7 (200 +29).\n\nFirst, 500\u00d7200 =100,000.\n\n500\u00d729 =14,500.\n\n48\u00d7200 =9,600.\n\n48\u00d729 = 1,392.\n\nNow add all four parts:100,000 +14,500 =114,500.\n\n114,500 +9,600 =124,100.\n\n124,100 +1,392 =125,492. Same result again.\n\nTherefore, the product of 548 and 229 is definitely 125,492. I think that's correct. I made a mistake initially by misreading the numbers, but after correcting, all methods give the same answer. So I'm confident that's the right result.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 548 and 229 is \\boxed{125492}.\n</think>\n\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 548 and 229, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm by breaking down the numbers and adding the results together.\n\nFirst, we break down 229 into 200, 20, and 9:\n\\[\n548 \\times 229 = 548 \\times (200 + 20 + 9)\n\\]\n\nNext, we compute each part separately:\n\\[\n548 \\times 200 = 109600\n\\]\n\\[\n548 \\times 20 = 10960\n\\]\n\\[\n548 \\times 9 = 4932\n\\]\n\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n109600 + 10960 = 120560\n\\]\n\\[\n120560 + 4932 = 125492\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this result using another method by expressing 229 as \\(230 - 1\\):\n\\[\n548 \\times 229 = 548 \\times (230 - 1)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 548 \\times 230 - 548 \\times 1\n\\]\n\\[\n= (548 \\times 200 + 548 \\times 30) - 548\n\\]\n\\[\n= (109600 + 16440) - 548\n\\]\n\\[\n= 126040 - 548\n\\]\n\\[\n= 125492\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 548 and 229 is \\(\\boxed{125492}\\).",
