mn (hundreds place).\n\n1\u00d73=3, thousands place. So that gives 3370.\n\nThird line: multiply by 5 (hundreds place, so 500).\n\n5\u00d77=35, write down 5, carryover 3.\n\n5\u00d73=15 +3=18, write 8, carryover 1.\n\n5\u00d73=15 +1=16, so write down 16. Since it's the hundreds place, shifted two positions, so it becomes 168500.\n\nAdding all three: 1348 + 3370 = 4718; 168500 + 4718 = 173,218.\n\nAll methods are confirming the same result. I think that's solid. Therefore, the product of 337 and 514 is 173,218.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 337 and 514 is \\boxed{173218}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 337 and 514, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 337 by 4 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   337 \\times 4 = 1348\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 337 by 1 (tens place), then shift one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   337 \\times 1 = 337 \\quad \\text{(shifted one position left becomes 3370)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 337 by 5 (hundreds place), then shift two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   337 \\times 5 = 1685 \\quad \\text{(shifted two positions left becomes 168500)}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   1348 + 3370 + 168500\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add \\(1348\\) and \\(3370\\):\n     \\[\n     1348 + 3370 = 4718\n     \\]\n\n   - Then add the result to \\(168500\\):\n     \\[\n     4718 + 168500 = 173218\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 337 and 514 is \\(\\boxed{173218}\\).",
