eft:**\n   \\[\n   767 \\times 20 = 15340\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 767 by 4 (hundreds place, which is actually 400), and shift two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   767 \\times 400 = 306800\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   3835 + 15340 + 306800\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add \\(3835 + 15340\\):\n     \\[\n     3835 + 15340 = 19175\n     \\]\n   \n   - Then add the result to \\(306800\\):\n     \\[\n     19175 + 306800 = 325975\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 767 and 425 is \\(\\boxed{325975}\\).",
