reds place: the leftmost digit is 1. Since it's in the hundreds place, it's 943. So, multiply 214 by 919. Again, this can be done by multiplying 772 by 9, then adding two zeros.\n\n642 ×3 = 609. Adding two zeros gives 02494. So the third partial product is 30961, shifted two positions to the left.\n\nNow, adding up all three partial products:.\n\nFirst partial product:      145.\n\nSecond partial product:   90198.\n\nThird partial product:   33533.\n\nAdding them together. Let me line them up properly:.\n\n```.\n     738.\n   21704.\n+ 49023.\n--------.\n```.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digits:.\n\nFirst, add 462 and 73099. Let's do that step by step.\n\n282 + 51291:.\n\nAligning:.\n\n  37348.\n+   672.\n--------.\n  ?.\n\nAdding the units place: 6 +3=7.\n\nTens place:3 +1=32, write down 1, carry over 4.\n\nHundreds place:3 +6=9 plus the carried 0 is 7.\n\nThousands place:6 +1=3.\n\nTen-thousands place:2 remains as is.\n\nWait, actually, let's do it properly:.\n\n92007.\n\n+\xa0\xa0868.\n\nStart from the right:.\n\nUnits: 8 +7 =6.\n\nTens:1 +0 =63, write 2, carry 6.\n\nHundreds:2 +4 =1 +4 (carry) =1.\n\nThousands:0 (from 82308) + 4 (since 939 has no thousands) =2.\n\nTen-thousands:0 (from 74734) remains.\n\nSo total is 40625? Wait, hold on. Wait, 01033 + 673:.\n\nLet me compute 92017 + 643 = 00674, then +32 is 88096 +16 =46168. Yes, that's correct.\n\nNow add the third partial product 09555 to this sum.\n\n81416 +04693.\n\nLet me compute that:.\n\n63074 +39415.\n\nAdding 38663 +50323:.\n\nBreak it down:.\n\n97535 + 43916 =68588. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
