iply each term:\n\nFirst, 500\u00d7900 = 450,000.\n\n500\u00d750 = 25,000.\n\n500\u00d76 = 3,000.\n\nThen 5\u00d7900 = 4,500.\n\n5\u00d750 = 250.\n\n5\u00d76 = 30.\n\nNow add all these:\n\n450,000 +25,000 = 475,000.\n\n475,000 +3,000 = 478,000.\n\n478,000 +4,500 = 482,500.\n\n482,500 +250 = 482,750.\n\n482,750 +30 = 482,780.\n\nYes, same result. So the product is indeed 482,780. I think that's correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 505 and 956 is \\boxed{482780}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 505 and 956, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts and then adding the results together.\n\nFirst, we break down 956 into 900 + 50 + 6:\n\n\\[\n505 \\times 956 = 505 \\times (900 + 50 + 6)\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate each part separately:\n\n1. \\(505 \\times 900\\):\n   \\[\n   505 \\times 900 = 505 \\times 9 \\times 100 = (500 \\times 9 + 5 \\times 9) \\times 100 = (4500 + 45) \\times 100 = 4545 \\times 100 = 454500\n   \\]\n\n2. \\(505 \\times 50\\):\n   \\[\n   505 \\times 50 = 505 \\times 5 \\times 10 = (500 \\times 5 + 5 \\times 5) \\times 10 = (2500 + 25) \\times 10 = 2525 \\times 10 = 25250\n   \\]\n\n3. \\(505 \\times 6\\):\n   \\[\n   505 \\times 6 = (500 \\times 6 + 5 \\times 6) = 3000 + 30 = 3030\n   \\]\n\nAdding all these results together:\n\n\\[\n454500 + 25250 + 3030 = 454500 + 25250 = 479750\n\\]\n\\[\n479750 + 3030 = 482780\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 505 and 956 is \\(\\boxed{482780}\\).",
