ethod to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, using standard multiplication:\n\nMultiply 790 by 198:\n\nFirst, write 790\n\u00d7 198\n________\n\nMultiply 790 by 8: 790 \u00d7 8 = 6,320.\n\nMultiply 790 by 90 (the second digit from right, which is 9 in the tens place, so 9\u00d710=90): 790 \u00d7 90 = 71,100.\n\nMultiply 790 by 100 (the third digit from right, which is 1 in the hundreds place, so 1\u00d7100=100): 790 \u00d7 100 = 79,000.\n\nNow add all three results:\n\n6,320\n+71,100 = 77,420\n\n77,420 + 79,000 = 156,420.\n\nSame result as before. So that checks out.\n\nWait, but in my first mistaken calculation with 019 and 443, I had a different answer, but since the correct numbers are 790 and 198, the answer is 156,420.\n\nAlternatively, another way to compute: 790 \u00d7 200 is 158,000, subtract 790 \u00d7 2 = 1,580 gives 156,420. Yep, that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, I think that is the correct product.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 790 and 198 is \\boxed{156420}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 790 and 198, we can use the distributive property by breaking down 198 into 200 - 2:\n\n\\[\n790 \\times 198 = 790 \\times (200 - 2)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(790 \\times 200\\):\n\n\\[\n790 \\times 200 = 790 \\times 2 \\times 100 = 1580 \\times 100 = 158000\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(790 \\times 2\\):\n\n\\[\n790 \\times 2 = 1580\n\\]\n\nSubtract the second result from the first:\n\n\\[\n158000 - 1580 = 156420\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can use standard multiplication:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   790 \\\\\n\\times 198 \\\\\n\\hline\n   6320 \\quad (\\text{790} \\times 8) \\\\\n  71100 \\quad (\\text{790} \\times 90) \\\\\n+79000 \\quad (\\text{790} \\times 100) \\\\\n\\hline\n  156420 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product is \\(\\boxed{156420}\\).",
