e multiplication, I got confused with the digits and numbers, which led to different results, but now that I approached it step by step, it's clear. So the correct answer should be 85,698.\n\nLet me just confirm with another method, like using a calculator approach.\n\n621 \u00d7 100 = 62,100.\n\n621 \u00d7 38. Wait, maybe 138 is 100+38, so 621\u00d7100 + 621\u00d738.\n\n621\u00d738 can be split into 621\u00d730 + 621\u00d78.\n\n621\u00d730 is 18,630 and 621\u00d78 is 4,968. Adding those gives 18,630 + 4,968 = 23,598.\n\nAdding that to 62,100 gives 62,100 + 23,598 = 85,698. Yep, same result.\n\nTherefore, I think the correct answer is 85,698. The confusion earlier was because I was mixing up the digits and places in my head, leading to errors in the first attempt. Taking it step by step and writing down each part helped clarify.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 621 and 138 is \\boxed{85698}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 621 and 138, we can use the distributive property and the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nFirst, we break down the multiplication using the distributive property:\n\\[\n621 \\times 138 = 621 \\times (100 + 30 + 8)\n\\]\nCalculating each part separately:\n\\[\n621 \\times 100 = 62100\n\\]\n\\[\n621 \\times 30 = 621 \\times 3 \\times 10 = 1863 \\times 10 = 18630\n\\]\n\\[\n621 \\times 8 = 4968\n\\]\n\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n62100 + 18630 + 4968\n\\]\n\nFirst, add \\(62100\\) and \\(18630\\):\n\\[\n62100 + 18630 = 80730\n\\]\n\nThen add the result to \\(4968\\):\n\\[\n80730 + 4968 = 85698\n\\]\n\nUsing the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n     621 \\\\\n   \\times 138 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     4968 \\quad (\\text{621 \u00d7 8}) \\\\\n    18630 \\quad (\\text{621 \u00d7 30}) \\\\\n   62100 \\quad (\\text{621 \u00d7 100}) \\\\\n   \\hline\n   85698 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 621 and 138 is \\(\\boxed{85698}\\).",
