orrect.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 216 and 398 is \\boxed{85968}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 216 and 398, we can use the standard algorithm and verify with the distributive property.\n\n**Using the Standard Algorithm:**\n\n1. **Multiply 216 by 8 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   216 \\times 8 = 1728\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 216 by 9 (tens place, which is 90):**\n   \\[\n   216 \\times 9 = 1944 \\quad \\text{(shifted one position to the left: 19440)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 216 by 3 (hundreds place, which is 300):**\n   \\[\n   216 \\times 3 = 648 \\quad \\text{(shifted two positions to the left: 64800)}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the results together:**\n   \\[\n   1728 + 19440 + 64800 = 85968\n   \\]\n\n**Verification using the Distributive Property:**\n\n1. **Break down 398 as \\(400 - 2\\):**\n   \\[\n   216 \\times 398 = 216 \\times (400 - 2)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate each part separately:**\n   \\[\n   216 \\times 400 = 86400\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   216 \\times 2 = 432\n   \\]\n\n3. **Subtract the results:**\n   \\[\n   86400 - 432 = 85968\n   \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 216 and 398 is \\(\\boxed{85968}\\).",
