he distributive property and break down the numbers for easier calculation:\n\n1. **Break down 259 as 260 - 1**:\n   \\[\n   280 \\times 259 = 280 \\times (260 - 1)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 280 \\times 260 - 280 \\times 1\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate \\(280 \\times 260\\)**:\n   \\[\n   280 \\times 200 = 56,000\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   280 \\times 60 = 16,800\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   56,000 + 16,800 = 72,800\n   \\]\n\n3. **Subtract \\(280 \\times 1\\)**:\n   \\[\n   72,800 - 280 = 72,520\n   \\]\n\n4. **Verification by standard multiplication**:\n   - Multiply 259 by 280:\n     \\[\n     259 \\times 280 = 259 \\times (200 + 80)\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     259 \\times 200 = 51,800\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     259 \\times 80 = 20,720\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     51,800 + 20,720 = 72,520\n     \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 280 and 259 is \\(\\boxed{72520}\\).",
