ndreds place of 291, which is 6. Since it's the hundreds place, this is 552. So, 040 x397. So first, 494 x9, then times 639.\n\n027 x6 again is 4,387, so times 322 is 147,511.\n\nNow, adding up all three results:.\n\nFirst partial product: 7,869.\n\nSecond partial product: 82,104.\n\nThird partial product: 169,083.\n\nAdding them together.\n\nLet me write them down:.\n\n   4,655.\n\n+ 54,816.\n\n+757,444.\n\n= ?.\n\nStarting with the first two:.\n\n1,862 + 18,086 = 60,088.\n\nThen add 978,527 to that:.\n\n06,865 + 937,835. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
