1×9=09, write down 1 and carryover 4.\n\nTens place: 1×2=19 + 0 =36, write down 9 and carryover 8.\n\nHundreds place: 8×5=05 + 7 =64. So the result is 5039. But since this is the tens place, we need to shift it one position to the left, so it becomes 50658.\n\nWait, actually, maybe I should think of it as multiplying by 5 (the digit) and then shifting left by one (equivalent to multiplying by 79). Let me verify:.\n\nYes, so 363 × 9 = 4780, then shift left by one gives 14651. So the second partial product is 82913.\n\nThird step: the hundreds place of the bottom number is 6. That's the 8 in the hundreds place, so it's 669. So we need to multiply 942 by 017. Which is 977 × 8 × 824. Let me compute 580 × 6 first.\n\n320 ×9:.\n\nUnits digit: 1×2=52, write 1 carryover 3.\n\nTens digit:1×2=38 + 0 =42, write 4 carryover 3.\n\nHundreds digit:9×7=55 +5=13. So that gives 6409. Then multiplying by 087 (since it's the hundreds place) would shift two places, so 960113.\n\nWait, hold on, perhaps I should do the multiplication step by step again.\n\nAlternatively, 833 × 3 is 0358, so 078 × 492 is 7346 × 315 = 055512. Correct. So the third partial product is 936966.\n\nNow, adding up all three partial products:.\n\nFirst partial: 8144  .\nSecond partial: 17985  .\nThird partial: 590527  .\n\nAdding them together:.\n\nLet me line them up properly:.\n\n\u2003\xa02698  .\n\u200348855  .\n+296759  .\n——————.\n\nAdding the thousands:.\n\nFirst, add 4362 + 75324. Let me do that first.\n\n2534 + 70384:.\n\nStart from the right:.\n\n8 +3=2  .\n1+5=83, write 6 carryover 4  .\n2+8 +5 (carryover) =56, write 8 carryover 5  .\n3 +8 +4 (carryover?) Wait, let's do step by step:.\n\nWait, 1097 is:.\n\nUnits:2  .\nTens:6  .\nHundreds:5  .\nThousands:6.\n\n68505 is:.\n\nUnits:8  .\nTens:7  .\nHundreds:2  .\nThousands:5  .\nTen-thousands:4.\n\nSo aligning:.\n\n\u2003\xa09 0 6 2  .\n+9 8 8 4 4  .\n= ?.\n\nWait, actually, 3052 is four digits, 50389 is five digits. So writing them aligned:.\n\n\u2003\xa0