wn as the first partial product: 1,494.\n\nNext, the middle digit is 9, which is in the tens place, so it represents 90. Multiply 90 by 498.\n\n9 \u00d7 498 = 4,482. Since it's the tens place, we write this as 44,820 (shifted one position to the left).\n\nThird, the leftmost digit is 6, which is in the hundreds place, so it represents 600. Multiply 600 by 498.\n\n6 \u00d7 498 = 2,988. Since it's the hundreds place, write this as 298,800 (shifted two positions to the left).\n\nNow, add all the partial products together:\n\n1,494\n\n+44,820\n\n+298,800\n\nLet's add them step by step.\n\nFirst, 1,494 + 44,820 = 46,314.\n\nThen, add 298,800 to 46,314:\n\n46,314 + 298,800 = 345,114.\n\nWait, so according to this method, the product is 345,114.\n\nBut let me verify with another method to ensure correctness. Let's try the distributive property again.\n\nBreaking down 498 and 693.\n\n498 can be written as 500 - 2.\n\n693 can be written as 700 - 7.\n\nTherefore, (500 - 2) \u00d7 (700 - 7).\n\nUsing the distributive property (FOIL method):\n\n= 500\u00d7700 - 500\u00d77 - 2\u00d7700 + 2\u00d77\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n500\u00d7700 = 350,000.\n\n500\u00d77 = 3,500.\n\n2\u00d7700 = 1,400.\n\n2\u00d77 = 14.\n\nSo putting it all together:\n\n350,000 - 3,500 - 1,400 + 14.\n\nFirst subtract 3,500 from 350,000: 350,000 - 3,500 = 346,500.\n\nThen subtract 1,400: 346,500 - 1,400 = 345,100.\n\nThen add 14: 345,100 + 14 = 345,114.\n\nOkay, so that matches the previous result. So the correct answer should be 345,114.\n\nWait, but in my first attempt I messed up the numbers entirely, but after correcting myself, both methods give 345,114. Let me try another way to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, using the standard algorithm again step by step:\n\nMultiplying 498 \u00d7 693.\n\nFirst, multiply 498 by 3 (units place):\n\n498 \u00d7 3 = 1,494.\n\nThen multiply 498 by 90 (tens place):\n\n498 \u00d7 9 = 4,482; adding a zero gives 44,820.\n\nThen multiply 498 by 600 (hundreds place):\n\n498 \u00d7