? Because in my second method I miscalculated the terms. So the correct product is 162,692.\n\nWait, but hold on, the original problem was 535 and 814? Or was it 535 and 814? Wait, hold on, the user's question was \"What is the Product of 703 and 973?\" but in the middle of my thinking, I was talking about 535 and 814. Wait, this is confusing. Did I mix up numbers?\n\nWait a second, let me check again. The user wrote: \"Please solve the math problem. Question: What is the Product of 703 and 973?\" But in my thinking process, I started with 535 and 814? That must have been a mistake. Oh no! I must have misread the problem initially. So I need to start over.\n\nThe actual problem is 703 multiplied by 973, not 535 and 814. That's a big mistake. So I need to redo the calculation with the correct numbers.\n\nAlright, so let's tackle 703 \u00d7 973. Let me write that down.\n\nFirst, I can use the standard multiplication algorithm here. Let me break it down step by step.\n\nFirst, write the numbers vertically:\n\n\u2003\u202f703\n\n\u00d7 973\n\n--------\n\nWe'll multiply each digit of the bottom number (973) with the top number (703), starting from the rightmost digit.\n\nStep 1: Multiply 703 by 3 (the units place of 973).\n\n703 \u00d7 3 = 2,109\n\nStep 2: Multiply 703 by 7 (the tens place of 973). Since this is the tens place, the result will be shifted one position to the left.\n\n703 \u00d7 7 = 4,921 \u2192 shifted becomes 49,210\n\nStep 3: Multiply 703 by 9 (the hundreds place of 973), shifted two positions to the left.\n\n703 \u00d7 9 = 6,327 \u2192 shifted becomes 632,700\n\nNow, add all three results together:\n\n\u2003\u202f2,109\n\n+49,210\n\n+632,700\n\n------------\n\nLet's add them step by step.\n\nFirst, 2,109 + 49,210:\n\n2,109 + 49,210 = 51,319\n\nThen add 632,700 to that:\n\n51,319 + 632,700 = 684,019\n\nWait, but let me check the calculations again to make sure.\n\nFirst multiplication: 703 \u00d7 3:\n\n700 \u00d73 = 2100,\n\n3 \u00d73 =9,\n\nso total is