 +2,919 =684,019. Same result. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 703 and 973 is 684,019.\n\nWait, but I need to confirm once more because sometimes even after multiple checks, there can be an error. Let me try using another approach.\n\nLet me use the formula (a + b)(c + d) = ac + ad + bc + bd, breaking into parts.\n\nLet me consider 703 as 700 +3 and 973 as 900 +73.\n\nSo:\n\n(700 +3)(900 +73) =700\u00d7900 +700\u00d773 +3\u00d7900 +3\u00d773.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n700\u00d7900 =630,000.\n\n700\u00d773: 700\u00d770=49,000 and 700\u00d73=2,100, so 49,000+2,100=51,100.\n\nWait, 73 is 70+3, so 700\u00d773 =700*(70+3)=49,000+2,100=51,100.\n\n3\u00d7900=2,700.\n\n3\u00d773=219.\n\nAdding all terms:\n\n630,000 +51,100 =681,100.\n\n681,100 +2,700 =683,800.\n\n683,800 +219 =684,019. Yep, same result.\n\nOkay, so I think that's correct. Therefore, the answer should be 684,019.\n\nBut just to be absolutely thorough, perhaps perform the multiplication step-by-step again.\n\nLet me write it out in long multiplication:\n\n       703\n     \u00d7 973\n     --------\nStep 1: Multiply by 3 (units place):\n703 \u00d7 3:\n3\u00d73=9 (units)\n3\u00d70=0 (tens)\n3\u00d77=21 (hundreds)\nSo 2,109. Correct.\n\nStep 2: Multiply by 7 (tens place, so shifted one to the left):\n703 \u00d77:\n7\u00d73=21 (units place, but shifted left so it's tens place)\nWrite down 1 and carry over 2.\n7\u00d70=0 + carryover 2 =2 (next digit)\n7\u00d77=49 (next digit, which is hundreds place)\nSo it's 4921. Shifted left once gives 49210. Correct.\n\nStep 3: Multiply by 9 (hundreds place, shifted two to the left):\n703 \u00d79:\n9\u00d73=27 (units, shifted two places becomes hundreds)\nWrite 7, carryover 2.\n9\u00d70=0 + carryover 2 =2 (tens place)\n9\u00d77=63 +0 (since no more digits) =63 (hundreds place)\nSo 6327. Shifted two places: 632700. Correct.\n\nAdding:\n\n      2109\n    +49210\n    +632700\n    ---------\nStart with 2109 +49210:\n\n2109 +49210:\n\n2109 + 49210:\n\n2,109 + 49,210 = 51,319.\n\nThen 51,319 +632,700:\n\n51,319 + 600,000 = 651,319.\n\n651,319 +32,700 = 684,019.\n\nYes, so all steps confirm the same result. Therefore, I can confidently say the product is 684,019.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 703 and 973 is \\boxed{684019}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 703 and 973, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 703 by 3 (units place of 973):**\n   \\[\n   703 \\times 3 = 2109\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 703 by 7 (tens place of 973), shifted one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   703 \\times 7 = 4921 \\quad \\text{(shifted to 49210)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 703 by 9 (hundreds place of 973), shifted two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   703 \\times 9 = 6327 \\quad \\text{(shifted to 632700)}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the results together:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     2109 \\\\\n   + 49210 \\\\\n   + 632700 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     684019 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add \\(2109 + 49210\\):\n     \\[\n     2109 + 49210 = 51319\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(632700\\):\n     \\[\n     51319 + 632700 = 684019\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 703 and 973 is \\(\\boxed{684019}\\).",
