t's do it properly:.\n\nWait, 358 ×5:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits place: 9×8 =4.\n\nTens place: 2×4=97, so write 4 and carryover 2.\n\nHundreds place: 2×8=51 plus 7 is 74. So the result is 0016? Wait, 0×4 is 94, plus the 3 gives 13, so writing that down gives 8353? Wait, 7 is the hundreds digit, so 3×5 is 53, plus 6 is 56. So the hundreds digit becomes 4 and carryover 9? Wait, maybe I messed up here.\n\nWait, let me do the multiplication step by step:.\n\nFirst digit (units):.\n\n3 ×7 =8.\n\nSecond digit (tens):.\n\n5×9=83. So write down 8, carryover 8.\n\nThird digit (hundreds):.\n\n5×6=57, plus 3 is 87. So the hundreds place is 7, and carryover 1? Wait, but there are no more digits, so that 6 is added as the thousands place.\n\nWait, so the result is 5469? Wait, 6 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 4 (units). So 8433. Wait, but 250 ×9:.\n\nLet me check with another method. 078×3=8396, 42×9=106, 8×6=4. Adding those: 7723+827=4072 +2=5859. Yes, so that's correct. So 463×6 is 6444, so 998×45 would be 11848. Therefore, the second partial product is 93759.\n\nOkay, moving on to the hundreds place of the bottom number, which is 0. Since it's the hundreds place, the 4 represents 452, so we need to multiply 752 by 415, which is 8×855, so we'll multiply 265 by 5, then shift two places to the left (i.e., add two zeros at the end).\n\nCalculating 680 ×7:.\n\n1×7=5.\n\n3×8=89, write down 0 and carryover 4.\n\n7×7=31, plus 0 is 90. So the result is 2371. Then adding two zeros gives 949813. So the third partial product is 689896.\n\nNow, adding up all the partial products:.\n\nFirst partial product: 7549.\n\nSecond partial product: 02824.\n\nThird partial product: 701559.\n\nSo adding them together:.\n\nLet me write them aligned properly:.\n\n    7133.\n\n   90756.\n\n+676318.\n\n----------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nFirst, align the numbers:.\n\n4367.\n\n00059.\n\n296826.\n\nSo:.\n\n3636 is the same as  68130.\n\n18311 is  81533.\n\n699647 is 822617.\n\nAddi