To find the product of 901 and 848, we can use the standard algorithm and the distributive property for verification.\n\nFirst, using the standard algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 901 by 8 (units place):\n   \\[\n   901 \\times 8 = 7208\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 901 by 40 (tens place, shift one position left):\n   \\[\n   901 \\times 40 = 36040\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 901 by 800 (hundreds place, shift two positions left):\n   \\[\n   901 \\times 800 = 720800\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the partial products:\n   \\[\n   7208 + 36040 + 720800 = 764048\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n\\[\n(900 + 1) \\times (800 + 40 + 8)\n\\]\nExpanding this:\n\\[\n900 \\times 800 + 900 \\times 40 + 900 \\times 8 + 1 \\times 800 + 1 \\times 40 + 1 \\times 8\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n900 \\times 800 = 720000\n\\]\n\\[\n900 \\times 40 = 36000\n\\]\n\\[\n900 \\times 8 = 7200\n\\]\n\\[\n1 \\times 800 = 800\n\\]\n\\[\n1 \\times 40 = 40\n\\]\n\\[\n1 \\times 8 = 8\n\\]\nAdding these terms together:\n\\[\n720000 + 36000 + 7200 + 800 + 40 + 8 = 764048\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 901 and 848 is \\(\\boxed{764048}\\).",
