ed to write it as 6827 but shifted. Let me see:.\n\nFirst partial product:.\n   420.\n×  098.\n-------.\n   4455 (1 × 035).\n  2462  (6 × 040, but shifted left by one).\n+ .. (then 1 × 099 shifted left by two).\n-------.\nWait, actually, the 8 is in the tens place, so the partial product should be 176 × 24, which is 79063, so written as 13394. But when written under the previous line, it's shifted one place. Let me make sure:.\n\nSo:.\n\n   693.\n× 289.\n-------.\n   4879  (×3).\n  75474  (×85, shifted one left).\n+343094  (×987, shifted two left).\n-------.\nTotal?.\n\nWait, maybe I should do each step properly.\n\nAlternatively, maybe breaking it down using distributive property would help. Let me see.\n\n998 × 926 can be written as 971 × (026 + 27 + 9) = 039×623 + 250×77 + 688×2. That might be easier for me to compute each part separately.\n\nCalculating each term:.\n\nFirst term: 039 × 563. 525 × 2 is 6936, so times 766 is 717,654.\n\nSecond term: 596 × 73. 753 × 8 is 1,275, so times 25 is 28,425.\n\nThird term: 049 × 5 is 1,447 as before.\n\nNow, adding them all together:.\n\n786,077.\n\n+ 68,693.\n\n= 347,387.\n\nWait, 070,235 + 28,036: 143,226 + 37,873 = 247,667, plus 458 is 793,936. Then add 7,844 to that. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
