\n50,904 +80,800 = 131,704.\n\nWait, that seems plausible. Let me check my steps again to be sure.\n\nFirst partial product: 3 \u00d7 808 = 2424. Correct.\n\nSecond partial product: 6 \u00d7 808 = 4848, shifted one digit (\u00d710) gives 48,480. Correct.\n\nThird partial product: 1 \u00d7 808 = 808, shifted two digits (\u00d7100) gives 80,800. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 2424 + 48,480 = 50,904. Then 50,904 +80,800 = 131,704.\n\nHmm, so the total is 131,704?\n\nWait, but let me check with another method to confirm. Maybe using distributive property:\n\n163 \u00d7 808 = (100 + 60 + 3) \u00d7 (800 + 8).\n\nMultiply each term:\n\nFirst, 100\u00d7800 = 80,000\n\n100\u00d78 = 800\n\n60\u00d7800 = 48,000\n\n60\u00d78 = 480\n\n3\u00d7800 = 2,400\n\n3\u00d78 =24\n\nNow add all these together:\n\n80,000 + 800 = 80,800\n\n48,000 + 480 = 48,480\n\n2,400 +24=2,424\n\nNow add those results:\n\n80,800 +48,480 = 129,280\n\n129,280 +2,424 = 131,704.\n\nSame result. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use calculator-like multiplication:\n\n808 \u00d7 163.\n\nBreakdown:\n\nFirst, 808 \u00d7 100 = 80,800\n\n808 \u00d7 60 = 48,480\n\n808 \u00d73 = 2,424\n\nAdding those gives 80,800 +48,480 = 129,280 +2,424 = 131,704. Yep.\n\nTherefore, the product of 163 and 808 is 131,704.\n\nBut wait, the original question was \"What is the Product of 163 and 808?\" So it should be 163 \u00d7808, not 808 \u00d7163, but multiplication is commutative, so it's the same result. So the answer is 131,704.\n\nBut let me confirm once again using another method to be thorough.\n\nLet me compute 163 \u00d7 800 first, which is 163 \u00d78 \u00d7100. 163\u00d78 is 1,304. Then \u00d7100 is 130,400.\n\nThen add 163 \u00d78 (since 808 is 800 +8):\n\nWait, no, that's not correct. Wait, 808 is 800 +8, so:\n\n163 \u00d7 (800 +8) = 163\u00d7800 +163\u00d78.\n\n163\u00d7800= (163\u00d78)\u00d7100 = 1,304\u00d7100 =130,400.\n\n163\u00d78: 160\u00d78=1,280 and 3\u00d78=24, so total 1,304.\n\nTherefore, total is 130,400