pute that: 40\u00d728 = 1,120 and 7\u00d728 = 196, so total 1,120 + 196 = 1,316.\n\nNow add all four terms:\n\n120,000 + 5,600 = 125,600\n\n125,600 + 28,200 = 153,800\n\n153,800 + 1,316 = 155,116. Okay, so that matches the standard algorithm. So my first attempt with the distributive property must have had an error in splitting the numbers or arithmetic.\n\nPerhaps I made a mistake in splitting the numbers into different parts. Let me check the initial breakdown again.\n\nWait, the user's question is actually for 725 and 845, not 247 and 628. Oh no! I must have misread the problem. Let me start over.\n\nThe question is: What is the product of 725 and 845?\n\nOkay, so my initial mistake was misreading the numbers as 247 and 628. That's a problem. Let me correct that.\n\nFirst, I'll try the standard algorithm approach with 725 \u00d7 845.\n\nLet me write it down:\n\n       725\n     \u00d7 845\n     ---------\n\nBreaking it down:\n\nMultiply 725 by 5: 725\u00d75 = 3,625\n\nMultiply 725 by 40: 725\u00d740 = 29,000\n\nMultiply 725 by 800: 725\u00d7800 = 580,000\n\nNow add them all together:\n\n3,625 + 29,000 = 32,625\n\n32,625 + 580,000 = 612,625\n\nWait, is that correct? Let me verify step by step.\n\nFirst, 725 \u00d7 5: 5\u00d75 is 25, write down 5 and carryover 2. 5\u00d72 is 10 plus 2 is 12, write down 2 and carryover 1. 5\u00d77 is 35 plus 1 is 36. So 3,625. That's right.\n\nThen 725 \u00d7 40: since it's 40, multiply by 4 and add a zero. 4\u00d7725 is 2,900. Adding a zero gives 29,000. Correct.\n\nThen 725 \u00d7 800: 8\u00d7725 is 5,800. Adding two zeros gives 580,000. Correct.\n\nAdding them up: 3,625 + 29,000 = 32,625. Then 32,625 + 580,000 = 612,625. Hmm, that seems straightforward.\n\nAlternatively, let me compute using another method to cross-verify.\n\nAnother way: Use the distributive property by splitting both numbers.\n\n725 can be split as 700 + 25, and 845 can be split as 800 + 45.\n\nSo (700 + 25)(800 + 45) = 700\u00d7800 + 700\u00d745 + 25\u00d7800 + 25\u00d745.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n700\u00d7800 = 560,000\n\n700\u00d745: 700\u00d740 = 28,000 and 700\u00d75 = 3,500 \u2192 total 31,500\n\n25\u00d7800 = 20,000\n\n25\u00d745: 25\u00d740 = 1,000 and 25\u00d75 = 125 \u2192 total 1,125\n\nNow adding all terms:\n\n560,000 + 31,500 = 591,500\n\n591,500 + 20,000 = 611,500\n\n611,500 + 1,125 = 612,625. Same result.\n\nHmm, okay, so that seems consistent. But let me try another approach, maybe using the difference of squares or some trick?\n\nAlternatively, note that 725 and 845. Let's see if they can be expressed in terms that make multiplication easier. For instance, 725 is 700 + 25, and 845 is 800 + 45, which is what I did above. Alternatively, maybe 845 is 850 - 5, and 725 is 700 + 25. Let's see:\n\n(700 + 25)(850 - 5) = 700\u00d7850 + 700\u00d7(-5) +25\u00d7850 +25\u00d7(-5)\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n700\u00d7850: 700\u00d7800 = 560,000; 700\u00d750 = 35,000 \u2192 total 595,000\n\n700\u00d7-5 = -3,500\n\n25\u00d7850: 25\u00d7800 = 20,000; 25\u00d750 = 1,250 \u2192 total 21,250\n\n25\u00d7-5 = -125\n\nAdding all terms:\n\n595,000 - 3,500 = 591,500\n\n591,500 + 21,250 = 612,750\n\n612,750 - 125 = 612,625. Same result again. So that's good.\n\nAlternatively, maybe compute 725 \u00d7 800 first, then add 725 \u00d745?\n\nWait, 725\u00d7845 is 725\u00d7(800 + 45) = 725\u00d7800 + 725\u00d745.\n\n725\u00d7800 is 725\u00d78\u00d7100 = 5,800\u00d7100 = 580,000. Wait, no: 725\u00d78 is 5,800? Let me check:\n\n725\u00d78: 700\u00d78=5,600; 25\u00d78=200 \u2192 total 5,800. So \u00d7100 is 580,000. That's correct.\n\nThen 725\u00d745: let's compute that. 725\u00d740 = 29,000 and 725\u00d75 = 3,625 \u2192 total 29,000 + 3,625 = 32,625.\n\nAdding to 580,000: 580,000 +32,625 = 612,625. Same result again. So that's consistent.\n\nHmm, so all methods point to 612,625. Let me confirm once more with another approach, perhaps using the standard multiplication vertically:\n\n       725\n     \u00d7 845\n     --------\n         3,625  (725 \u00d7 5)\n        29,000   (725 \u00d7 40, shifted one position)\n      580,000    (725 \u00d7 800, shifted two positions)\n     -------------\n      612,625\n\nYes, that's the same as before. So I think that's the correct answer. However, let me check with a calculator to be absolutely sure.\n\nWait, since I don't have a calculator here, perhaps I can compute 725 \u00d7 845 in another way. Let me try cross-multiplication.\n\nAlternatively, note that 725 \u00d7 845 can be written as (700 + 25)(800 + 45). Wait, that's what I already did. Alternatively, maybe using (a+b)(a-b) formula? Not sure if applicable here.\n\nAlternatively, compute 725 \u00d7 845 as follows:\n\nFirst, compute 700 \u00d7 800 = 560,000\n\nThen 700 \u00d7 45 = 31,500\n\n25 \u00d7 800 = 20,000\n\n25 \u00d7 45 = 1,125\n\nAdding them all gives 560k + 31.5k = 591.5k + 20k = 611.5k + 1.125k = 612,625. Yep.\n\nAlternatively, compute 725 \u00d7 845:\n\nLet me think of 725 as 5\u00d7145, and 845 as 5\u00d7169. So the product is 25 \u00d7 145 \u00d7 169.\n\nCalculating 145 \u00d7 169 first:\n\n145\u00d7170 = 145\u00d7100 + 145\u00d770 = 14,500 + 10,150 = 24,650. But since it's 169, subtract 145: 24,650 - 145 = 24,505. Then multiply by 25: 24,505 \u00d725.\n\n24,505 \u00d7 25: 24,505 \u00d7 100 = 2,450,500 divided by 4 (since 25 is a quarter of 100). Wait, 25 is a quarter of 100, so 24,505 \u00d725 = (24,505 \u00d7100)/4 = 2,450,500 /4 = 612,625. Exactly. So that works too.\n\nWow, that's a good method. So breaking into factors and simplifying.\n\nTherefore, the product of 725 and 845 is 612,625.\n\nWait, but let me make sure I didn't make a mistake in the 145\u00d7169 part. Let's recompute that:\n\n145 \u00d7 169:\n\nBreak 169 into 170 -1.\n\nSo 145\u00d7170 = 145\u00d7(100 + 70) = 145\u00d7100 + 145\u00d770 = 14,500 + 10,150 = 24,650. Then subtract 145\u00d71 = 145, so 24,650 - 145 = 24,505. Correct.\n\nThen 24,505 \u00d725: 24,505 \u00d7 20 = 490,100; 24,505 \u00d75 = 122,525. Adding those