the product of 216 and 124, we can use the standard algorithm and verify with different methods:\n\n1. **Standard Algorithm:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     \\quad 216 \\\\\n   \\times \\quad 124 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     \\quad 864 \\quad (\\text{216 \u00d7 4}) \\\\\n   + \\quad 4320 \\quad (\\text{216 \u00d7 20, shifted one position left}) \\\\\n   + 21600 \\quad (\\text{216 \u00d7 100, shifted two positions left}) \\\\\n   \\hline\n     \\quad 26784 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Distributive Property:**\n   \\[\n   216 \\times 124 = 216 \\times (100 + 20 + 4) = 216 \\times 100 + 216 \\times 20 + 216 \\times 4\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   216 \\times 100 = 21600, \\quad 216 \\times 20 = 4320, \\quad 216 \\times 4 = 864\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   21600 + 4320 + 864 = 26784\n   \\]\n\n3. **Alternative Breakdown:**\n   \\[\n   216 \\times 124 = (200 + 16) \\times 124 = 200 \\times 124 + 16 \\times 124\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   200 \\times 124 = 24800, \\quad 16 \\times 124 = 1984\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   24800 + 1984 = 26784\n   \\]\n\n4. **Using Difference of Terms:**\n   \\[\n   216 \\times 124 = 216 \\times (125 - 1) = 216 \\times 125 - 216\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   216 \\times 125 = \\frac{216 \\times 1000}{8} = 27000\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   27000 - 216 = 26784\n   \\]\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent. Therefore, the product of 216 and 124 is \\(\\boxed{26784}\\).",
