\n\nSecond partial product: 24461.\n\nThird partial product: 00378.\n\nAdding them together. Let's line them up properly:.\n\n     9149.\n    23565.\n+ 27516.\n---------.\n    .\nStarting from the rightmost digit:.\n\n7 + 3 + 8 = 6.\n\n3 + 4 + 1 = 4.\n\n1 + 7 + 6 = 6.\n\n0 + 5 + 4 = 76 (write down 9, carry over 3).\n\n8 (from the first number, since it's only four digits) plus the carried-over 0 = 2.\n\nWait, hold on, maybe I should write it out step by step to avoid confusion.\n\nLet me write each number aligned:.\n\n      2824.\n     55683.\n+  11617.\n----------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits place: 9 + 5 + 1 = 6.\n\nTens place: 1 + 9 + 7 = 6.\n\nHundreds place: 1 + 2 + 6 = 6.\n\nThousands place: 7 + 5 + 2 = 69. So write 1, carry over 7.\n\nTen-thousands place: 5 (from 9413) + 0 (from 31959) + 0 (from 92221) plus the carried-over 2. Wait a second, maybe I messed up the alignment here. Let me check the actual positions again.\n\nWait, perhaps I need to make sure all the numbers are properly aligned by place value. Let me write them with commas for clarity:.\n\n6,835.\n\n84,001.\n\n77,891.\n\nAdding these together:.\n\nFirst, write all numbers vertically:.\n\n      2,639.\n     93,769.\n+  57,311.\n----------.\n    .\nAdding the units digits: 3 + 8 + 8 = 3.\n\nTens place: 9 + 5 + 1 = 0.\n\nHundreds place: 8 + 8 + 6 = 2.\n\nThousands place: 5 (from 0,132) + 4 (from 36,015) + 9 (from 98,887) = 7 + 0 is 27, plus 6 is 59. So write 1 and carry over 2.\n\nTen-thousands place: The first number (7,094) doesn't have a digit here, so 1. The second number (85,511) has 3 in the ten-thousands place? Wait, 87,934 is 7 (ten thousands?), no, 22,591 is 1 (ten thousands place) is 4? Wait, let me parse each number:.\n\n9,992 is 2 thousands, 5 hundreds, 8 tens, 3 units.\n\n87,602 is 2 ten thousands, 1 thousands, 9 hundreds, 8 tens, 9 units.\n\n64,633 is 7 ten thousands, 6 thousands, 7 hundreds, 4 tens, 7 units.\n\nWait a second, so when adding, the ten-thousands place:.\n\nFir