edoing it step by step, both methods give the same result. Therefore, I'm confident that 317 multiplied by 996 is 315,732.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 317 and 996 is \\boxed{315732}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 317 and 996, we can use the distributive property by recognizing that 996 can be expressed as 1000 - 4. \n\nFirst, we calculate the product using this breakdown:\n\\[\n317 \\times 996 = 317 \\times (1000 - 4)\n\\]\n\nNext, we apply the distributive property:\n\\[\n317 \\times 1000 - 317 \\times 4\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n\\[\n317 \\times 1000 = 317000\n\\]\n\\[\n317 \\times 4 = 1268\n\\]\n\nSubtracting the second result from the first:\n\\[\n317000 - 1268 = 315732\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 317 and 996 is \\(\\boxed{315732}\\).",
