t me verify:\n\n200 \u00d74=800\n\n90\u00d74=360 \u2192 total 1160\n\n2\u00d74=8 \u2192 total 1168. Yes, that's correct. So since it's the tens place, we need to shift one position to the left, so it becomes 11680.\n\nWait, but actually, when you multiply by the tens digit, you shift one place, so it's 292\u00d74\u00d710 = 1168\u00d710=11680. That's correct.\n\nThird partial product: 292 \u00d73 (hundreds place of 345), which is 300. So we shift two places to the left (equivalent to multiplying by 300).\n\nFirst compute 292 \u00d73:\n\n2\u00d73=6\n\n9\u00d73=27, carryover 2\n\n2\u00d73=6 +2=8\n\nSo 292\u00d73 is 876. Then shifted two places left becomes 87600.\n\nNow, add all three partial products:\n\n1460\n\n+11680\n\n+87600\n\n--------\n\nLet's add them step by step.\n\nFirst, 1460 + 11680:\n\n1460 + 11680 = 13140.\n\nThen add 87600 to that total:\n\n13140 + 87600 = 100,740.\n\nWait, let me check:\n\n1460 + 11,680:\n\nAdding 1,460 + 11,680:\n\n1,460 + 10,000 = 11,460\n\n11,460 + 1,680 = 13,140. Correct.\n\nThen 13,140 + 87,600:\n\n13,140 + 80,000 = 93,140\n\n93,140 + 7,600 = 100,740. Yes.\n\nTherefore, the product of 292 and 345 is 100,740.\n\nWait a second, let me verify with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternative method: Break down the numbers using distributive property.\n\n292 \u00d7 345 = 292 \u00d7 (300 + 40 +5) = (292\u00d7300) + (292\u00d740) + (292\u00d75)\n\nCompute each term:\n\n292\u00d7300 = 292\u00d73\u00d7100 = 876\u00d7100=87,600\n\n292\u00d740 = 292\u00d74\u00d710 = 1,168\u00d710=11,680\n\n292\u00d75=1,460\n\nAdding them together: 87,600 +11,680 = 99,280; then +1,460 = 100,740. Same result. Okay, that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another approach, like the lattice method or the box method, but since I got the same answer with two methods, I think it's correct.\n\nAlternatively, check using estimation:\n\n292 is close to 300, and 345 is close to 350. 300\u00d7350=105,000. Our answer 100,740 is a bit less, which makes sense because both numbers were rounded up. So that seems plausible.\n\nAlternatively, compute 292\u00d7345:\n\nLet me do 292\u00d7345:\n\nFirst, 300\u00d7345 = 103,500\n\nSubtract 8\u00d7345 (since 292 is 300-8)\n\n8\u00d7345= 2,760\n\nTherefore, 103,500 - 2,760 = 100,740. Exactly the same. So that confirms it again.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident the answer is 100,740.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 292 and 345 is \\boxed{100740}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 292 and 345, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **First partial product (units place):**\n   \\[\n   292 \\times 5 = 1460\n   \\]\n   Calculation: \\(2 \\times 5 = 10\\), \\(9 \\times 5 = 45\\), \\(2 \\times 5 = 10\\) with appropriate carries, resulting in 1460.\n\n2. **Second partial product (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   292 \\times 40 = 11680\n   \\]\n   Calculation: \\(292 \\times 4 = 1168\\), then shifted one position to the left (multiplying by 10) gives 11680.\n\n3. **Third partial product (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   292 \\times 300 = 87600\n   \\]\n   Calculation: \\(292 \\times 3 = 876\\), then shifted two positions to the left (multiplying by 100) gives 87600.\n\nAdding all the partial products together:\n\\[\n1460 + 11680 + 87600\n\\]\n\nFirst, add 1460 and 11680:\n\\[\n1460 + 11680 = 13140\n\\]\n\nThen add the result to 87600:\n\\[\n13140 + 87600 = 100740\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 292 and 345 is \\(\\boxed{100740}\\).",
