y 8:\n\n330\n\nx  8\n\n-----\n\n2640.\n\nThen multiply 330 by 10 (the tens place):\n\n330\n\nx 10\n\n-----\n\n3300.\n\nThen multiply 330 by 100 (the hundreds place):\n\n330\n\nx100\n\n-----\n\n33000.\n\nAdding all together: 2640 + 3300 = 5940; 5940 +33,000 = 38,940. Correct.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident that the answer is 38,940.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 330 and 118 is \\boxed{38940}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 330 and 118, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 330 by the units digit of 118 (8):**\n   \\[\n   330 \\times 8 = 2640\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 330 by the tens digit of 118 (1), which is in the tens place (equivalent to multiplying by 10):**\n   \\[\n   330 \\times 10 = 3300\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 330 by the hundreds digit of 118 (1), which is in the hundreds place (equivalent to multiplying by 100):**\n   \\[\n   330 \\times 100 = 33000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   2640 + 3300 + 33000 = 38940\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 330 and 118 is \\(\\boxed{38940}\\).",
