(6 \\times 6 = 36 + 2 = 38\\)\n\n2. **Multiply 647 by 9 (tens place, shifted one position left):**\n   \\[\n   647 \\times 9 = 5823 \\quad \\text{(shifted left gives 58230)}\n   \\]\n   - \\(7 \\times 9 = 63\\) (write down 3, carry over 6)\n   - \\(4 \\times 9 = 36 + 6 = 42\\) (write down 2, carry over 4)\n   - \\(6 \\times 9 = 54 + 4 = 58\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 647 by 5 (hundreds place, shifted two positions left):**\n   \\[\n   647 \\times 5 = 3235 \\quad \\text{(shifted left gives 323500)}\n   \\]\n   - \\(7 \\times 5 = 35\\) (write down 5, carry over 3)\n   - \\(4 \\times 5 = 20 + 3 = 23\\) (write down 3, carry over 2)\n   - \\(6 \\times 5 = 30 + 2 = 32\\)\n\n4. **Add the results:**\n   \\[\n   3882 + 58230 + 323500 = 385612\n   \\]\n\n**Verification using Distributive Property:**\n\\[\n647 \\times 596 = (600 + 47)(500 + 96)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 600 \\times 500 + 600 \\times 96 + 47 \\times 500 + 47 \\times 96\n\\]\n\\[\n= 300000 + 57600 + 23500 + 4512 = 385612\n\\]\n\n**Verification using Algebraic Identity:**\n\\[\n(a)(b) = \\left(\\frac{a + b}{2}\\right)^2 - \\left(\\frac{a - b}{2}\\right)^2\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{647 + 596}{2} = 621.5 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\frac{647 - 596}{2} = 25.5\n\\]\n\\[\n(621.5)^2 - (25.5)^2 = 386262.25 - 650.25 = 385612\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 647 and 596 is \\(\\boxed{385612}\\).",
