7 and 402 is \\boxed{380694}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 947 and 402, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, using the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. Multiply 947 by the units digit of 402 (which is 2):\n   \\[\n   947 \\times 2 = 1894\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 947 by the tens digit of 402 (which is 0, so the result is 0, but shifted one position to the left):\n   \\[\n   947 \\times 0 = 0 \\quad \\text{(shifted one position to the left becomes 00)}\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 947 by the hundreds digit of 402 (which is 4, so we multiply by 400):\n   \\[\n   947 \\times 400 = 947 \\times 4 \\times 100 = 3788 \\times 100 = 378800\n   \\]\n\nAdding all the partial products together:\n\\[\n1894 + 0 + 378800 = 380694\n\\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n\\[\n947 \\times 402 = 947 \\times (400 + 2) = (900 + 40 + 7) \\times (400 + 2)\n\\]\n\nBreaking down each term:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n900 \\times 400 & = 360000, \\\\\n900 \\times 2 & = 1800, \\\\\n40 \\times 400 & = 16000, \\\\\n40 \\times 2 & = 80, \\\\\n7 \\times 400 & = 2800, \\\\\n7 \\times 2 & = 14.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nAdding all these terms together:\n\\[\n360000 + 1800 + 16000 + 80 + 2800 + 14 = 380694\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 947 and 402 is \\(\\boxed{380694}\\).",
