ng:\n\n615 \u00d7800 = 492,000\n\n615 \u00d77 = 4,305\n\nThus, 492,000 - 4,305 = 487,695. Exactly the same. So that's a fourth method confirming the result.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident that the product of 615 and 793 is 487,695.\n\nWait, but let me check once more with another calculation. Maybe using calculator-like step-by-step.\n\nLet me compute 615 \u00d7700 first:\n\n615 \u00d77 = 4,305. So 615 \u00d7700 is 4,305 \u00d7100 = 430,500.\n\nThen 615 \u00d790:\n\n615 \u00d79 = 5,535. So \u00d710 is 55,350.\n\nThen 615 \u00d73 = 1,845.\n\nAdding them:\n\n430,500 +55,350 = 485,850.\n\nWait, wait, hold on, 430,500 +55,350:\n\n430,500 + 50,000 = 480,500\n\nThen +5,350 = 485,850.\n\nThen adding 1,845 gives 485,850 +1,845 = 487,695. Yes, that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do the multiplication digit by digit:\n\nLet me write it out as:\n\n\u2003\u2003\u2003615  \n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a0793  \n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014  \nFirst, multiply by 3 (units place):  \n615 \u00d73 = 1,845\n\nThen multiply by 9 (tens place, so shifted left one):  \n615 \u00d79 = 5,535 \u2192 shifted becomes 55,350\n\nThen multiply by7 (hundreds place, shifted left two):  \n615 \u00d77 = 4,305 \u2192 shifted becomes 430,500\n\nAdd them all:\n\n1,845  \n55,350  \n430,500  \n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014  \nTotal: 487,695. Perfect.\n\nAlternatively, let me check with another method: using the standard vertical multiplication:\n\n\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003615  \n\u2003\u2003\u00d7\u2003793  \n\u2003\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014  \n\u2003\u2003\u20031845\u2003 (615 \u00d7 3)  \n\u2003\u200355350\u2003 (615 \u00d7 90, shifted one position left)  \n\u2003430500\u2003 (615 \u00d7 700, shifted two positions left)  \n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014  \n\u2003Total: 487,695\n\nYes, that's exactly how it is. So all methods converge to the same answer. Therefore, I can be sure that the product is 487,695.\n\nI think that's thorough. I made a mistake at the beginning be