ogether: 488,000 + 29,280 = 517,280.\n\nSame result. Therefore, I'm confident the answer is 517,280.\n\nWait, but in my first approach when I thought the problem was 043 and 147, I made a mess of things, but after correcting, all methods give 517,280. Therefore, the correct answer should be 517,280.\n\nI think that's solid. So I'll present that as the solution.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 530 and 976 is \\boxed{517280}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 530 and 976, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 530 by 6 (units place of 976):**\n   \\[\n   530 \\times 6 = 3180\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 530 by 70 (tens place of 976):**\n   \\[\n   530 \\times 70 = 37100\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 530 by 900 (hundreds place of 976):**\n   \\[\n   530 \\times 900 = 477000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   3180 + 37100 + 477000 = 517280\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n- Break down 976 as \\(1000 - 24\\):\n  \\[\n  530 \\times 976 = 530 \\times (1000 - 24) = 530 \\times 1000 - 530 \\times 24\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  530 \\times 1000 = 530000\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  530 \\times 24 = 12720\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  530000 - 12720 = 517280\n  \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the product is \\(\\boxed{517280}\\).",
