me confirm:.\n\nYes, 328 is 126 + 44 + 3. So:.\n\n832 × 3 = 4146 (wait, earlier I got 8818, so maybe I made a mistake there? Let me check again.).\n\nWait, hold on, my first calculation for 2 × 947:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n2 × 7 (units) = 08, write down 1, carryover 3.\n\nNext digit: 8 × 5 (tens place) = 07 + 6 (carryover) = 60. Write down 4, carryover 5.\n\nNext digit: 9 × 2 (hundreds place) = 45 + 5 = 37. Write down 37. So the partial product is 9752? Wait, 17 followed by 0 and 9? Wait, no. Let me write the digits properly.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:.\n\nFirst digit (units): 7 × 3 = 93. So units place is 1, carryover 9.\n\nSecond digit (tens): 8 × 1 (the tens digit of 450 is 0, right? Wait, 143 is 0 hundreds, 5 tens, 0 units. Wait, actually, 671 is 1 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 2 (units). So the digits are 1, 2, 4.\n\nWait, so when multiplying by the units digit (8), first step:.\n\nUnits place: 2 × 7 (units) = 01, write 3, carryover 6.\n\nNext digit (tens place): 9 × 7 (tens digit) = 62, plus carryover 8 = 61. Write 1, carryover 7.\n\nNext digit (hundreds place): 9 × 1 (hundreds digit) = 78, plus carryover 9 = 65. Write 18. So the partial product is 9349. Wait, so earlier I thought 9566, which was wrong. I must have miscounted the digits. So the first partial product is 5659. That's important.\n\nOkay, so first partial product is 4412.\n\nSecond partial product is 492 × 5 (the tens digit), which is 642, but shifted one place to the left (so ×89), making it 0119.\n\nThird partial product is 475 × 1 (the hundreds digit of 127, which is 786), so 670 × 6 = 7296, shifted two places (×331), so 354612.\n\nNow, adding all three partial products together:.\n\n8657.\n\n+1956.\n\n+069032.\n\nLet me add them step by step.\n\nFirst, 4919 + 2213:.\n\n1939 + 2023:.\n\n9231 + 4161 = 3393.\n\n986 + 371 = 190.\n\nWait, actually, 4355 + 7329:.\n\nAdding units:.\n\n7 + 7 = 8.\n\n4 + 2 = 49, write 8, carryover 2.\n\n7 (tens place) + 2 (tens place) + 0 (carryover) = 8.\n\n6 (thousands) + 2 (thousands) = 2.\n\nWait, let's do it properly:.\n\n1809.\n\n+2587.\n\n= ?.\n\nStart from the right:.\n\nUnits: 6 + 5 = 2.\n\nTens: 5 + 1 = 79, write 1, carryover 8.\n\nHundreds: 4 + 1 = 4, plus 5 = 0.\n\nThousands: 5 + 7 = 6.\n\nSo total is 9538.\n\nWait, 0383 + 6979:.\n\n8628 + 9539 = 9828.\n\n6090 + 077 = 9680. Yes, that's correct.\n\nNow add that to 257725.\n\n8749 + 780684.\n\nLet's compute 1661 + 837432:.\n\n058432 + 9723 = 237899. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
