\nNext, the tens digit of 168 is 6 (which is actually 60). So multiply 463 \u00d760.\n\nFirst compute 463 \u00d76 = 2,778,\n\nthen add a zero to make it 27,780. That's the second partial product, shifted one place to the left.\n\nThen the hundreds digit is 1 (in the hundreds place, so it's 100). Multiply 463 \u00d7100 = 46,300. That's the third partial product, shifted two places to the left.\n\nNow add all three partial products:\n\n3,704\n\n27,780\n\n+46,300\n\n--------\n\nLet's add them step by step.\n\nFirst, add 3,704 + 27,780:\n\n3,704 + 27,780 = 31,484.\n\nThen add 46,300 to that:\n\n31,484 + 46,300.\n\n31,484 + 40,000 =71,484,\n\n71,484 +6,300=77,784.\n\nSo total is 77,784.\n\nWait, but let me check again:\n\nWait, 463 \u00d7 168:\n\nAlternatively, 168 can be broken down into 100 + 60 +8,\n\nso 463\u00d7100 =46,300,\n\n463\u00d760 =27,780,\n\n463\u00d78=3,704,\n\nAdding them gives 46,300 +27,780 =74,080,\n\nthen +3,704 =77,784. That seems correct.\n\nWait but let me verify using another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, using the standard multiplication:\n\n463\n\n\u00d7168\n\nFirst step: 463 \u00d78 =3,704\n\nSecond step: 463 \u00d760 =27,780 (written as 27780 shifted one position)\n\nThird step: 463 \u00d7100=46,300 (shifted two positions)\n\nAdding them:\n\n3,704\n\n27,780\n\n46,300\n\nAdd first two:3,704+27,780 =31,484\n\nThen 31,484 +46,300 =77,784.\n\nYes, that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using the distributive property another way:\n\n463 \u00d7168 = 463\u00d7(170 -2) =463\u00d7170 -463\u00d72.\n\nCalculate 463\u00d7170:\n\n463\u00d7100=46,300,\n\n463\u00d770=32,410 (since 463\u00d77=3,241, so \u00d710=32,410),\n\nTotal 46,300 +32,410=78,710.\n\nThen subtract 463\u00d72=926,\n\nSo 78,710 -926 =77,784. Same result. Good.\n\nAlternatively, maybe check with calculator approximation:\n\n463 \u00d7 168. Let's approximate to 460\u00d7170 =78,200. But actual is 77,784, which is 416 less, which makes sense since we took away 3\u00d7170 and added 460\u00d7(-2). Hmm, but anyway, the exact calculation gives 77,784. So I think that's the right answer.\n\nWait, but in my initial thinking process, I messed up the problem numbers, but corrected myself later. So the final answer should be 77,784. Let me confirm once more with another approach.\n\nLet me do the multiplication step by step:\n\nMultiply 463 by 8:\n\n4 \u00d7 8 =32, write down 2, carryover 3.\n\n6\u00d78=48 +3=51, write down 1, carryover5.\n\n4\u00d78=32 +5=37. So that gives 3704. Correct.\n\nThen multiply by 60 (the 6 in tens place):\n\n463 \u00d76:\n\n3\u00d76=18, write 8, carryover1.\n\n6\u00d76=36 +1=37, write7, carryover3.\n\n4\u00d76=24 +3=27. So that's 2,778. Then times10 is 27,780. Correct.\n\nMultiply by 100 (the 1 in hundreds place):\n\n463\u00d71=463, times 100 is 46,300. Correct.\n\nAdding them all together:\n\n3,704\n\n+27,780 =31,484\n\n+46,300 =77,784.\n\nYes, so I think that's correct. Therefore, the product of 463 and 168 is 77,784.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 463 and 168 is \\boxed{77784}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 463 and 168, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 463 by 8 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     463 \\\\\n   \\times \\quad 8 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     3704 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   \\[\n   463 \\times 8 = 3704\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 463 by 60 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     463 \\\\\n   \\times \\quad 60 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     27780 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   \\[\n   463 \\times 6 = 2778 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero)} \\quad 27780\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 463 by 100 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     463 \\\\\n   \\times \\quad 100 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     46300 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   \\[\n   463 \\times 100 = 46300\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     3704 \\\\\n   + 27780 \\\\\n   + 46300 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     77784 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Step-by-step addition:\n   \\[\n   3704 + 27780 = 31484\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   31484 + 46300 = 77784\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 463 and 168 is \\(\\boxed{77784}\\).",
