\n\nSo all methods confirm that the product is 127,813.\n\nTherefore, after carefully checking with multiple methods and verifying each step, I can confidently say that the result is 127,813.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 133 and 961 is \\boxed{127813}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 133 and 961, we can use the standard multiplication method step by step:\n\n1. Multiply 133 by the units digit of 961 (which is 1):\n   \\[\n   133 \\times 1 = 133\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 133 by the tens digit of 961 (which is 6, representing 60):\n   \\[\n   133 \\times 60 = 7980\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 133 by the hundreds digit of 961 (which is 9, representing 900):\n   \\[\n   133 \\times 900 = 119700\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results of these three multiplications together:\n   \\[\n   133 + 7980 + 119700\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add 133 and 7980:\n     \\[\n     133 + 7980 = 8113\n     \\]\n\n   - Then add the result to 119700:\n     \\[\n     8113 + 119700 = 127813\n     \\]\n\nTo verify, we can use another method by breaking down the multiplication:\n- Express 961 as \\(900 + 60 + 1\\):\n  \\[\n  133 \\times (900 + 60 + 1) = 133 \\times 900 + 133 \\times 60 + 133 \\times 1\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  = 119700 + 7980 + 133 = 127813\n  \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 133 and 961 is \\(\\boxed{127813}\\).",
