e hundreds digit, which is 7. This is 503 \u00d7 700. So:\n\n503 \u00d7 7 = 3,521. Add two zeros to get 352,100.\n\nNow, add all three partial products together:\n\n1,006\n\n+30,180\n\n+352,100\n\nLet's add the first two: 1,006 + 30,180 = 31,186.\n\nThen add that to 352,100: 31,186 + 352,100.\n\n31,186 + 352,100: 31k + 352k = 383,186. Then + 186 gives 383,372?\n\nWait, let me check again:\n\n352,100\n\n+ 31,186\n\nAdding units: 0 +6 =6.\n\nTens: 0 +8=8.\n\nHundreds: 1 +1=2.\n\nThousands: 2 +1=3.\n\nTen thousands: 5 +3=8.\n\nHundred thousands: 3 +0=3. So 383,286?\n\nWait, maybe I miscalculated the addition. Let me write it down:\n\n352,100\n\n+\u00a0\u00a031,186\n\n= ?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n0 +6 =6\n\n0 +8 =8\n\n1 (from 352,100's hundreds place) +1 (from 31,186's hundreds place) = 2.\n\n2 (thousands place) +1 (thousands place of 31k) = 3.\n\n5 (ten thousands place) +3 (ten thousands from 31k?) Wait, 31,186 has 3 in the ten thousands place? No, 31,186 is 3 (ten thousands?), no, wait: 31,186 is 3 ten thousands, 1 thousand, 1 hundred, 8 tens, 6 units. Wait, actually, 31,186 is 3 (10,000) + 1 (1,000) +1 (100) +8 (10) +6.\n\n352,100 is 3 (100,000) +5 (10,000) +2 (1,000) +1 (100).\n\nSo adding them:\n\nHundred thousands: 3\n\nTen thousands:5 +3 =8\n\nThousands:2 +1 =3\n\nHundreds:1 +1 =2\n\nTens:0 +8 =8\n\nUnits:0 +6 =6\n\nSo total is 383,286.\n\nWait, but let me confirm with another method.\n\nAlternatively, compute 503 \u00d7 762.\n\nBreak down 762 into 700 +60 +2.\n\nSo:\n\n503 \u00d7700 = 503*7*100 = 3,521*100 = 352,100\n\n503 \u00d760 = 503*6*10 = 3,018*10 =30,180\n\n503 \u00d72 =1,006\n\nAdding those together:\n\n352,100 + 30,180 = 382,280. Then add 1,006: 382,280 +1,006 = 383,286. Okay, that matches.\n\nSo the product is 383,286.\n\nWait, but I thought maybe I had an error earlier when adding 31,186 and 352,100, but that's correct. So final answer should be 383,286.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps another way to verify.\n\nLet me try multiplying using another method, like the distributive property differently.\n\n503 \u00d7762 can be written as (500 +3) \u00d7(700 +60 +2).\n\nMultiply each term:\n\nFirst, 500\u00d7700 = 350,000\n\n500\u00d760 =30,000\n\n500\u00d72 =1,000\n\nThen 3\u00d7700 =2,100\n\n3\u00d760 =180\n\n3\u00d72 =6\n\nNow add all those:\n\n350,000 +30,000 +1,000 = 381,000\n\nThen the other terms:2,100 +180 +6 =2,286\n\nTotal: 381,000 +2,286 = 383,286. Same result.\n\nOkay, so that's consistent. Therefore, the product is 383,286.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 503 and 762 is \\boxed{383286}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 503 and 762, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify it using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, using the standard algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 503 by the units digit of 762 (which is 2):\n   \\[\n   503 \\times 2 = 1006\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 503 by the tens digit of 762 (which is 60), shifted one place to the left:\n   \\[\n   503 \\times 60 = 30180\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 503 by the hundreds digit of 762 (which is 700), shifted two places to the left:\n   \\[\n   503 \\times 700 = 352100\n   \\]\n\nAdding these partial products together:\n\\[\n1006 + 30180 + 352100 = 383286\n\\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n\\[\n503 \\times 762 = (500 + 3) \\times (700 + 60 + 2)\n\\]\n\nExpanding the terms:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n500 \\times 700 &= 350000, \\\\\n500 \\times 60 &= 30000, \\\\\n500 \\times 2 &= 1000, \\\\\n3 \\times 700 &= 2100, \\\\\n3 \\times 60 &= 180, \\\\\n3 \\times 2 &= 6.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nAdding all these terms together:\n\\[\n350000 + 30000 + 1000 + 2100 + 180 + 6 = 383286\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 503 and 762 is \\(\\boxed{383286}\\).",
