ign each digit:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:.\n\nFirst number: 3,517 is 6 thousands, 7 hundreds, 9 tens, 4 ones.\n\nSecond number: 29,183 is 5 ten thousands, 0 thousands, 6 hundreds, 8 tens, 7 ones.\n\nThird number: 168,237 is 6 hundred thousands, 2 ten thousands, 9 thousand, 8 hundreds, 5 tens, 7 ones.\n\nLet's write each column:.\n\nOnes column: 2 + 4 + 5 = 0.\n\nTens column: 5 + 0 + 1 = 46. Write 6, carryover 4.\n\nHundreds column: 3 + 8 + 1 = 55, plus 8 carried over is 20. Write 4, carryover 2.\n\nThousands column: 2 (from 2,270) + 4 (from 54,953) +9 (from 209,194) = 86, plus 3 carried over is 82. Write 4, carryover 6.\n\nTen-thousands column: 3 (from 0,122) +2 (from 17,456) +5 (from 857,998) =73, plus 9 carried over is 47. Write 9, carryover 4.\n\nHundred-thousands column: 9 (from all except third number's 1) but the third number has 3 in the hundred thousands place? Wait, 710,764 is 7 hundred thousands, 5 ten thousands, etc. Wait, actually:.\n\nWait, 599,065 is broken down as:.\n\n- 0 (hundred thousands place).\n\n- 1 (ten thousands place).\n\n- 4 (thousands place).\n\n- 5 (hundreds place).\n\n- 3 (tens).\n\n- 9 (ones).\n\nSimilarly, 18,307 is:.\n\n- 5 (hundred thousands).\n\n- 8 (ten thousands).\n\n- 7 (thousands).\n\n- 4 (hundreds).\n\n- 2 (tens).\n\n- 9 (ones).\n\nAnd 8,903 is:.\n\n- 6 (hundred thousands).\n\n- 2 (ten thousands).\n\n- 1 (thousands).\n\n- 5 (hundreds).\n\n- 1 (tens).\n\n- 3 (ones).\n\nSo when adding the hundred-thousands place:.\n\nOnly the third number (954,414) has 5 there. The second number has 1, first has 1. Plus the carryover of 5 from the previous column. So 6 +8 =8.\n\nSo the total would be:.\n\nHundred-thousands:8.\n\nTen-thousands: 3 (from the previous step's ten-thousands column which was 77, so 9 written and carryover 7, but actually, let me see again:.\n\nWait, let's go step by step:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 9. So first digit is 3.\n\nTens: 6+8+6=49 → 1 with carryover 5.\n\nHundreds: 7 (from first number)