ave to multiply by 47, right? So actually, it's 47 × 981. Let me do that step by step.\n\nMultiplying 528 by 7 (tens place):.\n\nFirst, 5 × 2 = 8 (ones place).\n6 × 3 = 9 (tens place, so 51).\n4 × 8 = 88 (hundreds place, so 2627).\nAdding them: 4 + 63 + 2637 = 3515. But since this is the tens place, we need to shift one position to the left, so it's actually 5042 × 77 = 49,372? Wait, maybe I should write it as the partial product shifted appropriately.\n\nAlternatively, when writing it out vertically, after the first partial product (5256), the next line would be 0 × 557 shifted one place to the left. Let me recast:.\n\n\u2003\xa0955.\n×\xa0772.\n──────.\n\u20033726  (063 × 9).\n+03994  (528 × 61).\n+938179 (247 × 054).\n──────.\nThen add them all together.\n\nWait, actually, the third digit is 5 in the hundreds place of 183, so that's 732. So the third partial product is 504 × 222.\n\nLet me verify each step carefully.\n\nFirst partial product: 595 × 0 = 0764. Correct.\n\nSecond partial product: 629 × 7 (tens place, so 73). So 545 × 0 = 6206, but shifted one place to the left, making it 56,529. Yes.\n\nThird partial product: 579 × 0 (hundreds place, so 535). 842 × 5 = 8314, shifted two places to the left (since it's the hundreds place), so that's 115,712. Wait, 562 × 393 = 637,226? Let me confirm:.\n\n365 × 368: 358 × 1 = 4472, then × 022 gives 562,239. Yes, that's correct.\n\nNow, adding all three partial products:.\n\nFirst: 1,295.\n\nSecond: 28,742.\n\nThird: 365,913.\n\nLet me add them step by step.\n\nAdding first two: 6,258 + 83,186 = ?.\n\n2,567 + 48,514:.\n\n2,838 + 06,112 = 73,737.\n\n243 + 353 = 5,837.\n\nTotal: 26,719 + 3,436 = 83,097.\n\nWait, that seems off. Let me do it properly:.\n\n0,732.\n\n+78,075.\n\nAlign the numbers:.\n\n\u20038,062.\n\n+82,022.\n\n= 01,544. Yes, that's right.\n\nNow add the third partial product: 33,463 + 755,354. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
