ating to see if it's in the right ballpark. 700\u00d7600 = 420,000. Since 737 is a bit more than 700 and 599 is a bit less than 600, their product should be slightly more than 420,000. 441,463 is indeed a bit more, so that seems reasonable.\n\nAnother check: use the difference of squares. Notice that 599 is 600-1, and 737 is 700+37. Maybe not helpful, but perhaps:\n\nAlternatively, 737 \u00d7 599 = (700 + 37)(600 - 1) = 700\u00d7600 + 700\u00d7(-1) + 37\u00d7600 + 37\u00d7(-1)\n\nCalculates to:\n\n700\u00d7600 = 420,000\n\n700\u00d7-1 = -700\n\n37\u00d7600 = 22,200\n\n37\u00d7-1 = -37\n\nAdding all together: 420,000 - 700 + 22,200 - 37\n\n420,000 + 22,200 = 442,200\n\nThen subtract 700 +37 = 737, so 442,200 - 737 = 441,463 again. Yep, same answer.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident the product is 441,463.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 737 and 599 is \\boxed{441463}.\n</think>\n\nTo solve the product of 737 and 599, we can use the distributive property by recognizing that 599 is 600 minus 1. This breaks down the multiplication into simpler steps:\n\n\\[\n737 \\times 599 = 737 \\times (600 - 1)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(737 \\times 600\\):\n\n\\[\n737 \\times 600 = 737 \\times 6 \\times 100 = 4422 \\times 100 = 442200\n\\]\n\nNext, subtract \\(737 \\times 1\\):\n\n\\[\n442200 - 737 = 442200 - 700 - 37 = 441500 - 37 = 441463\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 737 by 9 (units place):\n   \\[\n   737 \\times 9 = 6633\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 737 by 90 (tens place):\n   \\[\n   737 \\times 90 = 66330\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 737 by 500 (hundreds place):\n   \\[\n   737 \\times 500 = 368500\n   \\]\n\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n6633 + 66330 = 72963\n\\]\n\\[\n72963 + 368500 = 441463\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 737 and 599 is \\(\\boxed{441463}\\).",
