usands, 3 hundreds, 1 tens. 95,644 is 85 thousands, 6 hundreds. Hmm, maybe better to line them up:.\n\n  8,579.\n+50,693.\n--------.\n .\n\nAdding the units: 4 + 9 = 4.\n\nTens: 7 + 2 = 2.\n\nHundreds: 0 + 5 = 57. So write down 9 and carry over 3.\n\nThousands: 4 + 7 + 5 (carry) = 27. So write 9 and carry 8.\n\nTen-thousands: 3 + 9 + 3 (carry) = 4.\n\nSo total is 28,404.\n\nWait, let me check that again because 8,383 +05,684. Maybe another way: 60,125 + 2,144 is 70,113, then add 231: 16,386 + 147 = 65,917. Yeah, that's right.\n\nNow add that to 787,763.\n\n15,717 + 467,878. Let's see:.\n\n20,788 + 942,892 = 055,128. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
