ect. Therefore, the product is 250,560.\n\nBut wait, in my initial thought process, I was confused with different numbers like 899 and 420, but that's probably because I was overcomplicating or mixing up numbers. The correct problem is 720 \u00d7 348, so after redoing carefully, the answer is 250,560.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 720 and 348 is \\boxed{250560}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 720 and 348, we can use the standard multiplication method step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 720 by the units digit of 348 (8):**\n   \\[\n   720 \\times 8 = 5760\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 720 by the tens digit of 348 (4), which is actually 40:**\n   \\[\n   720 \\times 40 = 28800\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 720 by the hundreds digit of 348 (3), which is actually 300:**\n   \\[\n   720 \\times 300 = 216000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all three results together:**\n   \\[\n   5760 + 28800 + 216000\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add \\(5760 + 28800\\):\n     \\[\n     5760 + 28800 = 34560\n     \\]\n   \n   - Then, add the result to \\(216000\\):\n     \\[\n     34560 + 216000 = 250560\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 720 and 348 is \\(\\boxed{250560}\\).",
