it of 412 (2):**\n   \\[\n   427 \\times 2 = 854\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 427 by the tens digit of 412 (1, which represents 10):**\n   \\[\n   427 \\times 10 = 4270\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 427 by the hundreds digit of 412 (4, which represents 400):**\n   \\[\n   427 \\times 400 = 170800\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   854 + 4270 + 170800\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add 854 and 4270:\n     \\[\n     854 + 4270 = 5124\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to 170800:\n     \\[\n     5124 + 170800 = 175924\n     \\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the distributive property:\n- **Express 427 \u00d7 412 as:**\n  \\[\n  427 \\times (400 + 12) = 427 \\times 400 + 427 \\times 12\n  \\]\n  - Calculate each term:\n    \\[\n    427 \\times 400 = 170800\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    427 \\times 12 = 5124\n    \\]\n  - Add the results:\n    \\[\n    170800 + 5124 = 175924\n    \\]\n\nAnother verification using expansion:\n- **Express 427 \u00d7 412 as (420 + 7)(410 + 2):**\n  \\[\n  420 \\times 410 + 420 \\times 2 + 7 \\times 410 + 7 \\times 2\n  \\]\n  - Calculate each term:\n    \\[\n    420 \\times 410 = 172200\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    420 \\times 2 = 840\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    7 \\times 410 = 2870\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    7 \\times 2 = 14\n    \\]\n  - Add the results:\n    \\[\n    172200 + 840 + 2870 + 14 = 175924\n    \\]\n\nThus, the product of 427 and 412 is \\(\\boxed{175924}\\).",
