nThen 744 \u00d7 40 = 744 \u00d7 4 \u00d710 = (2,976) \u00d710 = 29,760.\n\nThen 744 \u00d71 =744.\n\nAdding all together: 595,200 + 29,760 = 624,960. Then +744 is 625,704. So that's correct.\n\nHmm, so perhaps my initial calculation is correct. But I want to be absolutely sure.\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 744 \u00d7 841 using another method, like the lattice method or breaking down numbers into smaller components.\n\nAlternatively, since 841 is 29 squared (29\u00d729=841), but 744 is 744. Not sure if that helps. Let me see:\n\nAlternatively, 744 \u00d7 29 \u00d729. But that might complicate more.\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 744 \u00d7 841 as (700 + 44) \u00d7 (800 + 40 +1).\n\nUsing the distributive property:\n\nFirst, expand (700 + 44)(800 + 40 + 1):\n\n= 700\u00d7800 + 700\u00d740 + 700\u00d71 + 44\u00d7800 + 44\u00d740 + 44\u00d71\n\nCompute each term:\n\n700\u00d7800 = 560,000\n\n700\u00d740 = 28,000\n\n700\u00d71 = 700\n\n44\u00d7800 = 35,200\n\n44\u00d740 = 1,760\n\n44\u00d71 = 44\n\nNow add all these:\n\n560,000 + 28,000 = 588,000\n\n588,000 + 700 = 588,700\n\n588,700 + 35,200 = 623,900\n\n623,900 + 1,760 = 625,660\n\n625,660 + 44 = 625,704.\n\nSame result again. So that's reassuring.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using a calculator would be faster, but since I can't use one, multiple methods confirm 625,704.\n\nTherefore, the product of 744 and 841 is 625,704.\n\nBut just to be thorough, let me do the multiplication vertically again step by step.\n\nMultiplying 744 by 841:\n\nFirst, write 744 \u00d7 841.\n\nStart with the units digit of 841, which is 1:\n\n1 \u00d7 744 = 744. Write this as the first partial product.\n\nNext, the tens digit is 4. Multiply 744 by 4, but shifted one place to the left (so \u00d710):\n\n4 \u00d7 744 = 2,976. Shifted left becomes 29,760. Second partial product.\n\nThird, the hundreds digit is 8. Multiply 744 by 8, shifted two places left (\u00d7100):\n\n8 \u00d7 744 = 5,952. Shifted two places becomes 595,200. Third partial