60 +8).\n\nBut that might complicate more, but let's try:\n\nFirst, 200\u00d7500 =100,000,\n\n200\u00d760 =12,000,\n\n200\u00d78 =1,600,\n\nThen 17\u00d7500 =8,500,\n\n17\u00d760 =1,020,\n\n17\u00d78 =136,\n\nNow sum all these:\n\n100,000 +12,000 =112,000,\n\n112,000 +1,600 =113,600,\n\n113,600 +8,500 =122,100,\n\n122,100 +1,020 =123,120,\n\n123,120 +136 =123,256.\n\nSame result. So that's a good check.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the lattice method, but that might take longer, but just to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps check with calculator if possible. Since I can't use a calculator, but I can do another multiplication.\n\nWait, let me try multiplying 217 \u00d7 568 step by step again.\n\nStarting over:\n\n217\n\n\u00d7568\n\nFirst, multiply 217 by 8:\n\n7\u00d78=56, write down 6, carryover 5\n\n1\u00d78=8 +5=13, write down 3, carryover 1\n\n2\u00d78=16 +1=17, so write 17.\n\nSo first partial product is 1736.\n\nNext multiply by 6 (tens place):\n\n217 \u00d76:\n\n7\u00d76=42, write 2, carryover 4\n\n1\u00d76=6 +4=10, write 0, carryover 1\n\n2\u00d76=12 +1=13.\n\nSince it's the tens place, we shift one to the left, so it becomes 13020.\n\nThird, multiply by 5 (hundreds place):\n\n217 \u00d75:\n\n7\u00d75=35, write 5, carryover 3\n\n1\u00d75=5 +3=8\n\n2\u00d75=10.\n\nSo that gives 1085, shifted two places becomes 108500.\n\nAdding them together:\n\n1736\n\n+13020\n\n=14756\n\n+108500\n\n=123,256.\n\nYes, same result.\n\nAlternatively, let me try multiplying 568 \u00d7217 to see if commutative property holds.\n\n568\u00d7200=113,600,\n\n568\u00d717=568\u00d710 +568\u00d77=5,680 +3,976=9,656,\n\nTotal is 113,600 +9,656=123,256.\n\nSame answer. So that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident that the product of 217 and 568 is 123,256.\n\nWait a second, but just to be thorough, perhaps I made a mistake in one of the steps? Let me check the 217\u00d76 again.\n\n217\u00d76:\n\n7\u00d76=42, so 2 with a carryover of 4.\n\n1\u00d76=6 +4=10, so 0 with carryover 1.\n\n2\u00d76=12 +1=13, so 13.\n\nSo that gives 1302 when not shifted. But since it's the tens place, shifting one gives 13020. Correct.\n\nSimilarly, 217\u00d75:\n\n7\u00d75=35, so 5, carryover 3.\n\n1\u00d75=5 +3=8, so 8.\n\n2\u00d75=10, so 10.\n\nThat gives 1085. Shifting two places gives 108,500. Correct.\n\nAdding 1,736 +13,020:\n\n1,736 +13,020.\n\n1,736 +10,000=11,736,\n\n11,736 +3,000=14,736,\n\n14,736 +20=14,756. Correct.\n\nThen adding 14,756 +108,500:\n\n14,756 +100,000=114,756,\n\n114,756 +8,500=123,256. Correct.\n\nAlright, all steps check out. Therefore, the answer is 123,256.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 217 and 568 is \\boxed{123256}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 217 and 568, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 217 by 8 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   217 \\times 8 = 1736\n   \\]\n   - Calculation steps:\n     - \\(7 \\times 8 = 56\\)\n     - \\(1 \\times 8 = 8\\) (plus carryover 5 gives 13)\n     - \\(2 \\times 8 = 16\\) (plus carryover 1 gives 17)\n\n2. **Multiply 217 by 60 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   217 \\times 60 = 13020\n   \\]\n   - Calculation steps:\n     - \\(217 \\times 6 = 1302\\)\n     - Shift one position to the left: \\(1302 \\times 10 = 13020\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 217 by 500 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   217 \\times 500 = 108500\n   \\]\n   - Calculation steps:\n     - \\(217 \\times 5 = 1085\\)\n     - Shift two positions to the left: \\(1085 \\times 100 = 108500\\)\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   1736 + 13020 + 108500\n   \\]\n   - First, add \\(1736 + 13020\\):\n     \\[\n     1736 + 13020 = 14756\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(108500\\):\n     \\[\n     14756 + 108500 = 123256\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 217 and 568 is \\(\\boxed{123256}\\).",
