600, and adding 344 \u00d720 gives the total. Yeah, 144k sounds right.\n\nAnother check: 420 \u00d7 300 = 126,000. 420 \u00d7 44 = 420\u00d740 + 420\u00d74 = 16,800 + 1,680 = 18,480. Then 126k +18,480 = 144,480. Correct.\n\nAlright, so after verifying multiple ways, I believe the correct answer is 144,480. I just need to make sure I didn't make any arithmetic errors in my steps. Let me check one more time with the standard multiplication:\n\n344 \u00d7 420:\n\nFirst, write 344 \u00d7 420 as 344 \u00d7 (4\u00d7100 + 2\u00d710 + 0\u00d71). So:\n\nMultiply 344 \u00d7 0 = 0.\n\nMultiply 344 \u00d7 2 (tens place): 344\u00d72=688, so write 6,880 (since it's the tens place).\n\nMultiply 344 \u00d74 (hundreds place): 344\u00d74=1,376, so write 137,600.\n\nAdding them:\n\n0\n\n+6,880\n\n+137,600\n\nTotal is 144,480. Yep, that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, the product of 344 and 420 is 144,480.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 344 and 420 is \\boxed{144480}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 344 and 420, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step:\n\n1. Write the numbers vertically:\n   ```\n    344\n  \u00d7 420\n  -------\n  ```\n\n2. Multiply 344 by 0 (units place of 420):\n   ```\n    344\n  \u00d7  420\n  -------\n      0   (since 344 \u00d7 0 = 0)\n  ```\n\n3. Multiply 344 by 2 (tens place of 420, which is 20):\n   ```\n    344\n  \u00d7  420\n  -------\n     6880  (since 344 \u00d7 2 = 688, shifted one position to the left)\n  ```\n\n4. Multiply 344 by 4 (hundreds place of 420, which is 400):\n   ```\n    344\n  \u00d7  420\n  -------\n   137600  (since 344 \u00d7 4 = 1376, shifted two positions to the left)\n  ```\n\n5. Add all the partial products together:\n   ```\n      0\n   + 6880\n   +137600\n  ---------\n   144480\n  ```\n\nThus, the product of 344 and 420 is \\boxed{144480}.",
