 So the product of 104 and 294 is 30,576. \n\nI think my mistake earlier was when I was initially breaking down the numbers incorrectly. But after using two different methods and getting the same answer, I can be confident that 30,576 is the right result. \n\nAlternatively, I can also do the multiplication step by step:\n\n   104  \n\u00d7 294  \n-------  \n   416   (104 \u00d7 4)  \n 9360    (104 \u00d7 90, which is the 9 in tens place)  \n20800    (104 \u00d7 200, the 2 in hundreds place)  \n-------  \nAdding them: 416 + 9360 = 9776; 9776 + 20800 = 30576. \n\nYep, that's consistent. So the final answer must be 30,576.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 104 and 294 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Breakdown using the distributive property**:\n   \\[\n   104 \\times 294 = 104 \\times (300 - 6) = (104 \\times 300) - (104 \\times 6)\n   \\]\n   - \\(104 \\times 300 = 31,200\\)\n   - \\(104 \\times 6 = 624\\)\n   - Subtract: \\(31,200 - 624 = 30,576\\)\n\n2. **Verification via standard multiplication**:\n   ```\n      104  \n    \u00d7 294  \n    ------  \n      416   (104 \u00d7 4)  \n     9360   (104 \u00d7 90)  \n    20800   (104 \u00d7 200)  \n    ------  \n     30,576\n   ```\n\nBoth methods confirm the result is **30,576**.\n\n**Answer**: \\boxed{30576}",
