      "text": "84, 100, 234, 800? Wait, maybe I made a mistake in the steps.\n\nHold on, maybe my breakdown was incorrect. Let me try another method. Using the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nMultiplying 555 by 971.\n\nLet me write it out step by step.\n\nFirst, write 555\n\ntimes 971\n\n________\n\nStarting with the units digit of the lower number (971's units digit is 1):\n\n1 * 555 = 555\n\nNext, the tens digit (7), but shifted one position to the left:\n\n7 * 555 = 3,885 (but shifted one left, so it's 38,850)\n\nThen the hundreds digit (9) shifted two positions:\n\n9 * 555 = 4,995 (shifted two left, so 499,500)\n\nAdding them together:\n\n555\n\n+38,850\n\n+499,500\n\nTotal:\n\n555 + 38,850 = 39,405\n\n39,405 + 499,500 = 538,905\n\nWait, so is that the answer? But let me check again.\n\nWait, 9*555 is 4,995? Let me recalculate: 500*9=4,500, 50*9=450, 5*9=45. So 4,500+450=4,950 +45=4,995. Yes, that's right. So shifted two places (hundreds place), so 4,995 * 100 = 499,500.\n\nThen 7*555: 500*7=3,500; 50*7=350; 5*7=35. So 3,500 + 350 = 3,850 +35= 3,885. Then shift one place (tens): 38,850.\n\nAdding all together: 555 + 38,850 = 39,405; 39,405 + 499,500 = 538,905. So the product is 538,905?\n\nWait, but earlier when I tried breaking down, I got a different number, but maybe I messed up that method. Let me verify with another approach.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using (500 + 55)(900 + 71). Wait, that might complicate. Alternatively, let me use the standard multiplication again.\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 555 * 1000 = 555,000. But since it's 555 * 971, which is 555*(1000 - 29). So that would be 555,000 - (555*29). Let's see if that's easier.\n\nCalculating 555*29: 555*30 = 16,650 minus 555 gives 16,650 - 555 = 16,095.\n\nTherefore, 555,000 - 16,095 = ?\n\n555,000 - 16,000 = 539,000\n\nThen subtract 95 more: 539,000 - 95 = 538,905.\n\nOkay, so that matches the previous result. So the answer is 538,905.\n\nWait a second, so why did I get confused earlier? Because when I first broke it down differently, maybe I made an arithmetic error. But both standard multiplication and the (a - b) method give me 538,905. So I think that's the correct answer. Let me confirm with a calculator approach.\n\nWait, 555 multiplied by 971:\n\n555 \u00d7 900 = 499,500\n\n555 \u00d7 70 = 38,850\n\n555 \u00d7 1 = 555\n\nAdding them up: 499,500 + 38,850 = 538,350; plus 555 is 538,905. Yep, same result. So I think that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 555 and 971 is 538,905.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 555 and 971 is \\boxed{538905}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 555 and 971, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 555 by the units digit of 971 (which is 1):\n   \\[\n   555 \\times 1 = 555\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 555 by the tens digit of 971 (which is 7), and shift the result one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   555 \\times 7 = 3,885 \\quad \\text{(shifted one position left becomes 38,850)}\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 555 by the hundreds digit of 971 (which is 9), and shift the result two positions to the left:\n   \\[\n   555 \\times 9 = 4,995 \\quad \\text{(shifted two positions left becomes 499,500)}\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results from the above steps:\n   \\[\n   555 + 38,850 + 499,500\n   \\]\n\n5. Perform the addition step-by-step:\n   \\[\n   555 + 38,850 = 39,405\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   39,405 + 499,500 = 538,905\n   \\]\n\nTo verify, we can use another method by breaking down 971 as \\(1000 - 29\\):\n1. Calculate \\(555 \\times 1000 = 555,000\\)\n2. Calculate \\(555 \\times 29\\):\n   \\[\n   555 \\times 30 = 16,650 \\quad \\text{then subtract 555} \\quad 16,650 - 555 = 16,095\n   \\]\n3. Subtract the result from 555,000:\n   \\[\n   555,000 - 16,095 = 538,905\n   \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 555 and 971 is \\(\\boxed{538905}\\).",
