ifted two positions.\n\nWait, let's do it step by step.\n\nFirst, multiply 309 by 0 (the units place of 390). That gives 0. So writing that down:\n\n    309\n  x 390\n  --------\n      000  (309 * 0)\n\nNext, multiply 309 by 9 (the tens place). Since it's the tens place, this is actually 90, so the result should be shifted one position to the left. Let's compute 309 * 9:\n\n309 * 9:\n\n9*9 = 81, write down 1, carry over 8.\n\n9*0 = 0 + 8 = 8.\n\n9*3 = 27, write down 27.\n\nSo 309 * 9 is 2,781. So shifted one position left, it becomes 27,810.\n\nThird, multiply 309 by 3 (the hundreds place of 390). Since it's the hundreds digit, this is actually 300, so the result should be shifted two positions to the left.\n\n309 * 3:\n\n3*9 = 27, write down 7, carry over 2.\n\n3*0 = 0 + 2 = 2.\n\n3*3 = 9.\n\nSo that gives 927. Shifted two places becomes 92,700.\n\nNow, add up all three results:\n\n    000\n+ 27,810\n+92,700\n----------\n\nAdding 27,810 + 92,700 first:\n\n27,810 + 92,700:\n\n27,810 + 90,000 = 117,810\n\nThen add 2,700 more: 117,810 + 2,700 = 120,510.\n\nThen adding the zero doesn't change anything. So total is 120,510. That matches the previous result. Good, so that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe another check using a different method. Let's see, perhaps using the commutative property, swapping the numbers.\n\n390 * 309. Let's compute that.\n\n390 * 300 = 117,000\n\n390 * 9 = 3,510\n\nAdding together: 117,000 + 3,510 = 120,510. Same result. Perfect.\n\nTherefore, the product of 309 and 390 is 120,510.\n\nWait, but just to be thorough, let me verify with another approach, maybe breaking down both numbers into smaller components.\n\n309 can be written as 300 + 9, and 390 as 300 + 90.\n\nSo, expanding (300 + 9)*(300 + 90).\n\nUsing the distributive property:\n\n= 300*300 + 300*90 + 9*300 + 9*90\n\nCompute each term:\n\n300*300 = 90,000\n\n300*90 = 27,000\n\n9*300 = 2,700\n\n9*90 = 810\n\nAdding them all together:\n\n90,000 + 27,000 = 117,000\n\n117,000 + 2,700 = 119,700\n\n119,700 + 810 = 120,510.\n\nSame result again. So that solidifies the answer.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using a calculator for verification, but since I don't have one here, these multiple methods all leading to the same answer gives me confidence.\n\nTherefore, I can conclude that the product of 309 and 390 is 120,510.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 309 and 390 is \\boxed{120510}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 309 and 390, we can use the distributive property and the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nFirst, using the distributive property:\n\\[\n309 \\times 390 = 309 \\times (400 - 10)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 309 \\times 400 - 309 \\times 10\n\\]\n\\[\n= 123600 - 3090\n\\]\n\\[\n= 123600 - 3090 = 120510\n\\]\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   309 \\\\\n\\times 390 \\\\\n\\hline\n   000 \\quad \\text{(309 \u00d7 0)} \\\\\n+ 27810 \\quad \\text{(309 \u00d7 9, shifted one position left)} \\\\\n+ 92700 \\quad \\text{(309 \u00d7 3, shifted two positions left)} \\\\\n\\hline\n  120510 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nAnother verification by breaking down both numbers:\n\\[\n(300 + 9) \\times (300 + 90)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 300 \\times 300 + 300 \\times 90 + 9 \\times 300 + 9 \\times 90\n\\]\n\\[\n= 90000 + 27000 + 2700 + 810\n\\]\n\\[\n= 90000 + 27000 = 117000\n\\]\n\\[\n117000 + 2700 = 119700\n\\]\n\\[\n119700 + 810 = 120510\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 309 and 390 is \\(\\boxed{120510}\\).",
