      "text": "123,456. Wait, I'm confused now. Maybe I should do the addition step by step.\n\nWait, let me try again with proper alignment. The first partial product is 78, 1 \u00d7 5 =5, so 285 \u00d7 7 is 1,995. Wait, maybe I need to use simpler numbers. Let me try a different approach.\n\nAlternatively, using expanded form:\n\n285 \u00d7 628 can be written as 285 \u00d7 (600 + 20 + 8) = 285\u00d7600 + 285\u00d720 + 285\u00d78.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n285 \u00d7 600 = 285 \u00d7 6 \u00d7 100 = 1,710 \u00d7 100 = 171,000.\n\n285 \u00d7 20 = 285 \u00d7 2 \u00d7 10 = 570 \u00d7 10 = 5,700.\n\n285 \u00d7 8 = 2,280.\n\nAdding these together: 171,000 + 5,700 = 176,700; 176,700 + 2,280 = 178,980.\n\nWait, but that contradicts my previous thought. Hmm, maybe I made a mistake in the partial products earlier. Let me check this way again.\n\nWait, 285 multiplied by 628.\n\nFirst, 285 \u00d7 600 = 285 \u00d7 6 \u00d7 100 = (285 \u00d7 6) \u00d7 100.\n\n285 \u00d7 6: 200\u00d76=1200, 80\u00d76=480, 5\u00d76=30. Adding those: 1200+480=1680, +30=1710. So \u00d7100 is 171,000.\n\n285 \u00d7 20 = 285 \u00d7 2 \u00d710 = 570 \u00d710 =5,700.\n\n285 \u00d78: 200\u00d78=1600, 80\u00d78=640, 5\u00d78=40. 1600+640=2240 +40=2280.\n\nAdding all three: 171,000 +5,700 =176,700; 176,700 +2,280=178,980. So the product should be 178,980.\n\nWait a second, but when I tried the standard algorithm earlier, I got confused, but this method seems straightforward. Let me confirm with another method, like the distributive property.\n\nAlternatively, 285 \u00d7628 = (200 +80 +5) \u00d7(600 +20 +8).\n\nMultiplying term by term:\n\n200\u00d7600 = 120,000\n\n200\u00d720 =4,000\n\n200\u00d78 =1,600\n\n80\u00d7600 =48,000\n\n80\u00d720 =1,600\n\n80\u00d78 =640\n\n5\u00d7600 =3,000\n\n5\u00d720 =100\n\n5\u00d78 =40.\n\nNow add all these up:\n\nStart with the largest terms:\n\n120,000 +48,000 =168,000\n\n168,000 +3,000 =171,000\n\nNext, 4,000 + 1,600 =5,600\n\n5,600 +1,600 =7,200\n\n7,200 +640 =7,840\n\n7,840 +100 =7,940\n\n7,940 +40 =7,980.\n\nNow add all those partial sums:\n\n171,000 (from the first group) +7,980 (second group) =178,980.\n\nYes, same result. So that's the correct product.\n\nBut wait, the original question was 746 multiplied by 536, not 285\u00d7628. Did I misread the problem?\n\nOh no! The user asked for 746 \u00d7 536, but in my thinking above I started working on 285\u00d7628. That was a mistake. I need to correct that.\n\nAlright, let me start over properly.\n\nProblem: 746 \u00d7 536.\n\nLet me use the standard algorithm this time correctly.\n\nFirst, write the numbers vertically aligned to the right:\n\n\u2003\u2003746\n\n\u00d7 536\n\n----------\n\nStarting with the rightmost digit of the second number (6):\n\nMultiply 746 by 6.\n\n6 \u00d7 6 = 36. Write down 6, carry over 3.\n\n6 \u00d7 4 = 24 + 3 = 27. Write down 7, carry over 2.\n\n6 \u00d7 7 = 42 + 2 = 44. Write down 44.\n\nSo the first partial product is 4,476.\n\nNext, multiply by the middle digit (3), which is in the tens place, so we'll shift one position to the left. Since it's the tens digit, the multiplication is by 30.\n\n3 \u00d7 6 = 18. Write down 8, carry over 1.\n\n3 \u00d7 4 = 12 + 1 = 13. Write down 3, carry over 1.\n\n3 \u00d7 7 = 21 + 1 = 22. Write down 22.\n\nSo the second partial product is 22,308 (since we shift one place left).\n\nNow multiply by the leftmost digit (5), which is in the hundreds place, so 500. Shift two positions to the left.\n\n5 \u00d7 6 = 30. Write down 0, carry over 3.\n\n5 \u00d7 4 = 20 + 3 = 23. Write down 3, carry over 2.\n\n5 \u00d7 7 = 35 + 2 = 37. Write down 37.\n\nSo the third partial product is 37,300 (shifted two places left, so actually 373,000).\n\nWait, hold on. Let me check again.\n\nWait, multiplying 746 by 5 (hundreds place, so 500):\n\nThe actual multiplication is 5 \u00d7 746 = ?\n\n5 \u00d7 6 = 30. Write 0, carry 3.\n\n5 \u00d7 4 = 20 + 3 = 23. Write 3, carry 2.\n\n5 \u00d77 = 35 +2=37. So that gives 3730. Since it's the hundreds place, we need to shift two zeros, so it becomes 373,000.\n\nTherefore, the three partial products are:\n\n4,476 (units)\n\n22,308 (tens)\n\n373,000 (hundreds)\n\nNow add them up:\n\nFirst, add 4,476 + 22,308:\n\n4,476 + 22,308:\n\n4,000 + 22,000 = 26,000\n\n476 + 308 = 784\n\nTotal: 26,000 + 784 = 26,784.\n\nNow add 373,000 to that:\n\n26,784 + 373,000 = 400, 000? Let me compute step by step.\n\n26,784 + 300,000 = 326,784\n\nThen add 73,000: 326,784 + 73,000 = 400,  326,784 +70,000 = 396,784, plus 3,000 = 399,784.\n\nWait, 326,784 + 373,000 is:\n\n326,784 + 373,000:\n\n300,000 + 300,000 = 600,000\n\n26,784 +73,000 = 99,784\n\nTotal: 600,000 + 99,784 = 699,784.\n\nWait, no, that's not right. Wait 26,784 + 373,000:\n\nBreakdown:\n\n373,000 + 20,000 = 393,000\n\n393,000 + 6,784 = 399,784.\n\nYes, so the total sum is 399,784.\n\nBut let me check the addition again:\n\nFirst partial product: 4,476\n\nSecond: 22,308 \u2192 Total so far: 26,784\n\nThird: 373,000 \u2192 26,784 + 373,000 = 399,784.\n\nHmm, but let's verify using another method to be sure.\n\nAlternative method: Break down the numbers.\n\n746 \u00d7 536 = 746 \u00d7 (500 + 36) = 746\u00d7500 + 746\u00d736.\n\nCompute each part:\n\n746 \u00d7500 = 746 \u00d75 \u00d7100 = 3,730 \u00d7100 = 373,000.\n\n746 \u00d736: Let's compute that.\n\nFirst, break down 36 as 30 +6.\n\n746 \u00d730 = 746 \u00d73 \u00d710 = 2,238 \u00d710 =22,380.\n\n746 \u00d76 = 4,476 (as before).\n\nAdding those: 22,380 +4,476 =26,856.\n\nTherefore, total product is 373,000 +26,856 = 399,856.\n\nWait, hold on! Now there's a discrepancy. Earlier, using the standard algorithm, I got 399,784, but using this breakdown, it's 399,856. Which one is correct?\n\nHmm, so I must have made an error in one of the methods.\n\nLet me recalculate the standard algorithm step:\n\nFirst partial product (units digit 6):\n\n746 \u00d76: 6\u00d76=36 (write 6, carry 3)\n\n6\u00d74=24 +3=27 (write 7, carry 2)\n\n6\u00d77=42 +2=44 (write 44). So that is 4,476. Correct.\n\nSecond partial product (tens digit 3, so \u00d730):\n\n746 \u00d73:\n\n3\u00d76=18 (write 8, carry 1)\n\n3\u00d74=12 +1=13 (write 3, carry 1)\n\n3\u00d77=21 +1=22 (write 22). So that is 2,238. But since it's the tens place, it's shifted one to the left, so 22,380. Wait, in my initial calculation I said 22,308. That's the mistake!\n\nAh, here's the error. Earlier when I did the second partial product, I must have miscalculated the units digit.\n\nWait, when I multiplied 746 by 3 (the tens digit), the result should be 2,238, and then shifted left by one (for the tens place), so it becomes 22,380, not 22,308. So that was my mistake in the first calculation.\n\nSo the three partial products are:\n\n4,476 (units)\n\n22,380 shifted left one \u2192 22,380 \u00d710? Wait no, shifting one digit to the left is equivalent to multiplying by 10. So 746\u00d730=22,380.\n\nThird partial product: 746\u00d7500=373,000.\n\nAdding them up:\n\nFirst two: 4,476 +22,380 = 26,856\n\nThen 26,856 +373,000 = 399,856. Which matches the second method.\n\nSo where did I go wrong in the initial standard algorithm? Let me retrace.\n\nEarlier, in the second partial product (the 3 in the tens place):\n\nI wrote \"the second partial product is 22,308 (since we shift one place left).\" But actually, 746\u00d73\u00d710 is 22,380. So the mistake was in the second partial product calculation: 3\u00d7746 is 2,238, not 2230.8. So I must have miscalculated 3\u00d7746 as 2230 instead of 2238.\n\nTherefore the correct total is 399,856.\n\nLet me verify with another method, perhaps the expanded form:\n\n746 \u00d7536 = (700 +40 +6) \u00d7 (500 +30 +6).\n\nMultiply each term:\n\nFirst, 700\u00d7500 = 350,000\n\n700\u00d730 =21,000\n\n700\u00d76 =4,200\n\n40\u00d7500 =20,000\n\n40\u00d730 =1,200\n\n40\u00d76 =240\n\n6\u00d7500 =3,000\n\n6\u00d730 =180\n\n6\u00d76 =36\n\nNow add all these together:\n\nStart with the largest terms:\n\n350,000 +21,000 =371,000\n\n371,000 +4,200 =375,200\n\nNext group:\n\n20,000 +1,200 =21,200\n\n21,200 +240 =21,440\n\nNext:\n\n3,000 +180 =3,180\n\n3,180 +36 =3,216\n\nNow add all three big groups:\n\n375,200 +21,440 =396,640\n\n396,640 +3,216 =399,856.\n\nYes, that matches. So the correct product is 399,856.\n\nTherefore, my initial mistake was in the second partial product calculation during the standard algorithm, where I incorrectly calculated 746\u00d73 as 2,230 instead of 2,238.\n\nSo the correct answer is 399,856.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 746 and 536 is \\boxed{399856}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 746 and 536, we can use the standard algorithm and verify with an expanded form approach.\n\n**Using the Standard Algorithm:**\n\n1. **Multiply 746 by 6 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     746 \\\\\n   \\times \\ 6 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     4476 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   \\[\n   6 \\times 6 = 36 \\quad (\\text{write } 6, \\text{ carry } 3) \\\\\n   6 \\times 4 = 24 + 3 = 27 \\quad (\\text{write } 7, \\text{ carry } 2) \\\\\n   6 \\times 7 = 42 + 2 = 44 \\quad (\\text{write } 44)\n   \\]\n   Partial product: 4,476.\n\n2. **Multiply 746 by 3 (tens place, shifted left by one):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     746 \\\\\n   \\times 30 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     22380 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 6 = 18 \\quad (\\text{write } 8, \\text{ carry } 1) \\\\\n   3 \\times 4 = 12 + 1 = 13 \\quad (\\text{write } 3, \\text{ carry } 1) \\\\\n   3 \\times 7 = 21 + 1 = 22 \\quad (\\text{write } 22)\n   \\]\n   Partial product shifted left by one: 22,380.\n\n3. **Multiply 746 by 5 (hundreds place, shifted left by two):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     746 \\\\\n   \\times 500 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     373000 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 6 = 30 \\quad (\\text{write } 0, \\text{ carry } 3) \\\\\n   5 \\times 4 = 20 + 3 = 23 \\quad (\\text{write } 3, \\text{ carry } 2) \\\\\n   5 \\times 7 = 35 + 2 = 37 \\quad (\\text{write } 37)\n   \\]\n   Partial product shifted left by two: 373,000.\n\n4. **Sum the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   4,476 + 22,380 = 26,856 \\\\\n   26,856 + 373,000 = 399,856\n   \\]\n\n**Verification with Expanded Form:**\n\\[\n746 \\times 536 = (700 + 40 + 6) \\times (500 + 30 + 6)\n\\]\nBreaking down and summing all terms:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&700 \\times 500 = 350,000 \\\\\n&700 \\times 30 = 21,000 \\\\\n&700 \\times 6 = 4,200 \\\\\n&40 \\times 500 = 20,000 \\\\\n&40 \\times 30 = 1,200 \\\\\n&40 \\times 6 = 240 \\\\\n&6 \\times 500 = 3,000 \\\\\n&6 \\times 30 = 180 \\\\\n&6 \\times 6 = 36 \\\\\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nAdding all these together:\n\\[\n350,000 + 21,000 + 4,200 + 20,000 + 1,200 + 240 + 3,000 + 180 + 36 = 399,856\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 746 and 536 is \\boxed{399856}.",
