atively, maybe using calculator steps. Let me do 444 \u00d7 981:\n\nCompute 444 \u00d7 981:\n\nBreakdown:\n\n981 \u00d7 400 = 392,400\n\n981 \u00d7 40 = 39,240\n\n981 \u00d74 = 3,924\n\nAdding all together: 392,400 + 39,240 = 431,640 + 3,924 = 435,564.\n\nSo, all methods lead to 435,564. Therefore, the correct answer should be 435,564. \n\nI think initially I misread the problem as different numbers, which led me to confusion, but upon correcting that, the calculations are consistent. So I can confidently say the product is 435,564.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 444 and 981 is \\boxed{435564}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 444 and 981, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into more manageable parts. Here are the key steps:\n\n1. **Breakdown using the distributive property**:\n   \\[\n   444 \\times 981 = 444 \\times (1000 - 19)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 444 \\times 1000 - 444 \\times 19\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate each part separately**:\n   - \\(444 \\times 1000 = 444000\\)\n   - \\(444 \\times 19\\):\n     \\[\n     444 \\times 10 = 4440\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     444 \\times 9 = 3996\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     4440 + 3996 = 8436\n     \\]\n\n3. **Subtract the results**:\n   \\[\n   444000 - 8436 = 435564\n   \\]\n\n4. **Verification using standard multiplication**:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n        444 \\\\\n     \\times 981 \\\\\n     \\hline\n        444 \\quad \\text{(444 \u00d7 1)} \\\\\n      35520 \\quad \\text{(444 \u00d7 80)} \\\\\n    399600 \\quad \\text{(444 \u00d7 900)} \\\\\n     \\hline\n     435564 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 444 and 981 is \\(\\boxed{435564}\\).",
