ce, shift one position to the left.\n\nFirst compute 841 \u00d76 = ?\n\n800\u00d76 =4,800\n\n40\u00d76=240\n\n1\u00d76=6\n\nTotal: 4,800 + 240 =5,040 +6 =5,046. So 5,046 \u00d710 =50,460. So second partial product is 50,460.\n\nThird digit is the hundreds place of 764, which is 7 (actually 700). Multiply 841 \u00d7700.\n\nFirst compute 841 \u00d77 = ?\n\n800\u00d77 =5,600\n\n40\u00d77=280\n\n1\u00d77=7\n\nTotal:5,600 +280 =5,880 +7 =5,887. Then \u00d7100 gives 588,700. So third partial product is 588,700.\n\nNow add all three partial products:\n\n3,364\n\n50,460\n\n+588,700\n\n------------\n\nAdding first two: 3,364 +50,460 =53,824.\n\nThen add 588,700: 53,824 + 588,700 = 642,524.\n\nOkay, so that's consistent with the distributive method. So my initial mistake must have been in the first approach when I was doing the partial products incorrectly. Probably miscalculations in the first method, maybe mixing up digits or places.\n\nTherefore, the correct product is 642,524.\n\nWait, but the user asked for the product of 841 and 764, right? Let me double-check the arithmetic once more.\n\nAlternatively, using another method: 841 \u00d7700 = 841 \u00d77 \u00d7100. 841\u00d77: 800\u00d77=5,600; 40\u00d77=280; 1\u00d77=7; total 5,600+280=5,880+7=5,887. So 5,887 \u00d7100=588,700.\n\nThen 841 \u00d760 = 841\u00d76\u00d710= (5,046)\u00d710=50,460.\n\n841\u00d74=3,364.\n\nAdding them: 588,700 +50,460 = 639,160 +3,364 = 642,524. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, use calculator verification:\n\nCompute 841 \u00d7764:\n\nLet me compute 800\u00d7700=560,000\n\n800\u00d760=48,000 \u2192 total 608,000\n\n800\u00d74=3,200 \u2192 611,200\n\n40\u00d7700=28,000 \u2192 639,200\n\n40\u00d760=2,400 \u2192 641,600\n\n40\u00d74=160 \u2192 641,760\n\n1\u00d7700=700 \u2192642,460\n\n1\u00d760=60 \u2192642,520\n\n1\u00d74=4 \u2192642,524. Yep, same result.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 642,524.\n\nBut the user initially mentioned \"Product of 841 and 764\" and my first attempt had a miscalculation but corrected it, so the final answer is 642,524.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 841 and 764 is \\boxed{642524}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 841 and 764, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm by breaking it down into partial products and then summing them up.\n\n1. **Multiply 841 by the units digit of 764 (4):**\n   \\[\n   841 \\times 4 = 3364\n   \\]\n   This is the first partial product.\n\n2. **Multiply 841 by the tens digit of 764 (60):**\n   \\[\n   841 \\times 60 = 50460\n   \\]\n   This is the second partial product.\n\n3. **Multiply 841 by the hundreds digit of 764 (700):**\n   \\[\n   841 \\times 700 = 588700\n   \\]\n   This is the third partial product.\n\n4. **Sum all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   3364 + 50460 + 588700\n   \\]\n   - Adding the first two partial products:\n     \\[\n     3364 + 50460 = 53824\n     \\]\n   - Adding the result to the third partial product:\n     \\[\n     53824 + 588700 = 642524\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 841 and 764 is \\(\\boxed{642524}\\).",
