lace, so multiplying 6 × 512 gives 0916, then shifted two places to the left would be 946577? Wait, let me confirm:.\n\nWait 4 × 677 is 0873. Then, because it's the hundreds digit, we need to shift two places, so it's 7941 multiplied by 342, which is 553632. Wait, but actually, in the standard multiplication, when you write it down, it would be:.\n\nFirst partial product: 285 (from the 8).\n\nSecond partial product: 2604 (from the 2, shifted one place).\n\nThird partial product: 8611 shifted two places, so 817537?.\n\nWait, but actually, when you write it out:.\n\n\u2003\u2003\u2003181.\n\n×\u202f\u202f896.\n\n--------.\n\n\u2003\u2003301\u202f\u202f (461 × 5).\n\n\u20030253\u202f\u202f (671 × 41, so shifted one).\n\n+961633 (649 × 335, shifted two).\n\nThen add them all together.\n\nWait, but let me verify the multiplication again for the 4:.\n\n5 × 208:.\n\n0 × 9 = 63 → 3, carryover 7.\n\n4 × 6 = 79 +6 =95 → 9, carryover 4.\n\n8 × 8 =50 +6 =26 → 66. So the result is 6050, yes. Then shifted two places (because it's the hundreds place) would be 9136 followed by two zeros? Wait no, actually, the shift is done by writing it two places over. Let me write it as:.\n\n\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003981.\n\n\u2003\u2003×\u202f161.\n\n\u2003\u2003--------.\n\n\u2003\u2003\u2003009\u202f (×6).\n\n\u2003\u202f3598\u202f (×8, shifted one).\n\n+1980\u202f (×8, shifted two?).\n\nWait, actually, perhaps I need to write each partial product properly.\n\nWait, let's see:.\n\nWhen you do 770 × 1 (units), it's 898.\n\nThen 101 × 7 (tens place) is 6274, so you write that shifted one to the left (so the zero is in the units, 7 in the tens, etc.).\n\nThen 194 × 1 (hundreds place) is 5852, shifted two to the left, so it's 548151? Wait, no, because if you shift two places, you add two zeros? Let me think again.\n\nAlternatively, maybe it's better to do the multiplication step by step with shifts:.\n\nFirst partial product: 143 × 9 = 684.\n\nSecond partial product: 988 × 91 = 214 ×6 ×44 = 2853 ×68 = 66,175? Wait, that can't be. Wait, no, 472 ×9 is 8999, so times 37 is 30,021? Wait, but 95 is 4×51, so 490×77 is indeed 66,738. But when writing the partial products, you just shift one place. Let me see:.\n\nWait, if you have 902 × 819, breaking down the multiplier:.\n\n571 = 536 + 75 + 9.\n\nTherefore, the total product is 804×648 + 572×46 + 500×9.\n\nSo 481×5 = 993,.\n\n499×34 = 435×2×32 = 4516×57 = 62,711,.\n\n048×661 = 292×7×799 = 6389×555 = 581,247.\n\nThen adding them all together:.\n\n665 + 54,482 = 91,045,. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
