check using a different approach. Let's use the distributive property in another way.\n\n220 \u00d7 776 = 220 \u00d7 (700 + 70 + 6) = 220\u00d7700 + 220\u00d770 + 220\u00d76.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n220\u00d7700 = 220\u00d77\u00d7100 = 1,540\u00d7100 = 154,000.\n\n220\u00d770 = 220\u00d77\u00d710 = 1,540\u00d710 = 15,400.\n\n220\u00d76 = 1,320.\n\nAdding them together: 154,000 + 15,400 = 169,400; then 169,400 + 1,320 = 170,720. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the commutative property, 776\u00d7220. Let's try multiplying 776 by 220 as 776\u00d722\u00d710.\n\nFirst compute 776\u00d722:\n\n776\u00d720 = 15,520\n\n776\u00d72 = 1,552\n\nAdding those gives 15,520 + 1,552 = 17,072.\n\nThen multiply by 10: 17,072\u00d710 = 170,720. Yep, same answer again.\n\nAlright, so all methods converge to 170,720. So I think that's the correct product. Maybe initially I was confused because I started with different numbers in my head, but after correcting myself, everything checks out.\n\nTherefore, the product of 220 and 776 is 170,720.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 220 and 776 is \\boxed{170720}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 220 and 776, we can use the distributive property and break down the multiplication into simpler steps.\n\nFirst, note that 220 can be expressed as 200 + 20. Therefore, we can compute the product as follows:\n\n\\[\n776 \\times 220 = 776 \\times (200 + 20)\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n\n1. \\( 776 \\times 200 \\):\n   \\[\n   776 \\times 200 = 776 \\times 2 \\times 100 = 1552 \\times 100 = 155200\n   \\]\n\n2. \\( 776 \\times 20 \\):\n   \\[\n   776 \\times 20 = 776 \\times 2 \\times 10 = 1552 \\times 10 = 15520\n   \\]\n\nAdding these two results together:\n\n\\[\n155200 + 15520 = 170720\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using another method by breaking down 776 into 700 + 70 + 6:\n\n\\[\n220 \\times 776 = 220 \\times (700 + 70 + 6)\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n\n1. \\( 220 \\times 700 \\):\n   \\[\n   220 \\times 700 = 220 \\times 7 \\times 100 = 1540 \\times 100 = 154000\n   \\]\n\n2. \\( 220 \\times 70 \\):\n   \\[\n   220 \\times 70 = 220 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 1540 \\times 10 = 15400\n   \\]\n\n3. \\( 220 \\times 6 \\):\n   \\[\n   220 \\times 6 = 1320\n   \\]\n\nAdding these results together:\n\n\\[\n154000 + 15400 + 1320 = 170720\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 220 and 776 is \\(\\boxed{170720}\\).",
