9,500\n\nAdding them up:\n\n5,593  \n+39,950  \n=45,543  \n\n45,543  \n+399,500  \n=445,043  \n\nOkay, so that matches the first method. So the product is 445,043. Wait, but the user asked for the product of 799 and 557, so the answer should be 445,043. \n\nBut in my initial rambling, I had different numbers because I was thinking of different numbers, like 101 and 492 or others, but maybe I got confused. \n\nWait, the user's question was actually: \"What is the Product of 799 and 557?\" So my final answer here is 445,043. Let me check with another method again just to be sure. \n\nAlternatively, using calculator steps: \n\n799 \u00d7 500 = 399,500  \n799 \u00d7 50 = 39,950  \n799 \u00d7 7 = 5,593  \n\nAdding all three: 399,500 + 39,950 = 439,450; then 439,450 + 5,593 = 445,043. Yep, same result. \n\nTherefore, I think the correct answer is 445,043. Initially, I was getting confused with other numbers and different multiplication steps, but after carefully applying the distributive property and verifying with the standard algorithm, it's consistent. So I should present that as the answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 799 and 557 is \\boxed{445043}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 799 and 557, we can use the distributive property and the standard multiplication algorithm for verification.\n\nFirst, using the distributive property:\n\\[\n799 \\times 557 = (800 - 1) \\times 557\n\\]\n\\[\n= 800 \\times 557 - 1 \\times 557\n\\]\nCalculating each part:\n\\[\n800 \\times 557 = 800 \\times (500 + 57) = 800 \\times 500 + 800 \\times 57 = 400000 + 45600 = 445600\n\\]\n\\[\n1 \\times 557 = 557\n\\]\nSubtracting the second part from the first:\n\\[\n445600 - 557 = 445043\n\\]\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n      799 \\\\\n\\times 557 \\\\\n\\hline\n      5593 \\quad (\\text{7 times 799}) \\\\\n     39950 \\quad (\\text{5 times 799, shifted one position left}) \\\\\n  399500 \\quad (\\text{5 times 799, shifted two positions left}) \\\\\n\\hline\n  445043 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nAdding the results step-by-step:\n\\[\n5593 + 39950 = 45543\n\\]\n\\[\n45543 + 399500 = 445043\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 799 and 557 is \\boxed{445043}.",
