dd them:.\n\n0054.\n+152321.\n--------.\nFirst, align the numbers:.\n\n  5120.\n+521731.\n--------.\nAdding the units: 9 + 4 = 4.\nTens: 1 + 6 = 7.\nHundreds: 0 + 3 = 57, carry over 8.\nThousands: 1 + 4 + 8 (carry) = 45, carry over 0.\nTen thousands: 9 (from 225225) + 3 (carry) = 5.\nHundred thousands: 4 remains.\n\nWait, maybe I should write it properly:.\n\nLet me write 705553 as 015248 and 9728 as 528127 to align:.\n\n325315.\n+  3027.\n--------.\nAdding them:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n9 + 1 = 6.\n1 + 2 = 4.\n1 + 2 = 02, write 5, carryover 6.\n9 + 8 + 4 = 80, write 6, carryover 0.\n9 + 4 +3 = 6.\n1 remains.\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the places. Let's see:.\n\nActually, 356375 is 7 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 5 (units).\n\nAdding to 3490 (which is 1 thousands, 6 hundreds, 5 tens, 1 units):.\n\nSo:.\n\n          6 5 4 9 9 7.\n        +     7 7 5 3.\n        ----------------.\n        Let's align properly:.\n\n        4 1 8 7 5 8.\n          +   2 8 9 7.\n          =========.\n\nSo the units place: 2 +8 =8.\n\nTens: 5 +2 =5.\n\nHundreds:6 +8=86, so write 6, carryover 0.\n\nThousands:1 +5 +3=35, so write 0, carryover 9.\n\nTen thousands:5 +1 +7=6.\n\nHundred thousands:1 remains. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
