478,200 +4,800 = 483,000\n\nThen 483,000 -18 = 482,982.\n\nSame result again. So that's consistent. Therefore, the correct answer should be 482,982.\n\nI think my confusion in the initial steps was because I was mixing up the digits and probably miscalculating the partial products. Breaking it down into components like the distributive property makes it clearer. So the final answer is 482,982.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 606 and 797 is \\boxed{482982}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 606 and 797, we can use the distributive property to break down the multiplication into simpler steps:\n\n\\[\n606 \\times 797 = 606 \\times (800 - 3)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(606 \\times 800\\):\n\n\\[\n606 \\times 8 = 4848 \\implies 4848 \\times 100 = 484800\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(606 \\times 3\\):\n\n\\[\n606 \\times 3 = 1818\n\\]\n\nSubtract the second result from the first:\n\n\\[\n484800 - 1818 = 482982\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can also use the standard multiplication method:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   \\quad 606 \\\\\n\\times 797 \\\\\n\\hline\n   4242 \\quad (\\text{606} \\times 7) \\\\\n  54540 \\quad (\\text{606} \\times 90) \\\\\n+424200 \\quad (\\text{606} \\times 700) \\\\\n\\hline\n  482982 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nAdding the partial products:\n\n\\[\n4242 + 54540 = 58782\n\\]\n\\[\n58782 + 424200 = 482982\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 606 and 797 is \\(\\boxed{482982}\\).",
