      "text": "185 multiplied by 988 is equal to 42,845, 583, 840? Hmm, wait, maybe I made a mistake in addition somewhere.\n\nWait, let me try a different method to verify. Maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\nLet me write down 185 \u00d7 988.\n\nFirst, write 185 multiplied by 8, then 185 multiplied by 80, then 185 multiplied by 900, and add them all together.\n\nSo:\n\nFirst step:\n\n185 \u00d7 8 = 1,480.\n\nSecond step:\n\n185 \u00d7 80 = 14,800.\n\nThird step:\n\n185 \u00d7 900 = 166,500.\n\nAdd them up: 1,480 + 14,800 = 16,280. Then 16,280 + 166,500 = 182,780. Wait, but that gives 182,780, which seems low? Hmm, maybe I did that wrong.\n\nWait, 900 \u00d7 185 is indeed 166,500. 80\u00d7185 is 14,800. 8\u00d7185 is 1,480. Adding them together: 166,500 +14,800 is 181,300. Then add 1,480: 181,300 +1,480 = 182,780. Hmm, but let me check with another method.\n\nAlternatively, 185 \u00d7 988 can be rewritten as 185 \u00d7 (1000 - 12) = 185\u00d71000 - 185\u00d712.\n\nSo that's 185,000 - 2,220 = 182,780. Okay, so that matches the previous result.\n\nWait a second, so why did I get confused earlier with different numbers? Maybe I was thinking of a different problem. But in this case, the correct product should be 182,780.\n\nWait, but let me verify with calculator steps:\n\n185 \u00d7 988:\n\nFirst, 185 \u00d7 900 = 166,500.\n\n185 \u00d7 80 = 14,800.\n\n185 \u00d7 8 = 1,480.\n\nAdding them: 166,500 + 14,800 = 181,300.\n\nThen +1,480 = 182,780.\n\nYes, that's correct. So the product is 182,780. Hmm, so maybe my initial confusion was from mixing up numbers in my head, but the systematic approach gives 182,780. Let me check once more with another method.\n\nAlternatively, using the distributive property:\n\n185 \u00d7 988 = 185 \u00d7 (900 + 80 + 8) = (185\u00d7900) + (185\u00d780) + (185\u00d78) = 166,500 + 14,800 + 1,480 = 166,500 + 14,800 is 181,300; 181,300 +1,480 is 182,780. Yep, that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe compute using the standard multiplication:\n\n\u2003\u2003185\n\n\u00d7 988\n\n--------\n\nFirst, multiply 185 by 8: 1,480\n\nThen multiply 185 by 80 (which is 8\u00d710): 14,800\n\nThen multiply 185 by 900 (which is 9\u00d7100): 166,500\n\nAdding them all together: 1,480 +14,800 = 16,280; 16,280 +166,500 = 182,780.\n\nWait, but actually, when you do standard multiplication, you have to consider the positions:\n\nWait, actually, maybe I messed up the place values. Let's do it step by step properly.\n\nMultiplying 185 by 988:\n\nStart with the units digit of 988, which is 8:\n\n185 \u00d7 8 = 1,480.\n\nThen the tens digit is 8 (since 988 is 9 hundreds, 8 tens, 8 units):\n\nSo multiply 185 by 80 (the tens place):\n\n185 \u00d7 80 = (185 \u00d7 8) \u00d7 10 = 1,480 \u00d7 10 = 14,800.\n\nThen the hundreds digit is 9 (in the hundreds place, so it's 900):\n\n185 \u00d7 900 = 185 \u00d7 9 \u00d7 100 = (1,665) \u00d7 100 = 166,500.\n\nNow, adding up all three results:\n\n1,480 (units) +14,800 (tens) +166,500 (hundreds) = 1,480 +14,800 = 16,280; 16,280 +166,500 = 182,780.\n\nSo that's correct. Therefore, the product is 182,780.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using a calculator for verification, but since I can't use one, I have to rely on arithmetic.\n\nWait, but let me check another way: 185 \u00d7 1000 is 185,000. Since 988 is 12 less than 1000, subtract 185\u00d712 from 185,000.\n\n185\u00d712: 185\u00d710=1,850; 185\u00d72=370 \u2192 1,850+370=2,220.\n\nSo 185,000 - 2,220 = 182,780. Yep, same result.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 182,780.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 185 and 988 is \\boxed{182780}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 185 and 988, we can use the distributive property and break down the multiplication into smaller parts:\n\n1. Multiply 185 by 8 (the units place of 988):\n   \\[\n   185 \\times 8 = 1,480\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 185 by 80 (the tens place of 988):\n   \\[\n   185 \\times 80 = 14,800\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 185 by 900 (the hundreds place of 988):\n   \\[\n   185 \\times 900 = 166,500\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results of the three multiplications together:\n   \\[\n   1,480 + 14,800 + 166,500\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add \\(1,480 + 14,800\\):\n     \\[\n     1,480 + 14,800 = 16,280\n     \\]\n\n   - Then, add the result to \\(166,500\\):\n     \\[\n     16,280 + 166,500 = 182,780\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 185 and 988 is \\(\\boxed{182780}\\).",
