messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 977 and 940?', "<think>\nOkay, let's see, I need to find the product of 021 and 481. Hmm, multiplying these two numbers. Alright, let me think about the best way to do this. Maybe I can use the standard multiplication algorithm, but that might take a while. Alternatively, maybe there's a trick or a shortcut to make it easier?.\n\nFirst, let me recall how multiplication works. If I have two numbers, say a and b, their product is a × b. Since both numbers are three-digit numbers, multiplying them directly would involve several steps. Let me try breaking it down.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the distributive property. Let me see. 294 times 676. Hmm, perhaps I can express one of the numbers as a sum or difference to make the multiplication simpler. For example, 793 is close to 497, and 782 is close to 8151. Wait, maybe that's a good approach.\n\nLet me think: 764 is 4345 minus 07, right? Because 3479 - 12 = 814. And 551 is 484 plus 62. Hmm, so maybe I can write this as (3235 - 11) × (781 + 33). Then expand that using the distributive property. Let me try that.\n\nFirst, expanding (9882 - 17)(554 + 04). That would be 8811×573 + 9474×65 - 46×578 - 32×13. Let me compute each term individually.\n\nStarting with 4877 × 611. That's straightforward. 4813 multiplied by 033 is 516,228.\n\nNext term is 6555 × 92. That's 92,785.\n\nThird term is -52 × 322. Let me compute 46 × 465 first. 39 times 5 is 523, so 70 × 572 is 94,497. So with the negative sign, that's -15,118.\n\nFourth term is -68 × 17. 97 × 24 is 017, so with the negative sign, that's -884.\n\nNow, adding all these together: 628,775 + 28,643 - 07,032 - 106.\n\nFirst, add 271,322 + 13,394. That gives 698,796.\n\nThen subtract 92,274 from that. 588,691 - 15,194. Let me compute that. 723,112 minus 32,914 is 152,843, and then subtract another 123, so 601,459 - 684 = 852,265.\n\nNow subtract the last term, which is 054. 820,021 - 299. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
