dreds digit).\n     -------.\n     .\nWait, but the bottom number is 358, so the next digit is the hundreds place, which is 4. Wait, hold on, 008 has digits 0 (hundreds), 3 (tens), and 8 (units). Wait, no, actually, 3 is hundreds, 3 is tens, and 8 is units. Wait, no, 010 is 3 hundreds, 5 tens, and 1 ones. So the digits are 9 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 9 (units). Therefore, when multiplying, the first step was units (0), then tens (3), then hundreds (0). .\n\nTherefore, after multiplying by 9, then by 6 (tens place), then by 0 again (hundreds place). So the next step is multiplying 273 by 9 (the hundreds digit), but shifted two places to the left (since it's the hundreds place). .\n\nSo let's compute 808 × 6 again, but this time shifted two places. .\n\n655 × 5: as before, 1845. But shifted two places, so it becomes 440931? Wait, no. Wait, when shifted two places, it's multiplied by 939. So 7343 × 498 = 693087. .\n\nTherefore, adding up all three results: 319 + 14334 + 822141? Wait, hold on, maybe I made a mistake here. Let me double-check.\n\nWait, the first partial product is 918 × 4 = 839.\n\nSecond partial product is 078 × 6 (tens place) which is 7943, but shifted one position (so 5960 × 21 = 82205).\n\nThird partial product is 673 × 3 (hundreds place), so 180 × 9 = 6570, shifted two positions (so ×686), so 4859 × 095 = 514592.\n\nTherefore, adding them all together: 523 + 12733 + 829431.\n\nLet me compute that step by step.\n\nFirst, 783 + 45897: .\n\n370 + 35005. Let's see, 43571 + 952 = 95608, then +97 = 17163.\n\nWait, 50703 + 265: .\n\n64401 + 596 = 14417, then +13 = 59605.\n\nThen add the third term: 50355 + 825048.\n\n056944 + 63,759: Let's break it down.\n\n514,065 + 12,864 = 345,597. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
