ing them together:\n\n792 + 7920 = 8712\n\n8712 + 39600 = 48,312.\n\nWait, let me verify the addition step by step.\n\nFirst, 792 + 7920:\n\n792 + 7920:\n\nAdding units digits: 2 + 0 = 2\n\nTens: 9 + 2 = 11, write down 1, carry over 1.\n\nHundreds: 7 + 9 = 16 + 1 (carry) = 17, write down 7, carry over 1.\n\nThousands: 0 + 7 = 7 + 1 = 8.\n\nSo that's 8,712. Then adding 39,600 to that:\n\n8,712 + 39,600:\n\nUnits: 2 + 0 = 2\n\nTens: 1 + 0 = 1\n\nHundreds: 7 + 6 = 13, write 3, carry 1.\n\nThousands: 8 + 9 = 17 + 1 = 18, write 8, carry 1.\n\nTen-thousands: 0 + 3 = 3 + 1 = 4.\n\nSo total is 48,312. That seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, I can check using another method, like the distributive property:\n\n396 \u00d7 122 = 396 \u00d7 (100 + 20 + 2) = 396\u00d7100 + 396\u00d720 + 396\u00d72 = 39,600 + 7,920 + 792 = same as above.\n\nAdding those: 39,600 + 7,920 = 47,520. Then 47,520 + 792 = 48,312.\n\nAnother way, maybe breaking down the numbers differently:\n\n122 can be written as 120 + 2.\n\nSo 396 \u00d7 120 = 396 \u00d7 12 \u00d7 10.\n\nFirst compute 396 \u00d7 12:\n\n396 \u00d7 10 = 3,960\n\n396 \u00d7 2 = 792\n\nAdding those gives 3,960 + 792 = 4,752. Then multiply by 10: 47,520.\n\nThen add 396 \u00d7 2 = 792. So total is 47,520 + 792 = 48,312. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the standard algorithm again but more carefully.\n\n      396\n    \u00d7 122\n    --------\n      792   (396\u00d72)\n     7920   (396\u00d720)\n    39600   (396\u00d7100)\n    --------\n    48312\n\nYes, that adds up correctly. So the product should be 48,312.\n\nWait, but let me confirm once more with a different method to be absolutely sure.\n\nLet me use the complement method or another approach. Alternatively, approximate the result to check for reasonableness.\n\n396 is close to 400, and 122 is close to 120. 400 \u00d7 120 = 48,000. Our result is 48,312, which is a bit higher, which makes sense because we increased both numbers slightly. So that seems reasonable.\n\nAlternative