p the numbers in the partial products, but breaking it down into the distributive property made it clearer. So the final answer should be 303,308.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 764 and 397 is \\boxed{303308}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 764 and 397, we can use the distributive property and break down the multiplication into smaller parts:\n\n1. **Break down 397 into 300, 90, and 7:**\n   - Calculate \\(764 \\times 300\\):\n     \\[\n     764 \\times 300 = 764 \\times 3 \\times 100 = 2292 \\times 100 = 229200\n     \\]\n   - Calculate \\(764 \\times 90\\):\n     \\[\n     764 \\times 90 = 764 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 6876 \\times 10 = 68760\n     \\]\n   - Calculate \\(764 \\times 7\\):\n     \\[\n     764 \\times 7 = 5348\n     \\]\n\n2. **Add the results of the three multiplications:**\n   - First, add \\(229200\\) and \\(68760\\):\n     \\[\n     229200 + 68760 = 297960\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(5348\\):\n     \\[\n     297960 + 5348 = 303308\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 764 and 397 is \\(\\boxed{303308}\\).",
