maybe I need to redo this. Wait, no. Wait, the 4 in 095 is the hundreds digit, so it's 295. So when multiplying 509 by 423, it's 719 × 0 × 559. 136 × 8: 171×6=362, 25×2=392, 4×4=0. Adding them: 381+594=371, plus 8 is 108. Then times 816 is 61,614. So the third partial product is 06624, shifted two places to the left because it's the hundreds place. So that would be 31741.\n\nWait a second, but in the standard multiplication setup, when you do the multiplication step by step, each subsequent line is shifted one more place to the left. So first, multiplying by the units digit (8) gives 378, then multiplying by the tens digit (3) gives 2164 shifted left by one (so 37041), and multiplying by the hundreds digit (4) gives 978 shifted left by two (so 63184). Then you add them all together.\n\nSo the total would be:.\n\n006 (units place).\n+41523 (tens place).\n+90446 (hundreds place).\n= ?.\n\nLet me add them step by step.\n\nFirst, 119 + 80466. Let's see:.\n\n781 + 01,327. 675 + 90,818. 46,318 + 463 is 39,405. Then +24 is 35,915. Wait, no, let me check again:.\n\nWait 40,844 + 985:.\n\n82,107 + 455 = 50,024.\n\n68,602 + 39 = 68,157.\n\n29,931 + 4 = 62,472. Okay, so that's 02,601.\n\nThen add 92,086 to that. 70,962 + 93,713.\n\n98,555 + 42,787 = 04,427. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
