owed by two zeros is 22600. \n\nAlright, I think that's solid. No mistakes here. The key was realizing I misread the numbers initially and correcting that. So the answer is 22,600.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 100 and 226 is calculated by multiplying the two numbers together:\n\n\\[\n100 \\times 226 = 22,\\!600\n\\]\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n1. **Multiply 226 by 100:**  \n   Since multiplying by 100 adds two zeros to the end of the number,  \n   \\[\n   226 \\times 100 = 22,\\!600.\n   \\]\n\n2. **Verification:**  \n   - Break down 226 into \\(200 + 26\\):  \n     \\[\n     100 \\times 200 = 20,\\!000 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 100 \\times 26 = 2,\\!600.\n     \\]\n   - Add the results:  \n     \\[\n     20,\\!000 + 2,\\!600 = 22,\\!600.\n     \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{22600}\n\\]",
