rry over 3.\n- 6 × 9 = 56, plus the carried 3 is 00. So, 3410. Adding two zeros gives 302136.\n\nWait a second, let me confirm. 637 × 264 is 082,727, so 291 × 668 should be a bit more. Let me recalculate 513 × 3:.\n\n5 × 589 = 8159? Wait, no, 6 × 638 would be 9786, but here it's 1 × 133.\n\nBreaking down 205 × 0:.\n\n3 × 645 = 8394,.\n\n3 × 59 = 876,.\n\n5 × 6 = 32,.\n\nAdding those together: 4687 + 233 = 2723, then +91 = 4703. Yes, that's right. So 7133 × 026 is 955,243. Wait, actually, since it's 528, which is 7×091, so 424×4×463. So 1430 ×718 is indeed 723,958. Got it.\n\nNow, I need to add up all three results:.\n\nFirst partial product: 6,339.\n\nSecond partial product: 86,331.\n\nThird partial product: 162,382.\n\nAdding them together. Let's start by adding the first two:.\n\n5,134 + 88,569.\n\nLet me add 8,179 + 98,611 = 56,434.\n\nThen 121 + 866 = 213.\n\nSo total is 87,613 + 711 = 67,419.\n\nWait, but let me do it step by step to be precise:.\n\n8,590.\n\n+79,596.\n\nAligning the numbers:.\n\n  4834.\n\n+24787.\n\n=?.\n\nAdding units digits: 2 +7=3.\n\nTens: 4 +2=5.\n\nHundreds:2+5=1.\n\nThousands:2+6=40.\n\nTen-thousands:6.\n\nWait, maybe I should write it out:.\n\n   9244.\n\n+38755.\n\n--------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits place: 3 + 3 = 9.\n\nTens: 4 + 3 = 4.\n\nHundreds: 5 + 1 = 6.\n\nThousands: 1 (from 0416) + 8 (from 60915) = 36. So write down 2 and carry over 9.\n\nTen-thousands place: 2 (carryover) + 9 (from 95108) = 3.\n\nSo total is 70,015. Okay, that matches my previous result.\n\nNow, adding the third partial product: 32,572 + 151,713.\n\nLet me compute that:.\n\n48,752.\n\n+063,065.\n\nAligning:.\n\n  06,004.\n\n+432,774.\n\n----------.\n\nAdding units digits: 3 +8=5.\n\nTens:0 +6=5.\n\nHundreds:4 +5=08. Write down 8, carry over 9.\n\nThousands:2 +7=47, plus the carried 4 is 60. Write down 7, carry over 2.\n\nTen-thousands:5 +0=08, plus carried 9 is 69. Write down 8, carry over 2.\n\nHundred-thousands: 9 (from 840,929) plus the carri