f 862 and 829 is \\boxed{714598}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 862 and 829, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 862 by the units digit of 829 (9):**\n   \\[\n   862 \\times 9 = 7758\n   \\]\n   - \\(9 \\times 2 = 18\\) (write down 8, carry over 1)\n   - \\(9 \\times 6 = 54 + 1 = 55\\) (write down 5, carry over 5)\n   - \\(9 \\times 8 = 72 + 5 = 77\\) (write down 77)\n\n2. **Multiply 862 by the tens digit of 829 (2), shifted one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   862 \\times 20 = 17240\n   \\]\n   - \\(2 \\times 2 = 4\\)\n   - \\(2 \\times 6 = 12\\) (write down 2, carry over 1)\n   - \\(2 \\times 8 = 16 + 1 = 17\\) (write down 1724, then shift left by one)\n\n3. **Multiply 862 by the hundreds digit of 829 (8), shifted two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   862 \\times 800 = 689600\n   \\]\n   - \\(8 \\times 2 = 16\\) (write down 6, carry over 1)\n   - \\(8 \\times 6 = 48 + 1 = 49\\) (write down 9, carry over 4)\n   - \\(8 \\times 8 = 64 + 4 = 68\\) (write down 6896, then shift left by two)\n\n4. **Add all partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   7758 + 17240 + 689600\n   \\]\n   - First, add \\(7758 + 17240\\):\n     \\[\n     7758 + 17240 = 24998\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(689600\\):\n     \\[\n     24998 + 689600 = 714598\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 862 and 829 is \\(\\boxed{714598}\\).",
