mbers incorrectly. Maybe I confused the digits. Let me confirm once more with another method, perhaps breaking down both numbers into smaller components.\n\nAlternatively, 980 \u00d7 403 can be written as (1000 - 20) \u00d7 (400 + 3). Let's expand that:\n\nFirst, multiply 1000 by 400: 1000\u00d7400 = 400,000\n\nThen 1000\u00d73 = 3,000\n\nThen -20\u00d7400 = -8,000\n\nThen -20\u00d73 = -60\n\nAdding all together: 400,000 + 3,000 = 403,000\n\nThen subtract 8,000: 403,000 - 8,000 = 395,000\n\nThen subtract 60: 395,000 - 60 = 394,940. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlright, so it seems like the correct product is 394,940. I think my initial confusion was from splitting the numbers incorrectly in the first try, but after verifying with two different methods, I can be confident that 394,940 is the correct result.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 980 and 403 is \\boxed{394940}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 980 and 403, we can use the distributive property and break down the multiplication into smaller parts:\n\n\\[\n980 \\times 403 = 980 \\times (400 + 3)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(980 \\times 400\\):\n\n\\[\n980 \\times 400 = 980 \\times 4 \\times 100 = 3920 \\times 100 = 392000\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(980 \\times 3\\):\n\n\\[\n980 \\times 3 = (900 + 80) \\times 3 = 900 \\times 3 + 80 \\times 3 = 2700 + 240 = 2940\n\\]\n\nAdd the results of the two parts together:\n\n\\[\n392000 + 2940 = 394940\n\\]\n\nWe can also verify this by expanding the numbers differently:\n\n\\[\n980 \\times 403 = (1000 - 20) \\times (400 + 3)\n\\]\n\nExpanding this product:\n\n\\[\n1000 \\times 400 + 1000 \\times 3 - 20 \\times 400 - 20 \\times 3\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n\\[\n1000 \\times 400 = 400000\n\\]\n\\[\n1000 \\times 3 = 3000\n\\]\n\\[\n-20 \\times 400 = -8000\n\\]\n\\[\n-20 \\times 3 = -60\n\\]\n\nAdding these together:\n\n\\[\n400000 + 3000 - 8000 - 60 = 403000 - 8000 - 60 = 395000 - 60 = 394940\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 980 and 403 is \\(\\boxed{394940}\\).",
