ave any typos or miscalculations when I first broke it down. Let me check the 897\u00d721 again:\n\n21 \u00d7 800 = 16,800\n\n21 \u00d790 = 1,890\n\n21 \u00d77 = 147\n\nAdding those: 16,800 + 1,890 = 18,690; 18,690 + 147 = 18,837. Then \u00d710 gives 188,370. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, 21 \u00d7897:\n\nLet me compute 20\u00d7897 = 17,940\n\nPlus 1\u00d7897 = 897\n\nTotal is 17,940 +897 = 18,837. Yep.\n\nSo, all checks out. Therefore, the answer is 188,370.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 210 and 897 is \\boxed{188370}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 210 and 897, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Breaking down the numbers**:\n   - \\(210 \\times 897 = (200 + 10) \\times 897\\)\n   - Calculate \\(200 \\times 897\\):\n     \\[\n     200 \\times 897 = 179400\n     \\]\n   - Calculate \\(10 \\times 897\\):\n     \\[\n     10 \\times 897 = 8970\n     \\]\n   - Add the results:\n     \\[\n     179400 + 8970 = 188370\n     \\]\n\n2. **Using the distributive property**:\n   - \\(897 \\times 210 = 897 \\times (21 \\times 10)\\)\n   - Calculate \\(897 \\times 21\\):\n     \\[\n     897 \\times 20 = 17940 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 897 \\times 1 = 897\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     17940 + 897 = 18837\n     \\]\n   - Multiply by 10:\n     \\[\n     18837 \\times 10 = 188370\n     \\]\n\n3. **Verification using another method**:\n   - \\(210 \\times 900 - 210 \\times 3\\)\n     \\[\n     210 \\times 900 = 189000 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 210 \\times 3 = 630\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     189000 - 630 = 188370\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 210 and 897 is \\(\\boxed{188370}\\).",
