g:\n\nFirst step: 911 \u00d7 8 = 7,288.\n\nSecond step: 911 \u00d7 0 (tens place) shifted one position to the left: 0000.\n\nThird step: 911 \u00d7 3 (hundreds place) shifted two positions left: 911 \u00d7 300 = 273,300.\n\nAdding them up:\n\n7,288 (from the ones place)\n+ 0000 (from the tens place shifted left, which is actually zero)\n+273,300 (from the hundreds place shifted left two)\n= 7,288 + 273,300 = 280,588.\n\nHmm, that matches my previous result. So maybe I was confused earlier when I thought I messed up, but actually the correct answer is 280,588.\n\nWait, but let me check with another method to be sure.\n\nAnother way: use the formula (a+b)(c+d) = ac + ad + bc + bd.\n\nBut maybe breaking down the numbers further.\n\nLet me break 911 into 900 + 11, and 308 into 300 + 8.\n\nSo, (900 + 11)(300 + 8) = 900\u00d7300 + 900\u00d78 + 11\u00d7300 + 11\u00d78.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n900\u00d7300 = 270,000.\n\n900\u00d78 = 7,200.\n\n11\u00d7300 = 3,300.\n\n11\u00d78 = 88.\n\nNow add them all together:\n\n270,000 + 7,200 = 277,200.\n\n277,200 + 3,300 = 280,500.\n\n280,500 + 88 = 280,588.\n\nSame result again. So that must be correct.\n\nWait, but the user initially mentioned 509 and 044, but that's part of their example thought process. The actual question is 911 \u00d7 308. So the correct answer is 280,588.\n\nBut let me confirm once more with direct multiplication.\n\nMultiplying 911 \u00d7 308:\n\nStart with 911 \u00d7 8 = 7,288.\n\nThen 911 \u00d7 0 (tens place) gives 0, but shifted one to the left: 0000.\n\nThen 911 \u00d7 3 (hundreds place) which is 2,733 shifted two to the left: 273,300.\n\nAdding them:\n\n7,288\n\n+ 0 (since the middle term is zero)\n\n+273,300\n\nTotal is indeed 280,588.\n\nSo I think that's correct. Maybe in my first mistaken thought process I was confused with different numbers, but now focusing on the actual question, it's 280,588.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 911 and 308 is \\boxed{280588}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 911 and 308, we can use the standard multiplication method by breaking down 308 into 300 + 8.\n\nFirst, calculate \\( 911 \\times 300 \\):\n\\[\n911 \\times 300 = 911 \\times 3 \\times 100 = 2733 \\times 100 = 273300\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\( 911 \\times 8 \\):\n\\[\n911 \\times 8 = (900 \\times 8) + (11 \\times 8) = 7200 + 88 = 7288\n\\]\n\nAdd the results of these two calculations:\n\\[\n273300 + 7288 = 280588\n\\]\n\nWe can also verify this by breaking down both numbers using the distributive property:\n\\[\n(900 + 11)(300 + 8) = 900 \\times 300 + 900 \\times 8 + 11 \\times 300 + 11 \\times 8\n\\]\n\\[\n= 270000 + 7200 + 3300 + 88 = 270000 + 7200 = 277200\n\\]\n\\[\n277200 + 3300 = 280500\n\\]\n\\[\n280500 + 88 = 280588\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 911 and 308 is \\(\\boxed{280588}\\).",
