duct: 15,860\n\nThird partial product: 237,900\n\nAdding first and second:\n\n3,172\n\n+15,860\n\n= 19,032\n\nThen add the third:\n\n19,032\n\n+237,900\n\n= 256,932.\n\nHmm, so the total is 256,932?\n\nWait a second, but let me verify this with another method to be sure. Maybe using the distributive property.\n\nBreaking down the numbers:\n\n793 x 324 = 793 x (300 + 20 + 4) = 793x300 + 793x20 + 793x4.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n793 x 300 = 793 x 3 x 100 = 2,379 x 100 = 237,900.\n\n793 x 20 = 793 x 2 x 10 = 1,586 x 10 = 15,860.\n\n793 x 4 = 3,172.\n\nAdding those together:\n\n237,900 + 15,860 = 253,760\n\nThen add 3,172: 253,760 + 3,172 = 256,932.\n\nOkay, so that matches the previous result. So the product is 256,932.\n\nBut wait, hold on. Let me use another method to cross-verify. Maybe approximate to check reasonableness.\n\n793 is close to 800, 324 is close to 300.\n\n800 x 300 = 240,000. So the actual answer should be a bit higher, since 793 is slightly less than 800 but 324 is a bit more than 300. Let's see:\n\nThe difference: 800 - 793 = 7, so 7 less, and 324 - 300 = 24 more. So the approximate difference would be (800 x 300) - (7 x 300) + (800 x 24) - (7 x 24). Hmm, maybe that's too complicated.\n\nAlternatively, 793 x 324 = (800 - 7)(300 + 24) = 800x300 + 800x24 -7x300 -7x24.\n\nCalculating:\n\n800x300 = 240,000\n\n800x24 = 19,200\n\n-7x300 = -2,100\n\n-7x24 = -168\n\nAdding them up: 240,000 + 19,200 = 259,200\n\n259,200 - 2,100 = 257,100\n\n257,100 - 168 = 256,932.\n\nThat's exactly the same result! So that confirms it again.\n\nTherefore, the product of 793 and 324 is 256,932.\n\nI think that's solid. The steps all add up, and cross-verified with two different methods. So I can be confident that the answer is 256,932.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 793 and 324 is \\boxed{256932}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 793 and 324, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, we break down the multiplication step-by-step:\n\n1. **Multiply 793 by 4 (units place of 324):**\n   \\[\n   793 \\times 4 = 3172\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 793 by 20 (tens place of 324):**\n   \\[\n   793 \\times 20 = 15860\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 793 by 300 (hundreds place of 324):**\n   \\[\n   793 \\times 300 = 237900\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the partial products:\n\\[\n3172 + 15860 + 237900\n\\]\n\nAdding these together:\n\\[\n3172 + 15860 = 19032\n\\]\n\\[\n19032 + 237900 = 256932\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we use the distributive property:\n\\[\n793 \\times 324 = 793 \\times (300 + 20 + 4)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 793 \\times 300 + 793 \\times 20 + 793 \\times 4\n\\]\n\\[\n= 237900 + 15860 + 3172 = 256932\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the result. Therefore, the product of 793 and 324 is \\(\\boxed{256932}\\).",
