rrect that. The second partial product (from the 6 in the tens place) is 3539, but shifted one place to the left, so it's 93756? Wait, no. Wait, actually, when you write it down:.\n\nThe first multiplication (by units digit 3) gives 5992.\n\nThen, the next line is multiplying by the 6 (tens digit), so you write it shifted one to the left, so it's 9780 but shifted, so the 6 is in the tens place, so it would be 7910 shifted left once, meaning 24705? Wait, let's see:.\n\nIf you have:.\n\n       379.\n     x 771.\n     -------.\n        9028  (0 x 296).\n       3239   (8 x 222, but shifted one position to the left).\n      139     (9 x 767, shifted two positions to the left).\n     ---------.\n      ?.\n\nWait, actually, when you shift one position to the left, the 7147 becomes 23872? Because adding a zero at the end? Or is it written as 8959 but indented one space?.\n\nYes, in the standard multiplication, each subsequent line is shifted left by one more position. So multiplying by the tens digit, you shift left once, so the first digit is in the tens column. So writing 2148 shifted left once would be 84381? Wait, no, actually, no. Let me think numerically:.\n\nIf you have 799 x 0 (the tens digit), the result is 3264, but since it's the tens place, you need to multiply by 93, so 2313 x46 = 03302. Then the next digit is the hundreds place (7 in 516), so 217 x3 x355 = 00644.\n\nTherefore, adding them up:.\n\n6971.\n\n+39959.\n\n+66433.\n\nWait, let me add these numbers step by step.\n\nFirst, 8562 + 12036 = ?.\n\n5897 + 37387:.\n\nAdding units digits: 9 + 5 =1.\n\nTens: 3 + 0 = 5.\n\nHundreds: 9 + 0 =4.\n\nThousands: 9 +1 =4 (from 4523) and 7 (from 36357). Wait, actually, let me write them out:.\n\n02994.\n\n+ 9897.\n\n= ?.\n\nStart from the right:.\n\n7 +9 =0.\n\n1 +9 =0.\n\n0 +6 =0.\n\n4 +9 =0.\n\nSo it would be 20402?.\n\nWait, let's do it properly:.\n\n77897.\n\n+  3544.\n\n= 98755 + 7643 is 76463, plus 058 is 06797. Yes.\n\nThen adding the third partial product: 0065