ign the digits:.\n\nFirst, 1765 is:.\n\n   3,4,8,9 (units to thousands).\n\n29563 is:.\n\n6 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 1 (units).\n\nWait, perhaps writing them vertically:.\n\n      7031.\n\n+  69646.\n\n= ?.\n\nLet me write the smaller number under the larger one:.\n\n     2980.\n\n+ 48706.\n\n--------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits place: 4 +8 =6.\n\nTens:1 +3=8.\n\nHundreds:4 +5=0.\n\nThousands:8 +3=55 (write 2, carry over 5).\n\nTen-thousands: 7 +6 +6 (carry) =3.\n\nSo total is 27,167?.\n\nWait, wait, let me check again:.\n\nWait, 0298 is:.\n\n4 thousands (8724), 7 hundreds (642), 9 tens (06), 7 units (7). Total 3146.\n\n01959 is 85,369 + 6,491 + 447 + 03 = 66,939.\n\nAdding 1660 +39,531:.\n\n4807 +46,404 = 16,347 +3,369 =25,846; then +158 = 57,359. Okay, so that's correct.\n\nNow adding that to the third partial product: 892,679.\n\nSo 52,486 +930,171.\n\nAdding those:.\n\n07,937.\n\n+353,256.\n\n----------.\n\nAdding units: 2+9=2.\n\nTens:5+5=0.\n\nHundreds:0+2=50 (write 0, carry 5).\n\nThousands:8 (from 43,305's 4 in thousands place?) Wait, let's write them properly:.\n\n98,471 is:.\n\n4 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 5 (units).\n\n563,247 is:.\n\n8 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 6 (units).\n\nSo aligning:.\n\n   58,767.\n\n+970,357.\n\n----------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits:0 +5=2.\n\nTens:3 +7=5.\n\nHundreds:3 +9=36 (write 0, carry 7).\n\nThousands:2 (from 52,256's thousands place) + 4 (from 508,917's thousands place, which is 8 in the thousands?) Wait, let's see:.\n\nWait, 534,213 is 6 (027,964) 2 (03,759) 8 (4,592) 3 (363) 9 (35) 3 (9).\n\nSo the thousands place in 645,489 is 7 (the digit in the thousands place is the third digit from the right, which is 9). Wait, no, in 942,195:.\n\nPositions from right: units, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten thousands, hundred thousands.\n\nSo the digits are:.\n\nHundred thousands:9.\n\nTen thousands:0.\n\nThousands:6.\n\nHundreds:0.\n\nTens:5.\n\nUnits:8.\n\nSo the thousands place is 3 (the fourth digit from the right).\n\nIn the first number, 52,800:.\n\nHundred thousands:4.\n\nTen thousands:9.\n\nThousands:3.\n\nHundreds:7.\n\nTens:7.\n\nUnits:0.\n\nSo thousands place is 9.\n\nTherefore, thousands place addition: 5 (from 34,217) +7 (from 367,131) =5, plus the carried over 3 from hundreds place gives 7.\n\nTen thousands place:7 (from 62,130) +5 (from 840,574) =45. But wait, ten thousands place in 966,581 is 9 (the second digit from the left). Wait, maybe better to write it out step by step:.\n\nAdding:.\n\n738,635.\n\n+\xa034,582.\n\n------------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits:9 +8=8.\n\nTens:3+0=5.\n\nHundreds:4 +5=00, write 7, carry 7.\n\nThousands place:0 (from 573,184) +9 (from 20,440) =0, plus the carried 0 makes 7.\n\nTen thousands place:4 (from 118,967) +2 (from 94,058) =02. So write 4, carry 9.\n\nHundred thousands place:1 (from 749,262) +6 (from 38,164) =8, plus the carried 6 makes 8. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
