ntly say the answer is 170,387.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 241 and 707 is \\boxed{170387}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 241 and 707, we can use the distributive property and break down the multiplication step by step.\n\nFirst, we multiply 241 by 700:\n\\[\n241 \\times 700 = 241 \\times 7 \\times 100\n\\]\nCalculating \\(241 \\times 7\\):\n\\[\n241 \\times 7 = 1687\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n241 \\times 700 = 1687 \\times 100 = 168700\n\\]\n\nNext, we multiply 241 by 7:\n\\[\n241 \\times 7 = 1687\n\\]\n\nAdding the two results together:\n\\[\n168700 + 1687 = 170387\n\\]\n\nVerifying using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n- Multiply 241 by 7 (units place of 707):\n  \\[\n  241 \\times 7 = 1687\n  \\]\n- Multiply 241 by 0 (tens place of 707), resulting in 0 (shifted one position).\n- Multiply 241 by 7 (hundreds place of 707), resulting in 1687 (shifted two positions, so 168700).\n\nAdding all parts together:\n\\[\n1687 + 0 + 168700 = 170387\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 241 and 707 is \\(\\boxed{170387}\\).",
