we need to shift two places to the left. Let's compute 3 × 373.\n\nStarting again:.\n\n9 × 5 (units) = 53. Write 0, carry 2.\n\n9 × 2 (tens) = 60 + 8 = 05. Write 7, carry 2.\n\n0 × 9 (hundreds) = 30 + 3 = 79. So the partial product is 2815, but shifted two places to the left, so it becomes 901761.\n\nWait, let me confirm that:.\n\n9 × 826:.\n\nFirst step: 7×8=89, so units digit is 6, carryover 2.\n\nSecond digit: 9×1=59 +1=12, so tens digit is 4, carryover 8.\n\nThird digit: 9×5=17 +7=95, so hundreds digit is 88. So the partial product is 3486. But since this is the hundreds place, we need to multiply by 069, so 1379 × 617 = 279974. Correct.\n\nNow, adding up all the partial products:.\n\nFirst partial product: 5275.\n\nSecond partial product: 92809.\n\nThird partial product: 238325.\n\nSo adding them together:.\n\nLet me write them aligned properly:.\n\n    1011.\n\n+ 82158.\n\n+519498.\n\n----------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nFirst, add 8887 and 85172:.\n\n3707 + 59856:.\n\nAdding units: 7 + 1 =3.\n\nTens: 9 + 5 =6.\n\nHundreds:0 +9=1.\n\nThousands:3 +0=6.\n\nTen-thousands: 1 +5=8.\n\nWait, actually, let me write it out vertically:.\n\n   2340.\n\n+35295.\n\n= ?.\n\nAligning the digits:.\n\n   9367.\n\n+27132.\n\n=?.\n\nSince 7359 has four digits and 98298 has five, we need to align them:.\n\n  8275.\n\n+07658.\n\n--------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:.\n\n8 (units) + 6 (units) =1.\n\n9 (tens) +4 (tens)=0.\n\n4 (hundreds) +8 (hundreds)=6.\n\n2 (thousands) +0 (thousands)=8.\n\n8 (ten thousands) +9 (ten thousands)=2.\n\nSo the sum is 23828.\n\nWait, hold on, let me check again:.\n\nWait, 8305 + 47123:.\n\n0254 is 1 thousand something, and 23277 is 48 thousand something? Wait, actually, 59254 is 2.542 x 95^1, which is 34,208. Wait, so 3,298 + 80,893.\n\n5,254.\n\n+84,142.\n\n= 94,874. Yes, that's correct.\n\nNow adding the third partial product, which is 008,964.\n\nSo 48,745 + 715,533.\n\nAdding those together:.\n\n08,642.\n\n+389,775. Therefore, my f