328,400 + 54 = 328,454. Same result again.\n\nSo I think 328,454 is the correct answer. Therefore, I must have made a mistake in my initial confused thought process where I got a different number. Probably because I was mixing up the numbers or miscalculating the partial products. But with the systematic approach, it's clear.\n\nAnother way to check: using calculator approximation.\n\nWait, since I can't use a calculator, but maybe approximate:\n\n800 \u00d7 400 = 320,000.\n\nThen 800\u00d76 = 4,800 and 9\u00d7400 = 3,600, so total additional is 4,800 + 3,600 = 8,400. Adding to 320,000 gives 328,400, then plus 54 gives 328,454. So that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, the correct product is 328,454.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 809 and 406 is \\boxed{328454}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 809 and 406, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 809 by 6 (units place of 406):**\n   \\[\n   809 \\times 6 = 4854\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 809 by 0 (tens place of 406):**\n   \\[\n   809 \\times 0 = 0 \\quad \\text{(shifted one position to the left gives 00)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 809 by 4 (hundreds place of 406):**\n   \\[\n   809 \\times 4 = 3236 \\quad \\text{(shifted two positions to the left gives 323600)}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   4854 + 0 + 323600 = 328454\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n- Break down the numbers:\n  \\[\n  406 \\times 809 = 406 \\times (800 + 9) = (406 \\times 800) + (406 \\times 9)\n  \\]\n- Calculate each part:\n  \\[\n  406 \\times 800 = 324800\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  406 \\times 9 = 3654\n  \\]\n- Sum the results:\n  \\[\n  324800 + 3654 = 328454\n  \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 809 and 406 is \\(\\boxed{328454}\\).",
