8. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, using the standard algorithm again but carefully step by step:\n\nMultiply 616 by each digit of 523:\n\nFirst digit (units): 3.\n\n616 \u00d73: 6\u00d73=18, carryover 1; 1\u00d73=3+1=4; 6\u00d73=18. So 1,848.\n\nSecond digit (tens): 2, but shifted one left:\n\n616 \u00d720 = 616\u00d72\u00d710=1,232\u00d710=12,320.\n\nThird digit (hundreds): 5, shifted two left:\n\n616\u00d7500 = 616\u00d75\u00d7100=3,080\u00d7100=308,000.\n\nAdding them all gives 1,848 +12,320 =14,168; 14,168 +308,000 =322,168.\n\nAlternatively, cross-check using another method: 616\u00d7523.\n\nLet me try to compute (600+16)\u00d7(500+23):\n\n=600\u00d7500 +600\u00d723 +16\u00d7500 +16\u00d723.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n600\u00d7500 = 300,000.\n\n600\u00d723 = 13,800.\n\n16\u00d7500=8,000.\n\n16\u00d723 = 368.\n\nAdding all together:\n\n300,000 +13,800 =313,800.\n\n313,800 +8,000 =321,800.\n\n321,800 +368 =322,168. Same result.\n\nTherefore, I can confirm that 616 multiplied by 523 is indeed 322,168.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 616 and 523 is \\boxed{322168}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 616 and 523, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 616 by 3 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   616 \\times 3 = 1848\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 616 by 20 (tens place, shifted one position left):**\n   \\[\n   616 \\times 20 = 12320\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 616 by 500 (hundreds place, shifted two positions left):**\n   \\[\n   616 \\times 500 = 308000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   1848 + 12320 + 308000\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add \\(1848 + 12320\\):\n     \\[\n     1848 + 12320 = 14168\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(308000\\):\n     \\[\n     14168 + 308000 = 322168\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 616 and 523 is \\(\\boxed{322168}\\).",
