 254,400 + 5,088 = 259,488. That matches.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the standard vertical multiplication:\n\n\u2003\u2003424  \n\u00d7\u202f612  \n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014  \nFirst multiply by 2: 424\u00d72=848  \nThen multiply by 10: 424\u00d710=4,240  \nThen multiply by 600: 424\u00d7600=254,400  \nAdd all three: 848 + 4,240 = 5,088; 5,088 + 254,400 = 259,488.\n\nYes, so the product is 259,488.\n\nWait, but let me confirm once more with another technique, maybe breaking down the numbers differently.\n\nPerhaps using (400 + 24)*(600 + 12). Let's expand this:\n\n400*600 = 240,000\n\n400*12 = 4,800\n\n24*600 = 14,400\n\n24*12 = 288\n\nNow add all these together:\n\n240,000 + 4,800 = 244,800\n\n244,800 + 14,400 = 259,200\n\n259,200 + 288 = 259,488.\n\nSame result. Okay, so that must be correct. I think my initial confusion was because I was mixing up different numbers in my head, but now after multiple methods, I see it's 259,488.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the user made a typo in the question, but assuming the problem is correctly stated as 424 \u00d7 612, the answer is 259,488.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 424 and 612 is \\boxed{259488}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 424 and 612, we can use the standard multiplication method step by step:\n\n1. Multiply 424 by 2 (units place):\n   \\[\n   424 \\times 2 = 848\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 424 by 10 (tens place, shifted one position to the left):\n   \\[\n   424 \\times 10 = 4240\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 424 by 600 (hundreds place, shifted two positions to the left):\n   \\[\n   424 \\times 600 = 254400\n   \\]\n\n4. Add all the results together:\n   \\[\n   848 + 4240 + 254400\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add \\(848 + 4240\\):\n     \\[\n     848 + 4240 = 5088\n     \\]\n   \n   - Then add the result to \\(254400\\):\n     \\[\n     5088 + 254400 = 259488\n     \\]\n\nWe can also verify this using the distributive property:\n- Break down the numbers:\n  \\[\n  424 \\times 612 = 424 \\times (600 + 12)\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  = 424 \\times 600 + 424 \\times 12\n  \\]\n\n- Calculate each part:\n  \\[\n  424 \\times 600 = 254400\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  424 \\times 12 = 5088\n  \\]\n\n- Add the results:\n  \\[\n  254400 + 5088 = 259488\n  \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 424 and 612 is \\(\\boxed{259488}\\).",
