orrect.\n\nWait, but in my initial thinking process I had some muddled steps where I confused numbers like 854 and 817, but after starting over, I got 158,193. Let me confirm with another approach, perhaps breaking down the numbers differently.\n\nAnother way: 200 \u00d7 729 = 145,800\n\n17 \u00d7 729: Let's compute 10\u00d7729=7,290; 7\u00d7729=5,103; so total 7,290 +5,103 =12,393\n\nAdding to 145,800 +12,393 = 158,193. Same result again.\n\nOkay, so I think the correct answer is 158,193.\n\nBut wait, the user originally wrote \"Product of 217 and 729\" but in their initial thought process, they wrote 443\u00d7048, 854\u00d7817, etc. Maybe that was just confusion while thinking. But the final question is 217\u00d7729, which I solved as 158,193. Let me just verify once more with exact multiplication:\n\n217 \u00d7 729:\n\nBreakdown:\n\n217 \u00d7 700 = 217 \u00d7 7 \u00d7 100 = 1,519 \u00d7 100 = 151,900\n\n217 \u00d7 20 = 4,340\n\n217 \u00d7 9 = 1,953\n\nAdding all together:\n\n151,900 + 4,340 = 156,240\n\n156,240 + 1,953 = 158,193\n\nYes, that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, use the standard multiplication vertically:\n\n\u2003\u2003\u00a0217\n\n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a0729\n\n----------\n\nMultiply 217 by 9: 1,953\n\nMultiply 217 by 20 (shift one zero): 4,340\n\nMultiply 217 by 700 (shift two zeros): 151,900\n\nAdding them:\n\n1,953\n\n+4,340 \u2192 6,293\n\n+151,900 \u2192 158,193.\n\nYep. So the answer should be 158,193. Therefore, after careful calculation and multiple verifications, I can confirm that the product of 217 and 729 is 158,193.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 217 and 729 is \\boxed{158193}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 217 and 729, we can break down the multiplication into smaller parts using the distributive property:\n\n1. Calculate \\(217 \\times 700\\):\n   \\[\n   217 \\times 700 = 217 \\times 7 \\times 100 = 1519 \\times 100 = 151900\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(217 \\times 20\\):\n   \\[\n   217 \\times 20 = 4340\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\(217 \\times 9\\):\n   \\[\n   217 \\times 9 = 1953\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results of the three parts together:\n   \\[\n   151900 + 4340 + 1953\n   \\]\n\n   First, add \\(151900\\) and \\(4340\\):\n   \\[\n   151900 + 4340 = 156240\n   \\]\n\n   Then add \\(1953\\):\n   \\[\n   156240 + 1953 = 158193\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 217 and 729 is \\(\\boxed{158193}\\).",
