eds place, we need to shift it two places to the left, effectively multiplying by 100. So 2864 \u00d7 100 = 286,400. \n\nYes, that matches. \n\nAlternatively, using distributive property: 716 \u00d7 (400) = 716 \u00d7 (4 \u00d7 100) = (716 \u00d7 4) \u00d7 100 = 2864 \u00d7 100 = 286,400. \n\nAll methods lead to the same result, so I'm confident that the product of 716 and 400 is 286,400. \n\nJust to be absolutely sure, maybe I can do a quick estimation to check if this is reasonable. 700 \u00d7 400 = 280,000. Since 716 is 16 more than 700, then 16 \u00d7 400 = 6,400. Adding that to 280,000 gives 286,400. Exactly the same result. \n\nPerfect, that's a solid verification. So I think that's the correct answer.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 716 and 400 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication**:  \n   \\( 716 \\times 400 = 716 \\times (4 \\times 100) \\).\n\n2. **Multiply 716 by 4**:  \n   \\[\n   700 \\times 4 = 2,\\!800 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 16 \\times 4 = 64 \\\\\n   \\text{Total} = 2,\\!800 + 64 = 2,\\!864\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply the result by 100**:  \n   \\[\n   2,\\!864 \\times 100 = 286,\\!400\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer**:  \n\\boxed{286400}",
