t is 9 (since 77,756 has 6 in the ten thousands place?) Wait, maybe I should write them properly aligned:.\n\nActually, 5,098 is four thousand nine hundred fifty-six, and 35,527 is fifty-six thousand six hundred forty. So adding:.\n\n   0,818.\n+09,337.\n--------.\n= 20,482? Let me check:.\n\n6,048 + 89,733 =41,845. Then add 1,018: 47,691 +7,498=13,549; plus 152 is 32,005. Yes, that's right.\n\nNow add the third number, 02,098 to 07,201.\n\n82,151 +66,577.\n\nLet me compute this:.\n\n25,285 +44,045. Adding the thousands:.\n\n32,351 +48,783 =048,072. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
