standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 708 by 7 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   708 \\times 7 = 4956\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 708 by 80 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   708 \\times 80 = 708 \\times 8 \\times 10 = 5664 \\times 10 = 56640\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 708 by 100 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   708 \\times 100 = 70800\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the results together:**\n   \\[\n   4956 + 56640 + 70800\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add 4956 and 56640:\n     \\[\n     4956 + 56640 = 61596\n     \\]\n\n   - Then add the result to 70800:\n     \\[\n     61596 + 70800 = 132396\n     \\]\n\nTo verify, we can also use the distributive property:\n- **Express 187 as 200 - 13:**\n  \\[\n  708 \\times 187 = 708 \\times (200 - 13) = 708 \\times 200 - 708 \\times 13\n  \\]\n\n- **Calculate each part:**\n  \\[\n  708 \\times 200 = 141600\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  708 \\times 13 = 9204\n  \\]\n\n- **Subtract the results:**\n  \\[\n  141600 - 9204 = 132396\n  \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 708 and 187 is \\(\\boxed{132396}\\).",
