he carryover 6 makes 94, so write 9 and carryover 3.\n\nHundred-thousands: 0 (from 770,974) plus the carried over 4 = 3.\n\nWait, let me see:.\n\nWait 795,198 is:.\n\n9 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 9 (units).\n\n63,169 is:.\n\n5 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 3 (units).\n\nAdding digit by digit:.\n\nHundred thousands: 7 + 2 = 9.\n\nTen thousands: 9 + 1 = 42, so write 7 and carryover 4.\n\nThousands: 8 + 0 = 05, plus the carried over 2 makes 49, so write 4 and carryover 8.\n\nHundreds: 9 + 7 = 8, plus carryover 6 is 9.\n\nTens: 7 + 6 = 3.\n\nUnits: 7 + 6 = 0.\n\nWait, hold on, that might not be right. Let me do it properly:.\n\nWait, perhaps better to write them aligned:.\n\n   640559.\n\n+   25238.\n\n----------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:.\n\nUnits: 6 + 6 = 3.\n\nTens: 3 + 0 = 3.\n\nHundreds: 6 + 6 = 5.\n\nThousands: 1 (from 058957's thousands place) + 1 (from 66271's thousands place) = 68. So write 4, carryover 7.\n\nTen-thousands: 5 (from 707592) + 6 (from 05204) = 34, plus the carried over 3 is 28. Write 7, carryover 8.\n\nHundred-thousands: 5 (from 654524) + 8 = 1, plus the carried over 4 is 3. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
