rrect product is 521,252.\n\nJust to confirm once more, perhaps by another approach:\n\nLet me compute 604 \u00d7 800 = 604 \u00d7 8 \u00d7 100 = (600\u00d78)+(4\u00d78) = 4,800 + 32 = 4,832 \u00d7100 = 483,200.\n\nThen, 604\u00d760 = 604\u00d76\u00d710 = (600\u00d76)+(4\u00d76)= 3,600 +24 =3,624\u00d710=36,240.\n\n604\u00d73=1,812. Adding all together: 483,200+36,240=519,440. Then 519,440+1,812=521,252.\n\nYep, so that's correct. Therefore, the answer should be 521,252. I think my first approach had errors in the partial products or in the addition steps, but upon redoing it carefully, it's consistent.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 604 and 863 is \\boxed{521252}.\n</think>\n\nTo solve the product of 604 and 863, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into hundreds, tens, and units.\n\nFirst, we decompose the numbers:\n- 604 can be written as \\(600 + 4\\)\n- 863 can be written as \\(800 + 60 + 3\\)\n\nUsing the distributive property:\n\\[\n(600 + 4) \\times (800 + 60 + 3)\n\\]\n\nExpanding the product term by term:\n\\[\n600 \\times 800 + 600 \\times 60 + 600 \\times 3 + 4 \\times 800 + 4 \\times 60 + 4 \\times 3\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n600 \\times 800 = 480,000\n\\]\n\\[\n600 \\times 60 = 36,000\n\\]\n\\[\n600 \\times 3 = 1,800\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\times 800 = 3,200\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\times 60 = 240\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\times 3 = 12\n\\]\n\nAdding all these results together:\n\\[\n480,000 + 36,000 = 516,000\n\\]\n\\[\n516,000 + 1,800 = 517,800\n\\]\n\\[\n517,800 + 3,200 = 521,000\n\\]\n\\[\n521,000 + 240 = 521,240\n\\]\n\\[\n521,240 + 12 = 521,252\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 604 and 863 is \\(\\boxed{521252}\\).",
