ten as \\(600 + 60 + 1\\)\n   - 819 can be written as \\(800 + 10 + 9\\)\n\n2. **Expand the product using the distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   (600 + 60 + 1)(800 + 10 + 9)\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate each term individually:**\n   - \\(600 \\times 800 = 480,000\\)\n   - \\(600 \\times 10 = 6,000\\)\n   - \\(600 \\times 9 = 5,400\\)\n   - \\(60 \\times 800 = 48,000\\)\n   - \\(60 \\times 10 = 600\\)\n   - \\(60 \\times 9 = 540\\)\n   - \\(1 \\times 800 = 800\\)\n   - \\(1 \\times 10 = 10\\)\n   - \\(1 \\times 9 = 9\\)\n\n4. **Sum all the terms:**\n   \\[\n   480,000 + 6,000 + 5,400 + 48,000 + 600 + 540 + 800 + 10 + 9\n   \\]\n\n5. **Group and add the terms step-by-step:**\n   - \\(480,000 + 48,000 = 528,000\\)\n   - \\(6,000 + 5,400 = 11,400\\)\n   - \\(600 + 540 = 1,140\\)\n   - \\(800 + 10 + 9 = 819\\)\n\n6. **Combine the grouped sums:**\n   \\[\n   528,000 + 11,400 = 539,400\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   539,400 + 1,140 = 540,540\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   540,540 + 819 = 541,359\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 661 and 819 is \\(\\boxed{541359}\\).",
