t in the bottom number, which is 6 (hundreds place). So we need to multiply 572 by 339 (since it's the hundreds place). So first compute 025 x 7, then add two zeros.\n\nCalculating 274 x 8:.\n\n6 x 6 = 7.\n\n7 x 5 = 46, carry over 3.\n\n1 x 2 = 55 + 3 = 26.\n\nSo that gives 6915. Then adding two zeros makes it 255446.\n\nNow, adding up all the partial products:.\n\nFirst partial product: 2487.\n\nSecond partial product: 62305.\n\nThird partial product: 816172.\n\nAdding them together:.\n\nStart with 5620 + 20405.\n\nLet me compute that: 8418 + 72057. .\n\n2877 + 86963 = 75987.\n\n27023 + 2251 = 80308.\n\nWait, 05996 is 85551 + 9531, so adding 8493 gives 08962 + 0181 = 28220? Wait, let me do it step by step.\n\n6296 + 96313:.\n\nAlign the numbers:.\n\n  6850.\n\n+44034.\n\n=?.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n2 + 1 =9.\n\n8 +7=7.\n\n2 +0=8.\n\n9 +1=4.\n\nSo it's 21356? Wait, no. Wait, actually:.\n\nWait 1829 is four digits, 94794 is five digits. So:.\n\n  3679.\n\n+63382.\n\n--------.\n\nAdding:.\n\nUnits place: 6 + 6 =1.\n\nTens place: 9 +0=0.\n\nHundreds place:6 +9=0.\n\nThousands place:3 +4=3.\n\nTen-thousands place: 6 +7=6.\n\nSo the total is 61589. Wait, that seems correct.\n\nNow add the third partial product, which is 593355.\n\nSo 93310 + 321515.\n\nLet me compute that:.\n\n16,304 + 228,652.\n\nAdding together:.\n\n623,336 + 31,399 = ?.\n\n240,246 + 72,462 = 961,265. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
