n\n8 (ten-thousands), 1 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\n84185 has digits: 4 (ten-thousands), 9 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\nAdding them:.\n\nOnes: 6 +2 =4  .\nTens:9+3=5  .\nHundreds:1+5=02 → 1 with carryover2  .\nThousands:5 +9=55 +4 (carryover) =26 → 3 with carryover0  .\nTen-thousands:3 +4=7 +0 (carryover)=7. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
