 43,800\n\nNow add all three results:\n\n1,022 + 10,220 = 11,242\n\n11,242 + 43,800 = 55,042\n\nSame result. So that checks out.\n\nWait, but let me actually do the multiplication step by step as taught in school to ensure.\n\nMultiplying 146 by 377:\n\nStart with the units place:\n\n146 \u00d77:\n\n6\u00d77=42, write down 2, carryover 4.\n\n4\u00d77=28 +4=32, write down 2, carryover 3.\n\n1\u00d77=7 +3=10, write down 0 and carryover 1? Wait, no, since we're done with digits. Wait, 1\u00d77 is 7 plus 3 is 10, so write 0 and carryover 1, but there are no more digits, so add that 1 as the next digit. So the first partial product is 1,022.\n\nNext, multiply by the tens place (7 in the tens place, so 70):\n\nShift one position to the left, so we have:\n\n146 \u00d77 = 1,022, but shifted left once \u2192 10,220.\n\nThen multiply by the hundreds place (3 in the hundreds place, so 300):\n\n146 \u00d73 = 438, shifted left two positions \u2192 43,800.\n\nNow add them up:\n\n1,022\n\n+10,220\n\n=11,242\n\nThen add 43,800:\n\n11,242 +43,800 = 55,042.\n\nYep, that's the same as before. So I think that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, another way: using the distributive property as (140 +6)(370 +7).\n\nBut maybe that's more complicated, but let's try:\n\n(140 +6)(370 +7) = 140\u00d7370 +140\u00d77 +6\u00d7370 +6\u00d77\n\nCompute each term:\n\n140\u00d7370 = (100+40)\u00d7370 = 100\u00d7370 +40\u00d7370 = 37,000 + 14,800 = 51,800\n\n140\u00d77 = 980\n\n6\u00d7370 = 2,220\n\n6\u00d77 = 42\n\nAdd them up: 51,800 + 980 = 52,780\n\n52,780 + 2,220 = 55,000\n\n55,000 +42 =55,042.\n\nSame result again. So that's good.\n\nAlternatively, using the formula (a+b)(c+d) = ac + ad + bc + bd. That worked here.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the complement method? Not sure, but seems unnecessary here.\n\nAlternatively, check with calculator: but since I can't use a calculator, but perhaps do an approximate estimation to check.\n\n146 is approximately 150, 377 is approximately 400.\n\n150\u00d7400 = 