80 = 7,912.\n\nThen add 137,600 to that:\n\n7,912 + 137,600 = 145,512.\n\nYes, that matches the distributive method result. So the correct product is 145,512. Therefore, the initial confusion was due to errors in the first partial products calculation where I might have miscalculated the multiplication steps or the shifts.\n\nSo the answer is 145,512. I should have stuck to the straightforward method initially. It's easy to get confused with the partial products if not carefully aligned and calculated. This shows the importance of methodically breaking down the problem and verifying through different methods if possible.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 172 and 846 is \\boxed{145512}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 172 and 846, we can use the distributive property and standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nFirst, breaking down using the distributive property:\n\\[\n172 \\times 846 = 172 \\times (800 + 40 + 6)\n\\]\nCalculating each term separately:\n\\[\n172 \\times 800 = 172 \\times 8 \\times 100 = 1376 \\times 100 = 137600\n\\]\n\\[\n172 \\times 40 = 172 \\times 4 \\times 10 = 688 \\times 10 = 6880\n\\]\n\\[\n172 \\times 6 = 1032\n\\]\nAdding the results together:\n\\[\n137600 + 6880 + 1032 = 145512\n\\]\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n    172 \\\\\n\\times 846 \\\\\n\\hline\n    1032 \\quad (\\text{172} \\times 6) \\\\\n   6880 \\quad \\quad (\\text{172} \\times 40) \\\\\n+137600 \\quad \\quad \\quad (\\text{172} \\times 800) \\\\\n\\hline\n  145512 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 172 and 846 is \\(\\boxed{145512}\\).",
