n the first method where I broke it into (100+12)(700+28). Let me recalculate that:\n\n100\u00d7700 = 70,000\n\n100\u00d728 = 2,800 \u2192 70k + 2.8k = 72,800\n\nThen 12\u00d7700 = 8,400 \u2192 72,800 + 8,400 = 81,200\n\nThen 12\u00d728 = 336 \u2192 81,200 + 336 = 81,536. So that matches.\n\nTherefore, the product of 112 and 728 is 81,536.\n\nWait, but in my initial thought process, I started with 790 and 250 and then switched to 112 and 728. Maybe I had a brain fart. Let me confirm the problem again. The user asked for the product of 112 and 728. Yes, so the final answer is 81,536.\n\nBut just to be thorough, let me do the multiplication step by step again.\n\nMultiplying 112 \u00d7 728:\n\nFirst, write 728\n\n\u00d7 112\n\n------------\n\nStart with the units digit of 112 (which is 2):\n\n728 \u00d7 2 = 1,456\n\nThen the tens digit (1, but since it's the tens place, it's actually \u00d710):\n\n728 \u00d7 10 = 7,280\n\nThen the hundreds digit (1, but \u00d7100):\n\n728 \u00d7 100 = 72,800\n\nNow add them all together:\n\n1,456 (from 2)\n\n+7,280 (from 10) = 8,736\n\n8,736 + 72,800 (from 100) = 81,536. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do it vertically:\n\n\u202f\u202f\u202f728\n\n\u00d7112\n\n--------\n\nFirst, multiply 728 by 2: 1,456\n\nThen multiply 728 by 1 (tens place, so shifted one left): 7,280\n\nThen multiply 728 by 1 (hundreds place, shifted two left): 72,800\n\nAdd them:\n\n1,456\n\n+7,280\n\n=8,736\n\n+72,800\n\n=81,536\n\nYep, consistent. So the correct answer is 81,536.\n\nI think I confused myself initially when I started with different numbers but then corrected. But through multiple methods, it's 81,536. I don't see any errors in these calculations. So I'm confident that's the right answer.\n\n</think>\n\nThe product of 112 and 728 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Breakdown using distributive property**:\n   - \\(112 \\times 728 = (100 + 12) \\times (700 + 28)\\)\n   - Expand the terms:\n     - \\(100 \\times 700 = 70,\\!000\\)\n     - \\(100 \\times 28 = 2,\\!800\\)\n     - \\(12 \\times 700 = 8,\\!400\\)\n     - \\(12 \\times 28 = 336\\)\n   - Sum the results:\n     - \\(70,\\!000 + 2,\\!800 = 72,\\!800\\)\n     - \\(72,\\!800 + 8,\\!400 = 81,\\!200\\)\n     - \\(81,\\!200 + 336 = 81,\\!536\\)\n\n2. **Verification via standard multiplication**:\n   - Multiply \\(728 \\times 2 = 1,\\!456\\)\n   - Multiply \\(728 \\times 10 = 7,\\!280\\)\n   - Multiply \\(728 \\times 100 = 72,\\!800\\)\n   - Add the partial products:\n     - \\(1,\\!456 + 7,\\!280 = 8,\\!736\\)\n     - \\(8,\\!736 + 72,\\!800 = 81,\\!536\\)\n\n**Final Answer**: \\(\\boxed{81536}\\)",
