ke any calculation errors in the difference of squares method, let me recheck:\n\nFirst, 234.5^2:\n\nAlternatively, compute 234.5 \u00d7 234.5:\n\n234.5 \u00d7 200 = 46,900\n\n234.5 \u00d7 34.5 = ?\n\nWait, maybe that's more complicated. Alternatively, since 234.5 multiplied by itself is same as (234 +0.5)^2, which we did earlier as 54,990.25. Then subtract (6.5)^2 = 42.25, which gives 54,948. Correct.\n\nTherefore, all methods lead to the same answer. \n\nI think that's thorough enough. Initially, I made a mistake in misreading the numbers, but after correcting that, multiple methods confirm the result. So the answer should be 54,948.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 228 and 241 is \\boxed{54948}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 228 and 241, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify using different methods.\n\nFirst, we write down the numbers vertically and multiply step by step:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   228 \\\\\n\\times 241 \\\\\n\\hline\n   228 \\quad \\text{(228 \u00d7 1)} \\\\\n  9120 \\quad \\text{(228 \u00d7 40, shifted one position left)} \\\\\n+45600 \\quad \\text{(228 \u00d7 200, shifted two positions left)} \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nAdding the results:\n\n\\[\n228 + 9120 = 9348\n\\]\n\\[\n9348 + 45600 = 54948\n\\]\n\nWe can also verify using the distributive property by breaking down the numbers:\n\n\\[\n228 \\times 241 = 228 \\times (200 + 40 + 1)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 228 \\times 200 + 228 \\times 40 + 228 \\times 1\n\\]\n\\[\n= 45600 + 9120 + 228\n\\]\n\\[\n= 45600 + 9120 = 54720\n\\]\n\\[\n54720 + 228 = 54948\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using the difference of squares method:\n\n\\[\n228 = 234.5 - 6.5 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 241 = 234.5 + 6.5\n\\]\n\\[\n(234.5 - 6.5)(234.5 + 6.5) = (234.5)^2 - (6.5)^2\n\\]\n\\[\n(234.5)^2 = 54990.25 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad (6.5)^2 = 42.25\n\\]\n\\[\n54990.25 - 42.25 = 54948\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 228 and 241 is \\(\\boxed{54948}\\).",
