rtial: 40,600\n\nThird partial: 406,000\n\nAdding them together:\n\n4,872 + 40,600 = 45,472\n\n45,472 + 406,000 = 451,472\n\nSo that's consistent with the second method. Therefore, the correct answer should be 451,472.\n\nBut wait, in my first attempt, I confused numbers and got a different result, but after correcting, both methods give me 451,472. So that's probably the right answer.\n\nAlternatively, let me do it another way to confirm. Let's use the distributive property again but breaking into different parts.\n\nLet me consider 812 \u00d7 556 as (800 + 12) \u00d7 (500 + 50 + 6).\n\nExpanding this:\n\n800\u00d7500 + 800\u00d750 + 800\u00d76 + 12\u00d7500 + 12\u00d750 + 12\u00d76.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n800\u00d7500 = 400,000\n\n800\u00d750 = 40,000\n\n800\u00d76 = 4,800\n\n12\u00d7500 = 6,000\n\n12\u00d750 = 600\n\n12\u00d76 = 72\n\nNow adding all these:\n\n400,000 + 40,000 = 440,000\n\n440,000 + 4,800 = 444,800\n\n444,800 + 6,000 = 450,800\n\n450,800 + 600 = 451,400\n\n451,400 + 72 = 451,472.\n\nSame result again. So confident now it's correct.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps use calculator-like step-by-step:\n\nMultiplying 812 \u00d7 556:\n\nFirst, write it down:\n\n       812\n     \u00d7 556\n     -------\n       4872  (812\u00d76)\n      40600  (812\u00d750, shifted one position)\n     406000  (812\u00d7500, shifted two positions)\n     --------\n     451472\n\nYes, adding those gives 4872 + 40600 = 45472, plus 406000 gives 451,472.\n\nTherefore, the correct product of 812 and 556 is 451,472.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 812 and 556 is \\boxed{451472}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 812 and 556, we can use the standard multiplication method and verify using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, using the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. Multiply 812 by 6 (units place):\n   \\[\n   812 \\times 6 = 4872\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 812 by 50 (tens place, the 5 in 556 represents 50):\n   \\[\n   812 \\times 50 = 40600\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 812 by 500 (hundreds place, the first 5 in 556 represents 500):\n   \\[\n   812 \\times 500 = 406000\n   \\]\n\n4. Add all the partial products together:\n   \\[\n   4872 + 40600 + 406000 = 451472\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n\nBreaking down the numbers:\n\\[\n812 \\times 556 = (800 + 12) \\times (500 + 50 + 6)\n\\]\n\nExpanding and calculating each term:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n800 \\times 500 &= 400000, \\\\\n800 \\times 50 &= 40000, \\\\\n800 \\times 6 &= 4800, \\\\\n12 \\times 500 &= 6000, \\\\\n12 \\times 50 &= 600, \\\\\n12 \\times 6 &= 72.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nAdding all the terms together:\n\\[\n400000 + 40000 + 4800 + 6000 + 600 + 72 = 451472\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 812 and 556 is \\(\\boxed{451472}\\).",
