nThen multiply by 110: 5,776 \u00d7100 =577,600 and 5,776 \u00d710 =57,760. Adding those gives 577,600 +57,760 =635,360.\n\nSame answer again. So I think that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 722 and 880 is 635,360.\n\nWait, but just to be thorough, maybe use another approach like the lattice method?\n\nHmm, lattice might take longer, but let me try.\n\nBut maybe not necessary since all methods so far have given me 635,360. Let me check with a calculator's logic.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do 722 \u00d7 800 = 577,600. Then 722 \u00d780 = 57,760. Adding those two gives 577,600 +57,760 = 635,360. Yep, that's the same as before.\n\nAlternatively, if I do 880 \u00d7700 =616,000 and 880 \u00d722=19,360, then adding them gives 616,000+19,360=635,360. Also same result.\n\nAlright, so I think that's solid. Therefore, the answer is 635,360.\n\nBut just to make sure, let me verify with another method. Let's do the standard multiplication step by step:\n\nMultiplying 722 by 880.\n\nFirst, write it down:\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0722\n\u00d7\u00a0880\n--------\n\nSince 880 has a 0 in the units place, first multiply by 0:\n\n722 \u00d70 =0, so write 0.\n\nThen multiply by 8 (tens place):\n\n722 \u00d78 = 5,776. Since it's the tens place, shift one position to the left:\n\n5,7760\n\nThen multiply by 8 (hundreds place):\n\n722 \u00d78 =5,776, shifted two positions left:\n\n577,600\n\nNow add them together:\n\n\u00a0\u00a057760\n+577600\n--------\n\u00a0635,360\n\nYes, adding 57,760 and 577,600 gives 635,360.\n\nAlright, that's consistent. I think that's the correct answer. I tried multiple methods and cross-verified. So I'm confident.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 722 and 880 is \\boxed{635360}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 722 and 880, we can use the standard multiplication method along with breaking down the numbers for clarity.\n\nFirst, break down 880 into 800 + 80:\n\\[\n722 \\times 880 = 722 \\times (800 + 80)\n\\]\n\nCalculate each part separately:\n\\[\n722 \\times 800 = 722 \\times 8 \\times 100 = 5776 \\times 100 = 577600\n\\]\n\\[\n722 \\times 80 = 722 \\times 8 \\times 10 = 5776 \\times 10 = 57760\n\\]\n\nAdd the results of the two parts together:\n\\[\n577600 + 57760 = 635360\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can also use the distributive property by expanding both numbers:\n\\[\n(700 + 22) \\times (800 + 80)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 700 \\times 800 + 700 \\times 80 + 22 \\times 800 + 22 \\times 80\n\\]\n\\[\n= 560000 + 56000 + 17600 + 1760\n\\]\n\\[\n= 560000 + 56000 = 616000\n\\]\n\\[\n17600 + 1760 = 19360\n\\]\n\\[\n616000 + 19360 = 635360\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the result. Therefore, the product of 722 and 880 is \\(\\boxed{635360}\\).",
