s correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 921 and 334 is \\boxed{307614}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 921 and 334, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 921 by 4 (units place):\n   \\[\n   921 \\times 4 = 3684\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 921 by 30 (tens place, so 3 in the tens place):\n   \\[\n   921 \\times 3 = 2763 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero)} \\quad 27630\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 921 by 300 (hundreds place, so 3 in the hundreds place):\n   \\[\n   921 \\times 3 = 2763 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros)} \\quad 276300\n   \\]\n\n4. Add all three results together:\n   \\[\n   3684 + 27630 + 276300\n   \\]\n\n5. Perform the addition step-by-step:\n   - Add the first two results:\n     \\[\n     3684 + 27630 = 31314\n     \\]\n   - Add the result to the third result:\n     \\[\n     31314 + 276300 = 307614\n     \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n- Break down the numbers and compute each term:\n  \\[\n  921 \\times 334 = (900 + 21) \\times (300 + 30 + 4)\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  = 900 \\times 300 + 900 \\times 30 + 900 \\times 4 + 21 \\times 300 + 21 \\times 30 + 21 \\times 4\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  = 270000 + 27000 + 3600 + 6300 + 630 + 84\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  = 270000 + 27000 = 297000\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  297000 + 3600 = 300600\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  300600 + 6300 = 306900\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  306900 + 630 = 307530\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  307530 + 84 = 307614\n  \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 921 and 334 is \\(\\boxed{307614}\\).",
