mpute 947 \u00d7 900.\n\nFirst, compute 947 \u00d7 9, then shift two places to the left (multiply by 100).\n\n947 \u00d7 9:\n\n7 \u00d7 9 = 63. Write 3, carryover 6.\n\n4 \u00d7 9 = 36 + 6 = 42. Write 2, carryover 4.\n\n9 \u00d7 9 = 81 + 4 = 85. So that gives 8,523.\n\nTherefore, 947 \u00d7 900 = 852,300.\n\nNow, we have three partial products:\n\n1. 947 \u00d7 8 = 7,576\n\n2. 947 \u00d7 80 = 75,760\n\n3. 947 \u00d7 900 = 852,300\n\nNow, add them all together:\n\nStart by adding the first two:\n\n7,576 + 75,760 = ?\n\n7,576 + 75,760:\n\nAdd units: 6 + 0 = 6\n\nTens: 7 + 6 = 13, write 3, carryover 1\n\nHundreds: 5 + 7 + 1 = 13, write 3, carryover 1\n\nThousands: 7 (from 7,576) + 5 (from 75,760) + 1 = 13. So that's 13, write 3 and carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands: 0 + 7 + 1 = 8.\n\nSo total is 83,336.\n\nWait, let me check again:\n\n7,576\n\n+75,760\n\n------------\n\nAdding:\n\n7,576\n\n+75,760\n\n= 83,336? Let's do it step by step:\n\n7,576 + 75,760:\n\nBreakdown:\n\n7,000 + 70,000 = 77,000\n\n500 + 5,000 = 5,500 \u2192 total so far 82,500\n\n70 + 760 = 830 \u2192 total 83,330\n\n6 + 0 =6 \u2192 total 83,336. Yes, correct.\n\nNow add the third partial product: 852,300 + 83,336.\n\nLet's compute that:\n\n852,300 + 83,336:\n\nBreakdown:\n\n800,000 + 80,000 = 880,000\n\n52,000 + 3,000 = 55,000 \u2192 total 935,000\n\n300 + 336 = 636 \u2192 total 935,636?\n\nWait, let me do it step by step:\n\n852,300\n\n+ 83,336\n\n________\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n0 +6 =6\n\n0+3=3\n\n3 +3=6\n\n2 (from 852,300's thousands place) + 3 (from 83,336's thousands place) = 5 \u2192 5 in thousands place.\n\n5 (from 852,300's ten thousands place) + 8 (from 83,336's ten thousands place) = 13 \u2192 write 3 in ten thousands place, carryover 1.\n\n8 (from 852,300's hundred thousands place) + 0 (since 83,336 has none) plus the carried over 1 =9 in hundred thousands place.\n\nSo total is 935,636.\n\nWait, let me verify with another method: 852,300 + 83,336.\n\n852,300 + 80,000 = 932,300\n\nThen add 3,336: 932,300 + 3,336 = 935,636. Yes, correct.\n\nTherefore, the total product is 935,636.\n\nWait, but let me check with another method to be sure. Maybe using the distributive property:\n\n947 \u00d7 988 = 947 \u00d7 (1000 - 12) = 947\u00d71000 - 947\u00d712.\n\nCompute each part:\n\n947 \u00d7 1000 = 947,000\n\n947 \u00d7 12 = ?\n\n947 \u00d7 10 = 9,470\n\n947 \u00d7 2 = 1,894\n\nSo 9,470 + 1,894 = 11,364\n\nTherefore, subtract: 947,000 - 11,364 = 935,636. \n\nYes! That's the same result. So that confirms it.\n\nAlternatively, let me do another multiplication check with the standard algorithm again to ensure I didn't make an error in the initial steps.\n\nCompute 947 \u00d7 988:\n\nStart with 947 \u00d7 8 =7,576 (correct)\n\n947 \u00d7 80 =75,760 (correct)\n\n947 \u00d7 900 =852,300 (correct)\n\nAdding them gives 7,576 + 75,760 = 83,336; then 83,336 + 852,300 =935,636. All steps check out.\n\nAlternatively, using another approach: breaking down both numbers.\n\n947 \u00d7 988 = (900 + 40 + 7) \u00d7 (900 + 80 + 8). But that might be more complex, but let's try multiplying terms:\n\n= 900\u00d7900 + 900\u00d780 + 900\u00d78 + 40\u00d7900 + 40\u00d780 + 40\u00d78 +7\u00d7900 +7\u00d780 +7\u00d78\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n900\u00d7900 = 810,000\n\n900\u00d780 =72,000\n\n900\u00d78 =7,200\n\n40\u00d7900 =36,000\n\n40\u00d780=3,200\n\n40\u00d78=320\n\n7\u00d7900=6,300\n\n7\u00d780=560\n\n7\u00d78=56\n\nNow add them all together:\n\nStart with 810,000 +72,000 = 882,000\n\n+7,200 \u2192889,200\n\n+36,000 \u2192925,200\n\n+3,200 \u2192928,400\n\n+320 \u2192928,720\n\n+6,300 \u2192935,020\n\n+560 \u2192935,580\n\n+56 \u2192935,636. \n\nYes, same result. So definitely 935,636.\n\nTherefore, the product of 947 and 988 is 935,636.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 947 and 988 is \\boxed{935636}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 947 and 988, we can use the standard algorithm for multiplication:\n\n1. **Multiply 947 by the units digit (8) of 988:**\n   \\[\n   947 \\