eft).\n\nAdding them:\n\n\u2003\u20036,948\n\n+54,040\n\n=60,988\n\nThen 60,988 +231,600 = 292,588.\n\nSo the product is 292,588.\n\nWait, but let me confirm with another method to be sure. Maybe using the standard vertical multiplication step-by-step.\n\nFirst, multiply 772 by 9:\n\n7 \u00d7 9 = 63, write down 3 and carry over 6.\n\n7 \u00d7 9 = 63 +6 = 69, write down 9 and carry over 6.\n\n7 \u00d7 9 = 63 +6 = 69. So 6,948. That's correct.\n\nNext, multiply 772 by 70. Since it's the tens place, we'll do 7 \u00d7 772 and then add a zero.\n\n7 \u00d7 2 =14, write 4 carry 1.\n\n7 \u00d77 =49 +1=50, write 0 carry5.\n\n7\u00d77=49+5=54. So 5,404. Then add a zero: 54,040.\n\nThird, multiply 772 by 300. 3 \u00d7772=2,316, then add two zeros: 231,600.\n\nAdding all three:\n\n6,948\n\n54,040\n\n231,600\n\nTotal: 6,948 +54,040 =60,988; 60,988+231,600=292,588.\n\nAlternatively, using another approach: (700 +72) \u00d7 (300 +79).\n\nBut that might complicate more, but let's see:\n\n(700 +72)(300 +79) =700\u00d7300 +700\u00d779 +72\u00d7300 +72\u00d779.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n700\u00d7300 = 210,000.\n\n700\u00d779 = 55,300.\n\n72\u00d7300 =21,600.\n\n72\u00d779: 70\u00d779=5,530 and 2\u00d779=158. So total 5,530+158=5,688.\n\nNow sum all four:\n\n210,000 +55,300 =265,300.\n\n265,300 +21,600=286,900.\n\n286,900 +5,688=292,588.\n\nSame result. So this confirms the answer is correct.\n\nAlternatively, check with calculator steps:\n\n772 \u00d7 379.\n\nCompute 772 \u00d7 300 = 231,600.\n\n772 \u00d7 70 = 54,040.\n\n772 \u00d7 9 =6,948.\n\nAdding those gives 231,600 +54,040 = 285,640 +6,948 =292,588.\n\nYes, so I think that's the correct answer. I must have confused myself earlier when I was thinking of different numbers, but now focusing on 772 and 379, the result is 292,588.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 772 and 379 is \\boxed{292588}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 772 and 379, we can use the distributive property and break down the multiplication into smaller parts