967 = 890,607. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another approach like the difference of squares or something, but these numbers might not be suitable. Alternatively, perhaps cross-verifying with approximate calculations.\n\nEstimate: 967 is approximately 1000, and 921 is approximately 900. So 1000 \u00d7 900 = 900,000. The exact answer should be a bit less because both numbers are slightly less than their rounded values. 967 is 33 less than 1000, and 921 is 79 less than 1000. Wait, but maybe not helpful.\n\nAlternatively, let's compute 967 \u00d7 921:\n\nAlternatively, reverse the multiplication: 921 \u00d7 967. Let me see if I get the same result.\n\n921 \u00d7 967:\n\nFirst, 921 \u00d7 7 = 6,447.\n\n921 \u00d7 60 = 55,260.\n\n921 \u00d7 900 = 828,900.\n\nAdding those: 6,447 + 55,260 = 61,707; plus 828,900 = 890,607. Same result. Okay, so that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, I believe the correct product is 890,607.\n\nWait, but in my initial thinking process, I started with different numbers (380 and 660) due to a misread. But after correcting that, the process is solid. So the final answer should be 890,607. Let me just check once again with another method, perhaps breaking down the numbers.\n\nAlternatively, express 967 as (900 + 60 +7) and 921 as (900 + 20 +1). Then multiply each term:\n\n(900 + 60 +7)(900 + 20 +1) = 900\u00d7900 + 900\u00d720 + 900\u00d71 + 60\u00d7900 + 60\u00d720 + 60\u00d71 + 7\u00d7900 + 7\u00d720 + 7\u00d71.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n900\u00d7900 = 810,000\n\n900\u00d720 = 18,000\n\n900\u00d71 = 900\n\n60\u00d7900 = 54,000\n\n60\u00d720 = 1,200\n\n60\u00d71 = 60\n\n7\u00d7900 = 6,300\n\n7\u00d720 = 140\n\n7\u00d71 = 7.\n\nNow adding all these together:\n\nStart with 810,000 + 18,000 = 828,000.\n\n828,000 + 900 = 828,900.\n\n828,900 + 54,000 = 882,900.\n\n882,900 + 1,200 = 884,100.\n\n884,100 + 60 = 884,160.\n\n884,160 + 6,300 = 890,460.\n\n890,460 + 140 = 890,600.\n\n890,600 + 7 = 890,607.\n\nPerfect, that matches the previous results.