ure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can compute 446*448 directly using another method.\n\nLet me write it out as:\n\n446 * 448 = 446*(400 + 40 + 8) = 446*400 + 446*40 + 446*8.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n446 * 400 = 178,400.\n\n446 * 40 = 17,840.\n\n446 * 8 = 3,568.\n\nAdding these together: 178,400 +17,840 = 196,240.\n\nThen add 3,568: 196,240 +3,568 = 199,808.\n\nSame result. Okay, so that's good. So the answer is 199,808.\n\nWait, but let me confirm once more with another method, perhaps the standard multiplication:\n\n   446\nx 448\n--------\n\nFirst multiply 446 by 8: 3,568.\n\nThen multiply 446 by 40: 17,840 shifted one position (add a zero at the end): 17,840*10=178,400? Wait, no. Wait, actually, 448 is 4 hundreds, 4 tens, 8 units. So:\n\nFirst step: 446 * 8 = 3,568.\n\nSecond step: 446 * 40 = 446 *4 *10 = 1,784 *10 = 17,840. So write this shifted one position to the left.\n\nThird step: 446 * 400 = 446*4 *100 = 1,784 *100 = 178,400. Shifted two positions left.\n\nThen add all three:\n\n   3,568\n  17,840\n+178,400\n----------\nTotal:\n\n3,568 +17,840 = 21,408.\n\n21,408 +178,400 = 199,808. Yep, same result.\n\nOkay, that seems consistent. So the correct answer is 199,808.\n\nWait, but in my initial steps I confused the numbers as 310 and 783, but then realized that was a mistake. So the final conclusion is 446*448=199,808.\n\nTherefore, the product is 199,808.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 446 and 448 is \\boxed{199808}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 446 and 448, we can use the difference of squares formula since the numbers are symmetric around 447. \n\nNotice that:\n\\[\n446 = 447 - 1 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 448 = 447 + 1\n\\]\n\nUsing the difference of squares formula:\n\\[\n(447 - 1)(447 + 1) = 447^2 - 1^2\n\\]\n\nFirst, we compute \\(447^2\\):\n\\[\n447^2 = (400 + 47)^2 = 400^2 + 2 \\cdot 400 \\cdot 47 + 47^2\n\\]\n\\[\n400^2 = 160000\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 400 \\cdot 47 = 800 \\cdot 47 = 37600\n\\]\n\\[\n47^2 = 2209\n\\]\nAdding these together:\n\\[\n160000 + 37600 + 2209 = 199809\n\\]\n\nSubtracting 1 from the result:\n\\[\n447^2 - 1 = 199809 - 1 = 199808\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can also compute the product directly:\n\\[\n446 \\times 448 = 446 \\times (400 + 40 + 8)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 446 \\times 400 + 446 \\times 40 + 446 \\times 8\n\\]\n\\[\n= 178400 + 17840 + 3568\n\\]\n\\[\n= 178400 + 17840 = 196240\n\\]\n\\[\n196240 + 3568 = 199808\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 446 and 448 is \\(\\boxed{199808}\\).",
