 632,800. Yep, same answer.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident that the correct product of 904 and 700 is 632,800.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 904 and 700 is \\boxed{632800}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 904 and 700, we can break down the multiplication into simpler steps:\n\n1. Recognize that 700 can be expressed as \\(7 \\times 100\\).\n2. First, multiply 904 by 7:\n   \\[\n   904 \\times 7 = (900 \\times 7) + (4 \\times 7) = 6300 + 28 = 6328\n   \\]\n3. Then, multiply the result by 100 (which is equivalent to adding two zeros):\n   \\[\n   6328 \\times 100 = 632800\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 904 and 700 is \\(\\boxed{632800}\\).",
