culation. So that's a good check.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident the correct answer is 113,920.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 356 and 320 is \\boxed{113920}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 356 and 320, we can break down the multiplication using the distributive property and standard multiplication steps:\n\n1. **Break down 320 into 300 and 20**:\n   \\[\n   356 \\times 320 = 356 \\times (300 + 20)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate each part separately**:\n   - Multiply 356 by 300:\n     \\[\n     356 \\times 300 = 356 \\times 3 \\times 100 = 1068 \\times 100 = 106800\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 356 by 20:\n     \\[\n     356 \\times 20 = 356 \\times 2 \\times 10 = 712 \\times 10 = 7120\n     \\]\n\n3. **Add the results of the two parts**:\n   \\[\n   106800 + 7120 = 113920\n   \\]\n\n4. **Verification using standard multiplication**:\n   - Multiply 356 by 0 (units place of 320) gives 0.\n   - Multiply 356 by 2 (tens place, which is 20) and shift one position left:\n     \\[\n     356 \\times 2 = 712 \\quad \\text{(shifted to 7120)}\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 356 by 3 (hundreds place, which is 300) and shift two positions left:\n     \\[\n     356 \\times 3 = 1068 \\quad \\text{(shifted to 106800)}\n     \\]\n   - Add all results:\n     \\[\n     0 + 7120 + 106800 = 113920\n     \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 356 and 320 is \\(\\boxed{113920}\\).",
