ift one position to the left:\n\n613 \u00d79 = 5,517 \u2192 shifted left by one: 55,170\n\nThird, multiply 613 by 8 (hundreds place, which is 800). Shift two positions to the left:\n\n613 \u00d78 = 4,904 \u2192 shifted left by two: 490,400\n\nNow add them together:\n\n  3,678\n\n+55,170\n\n+490,400\n\n------------\n\nStart with the first two:\n\n3,678 +55,170 = 58,848\n\nThen add 490,400:\n\n58,848 + 490,400 = 549,248\n\nSame result. So that seems correct.\n\nWait but let me do it step by step addition:\n\n3,678\n\n+55,170\n\n= 3,678 +50,000 =53,678; 53,678+5,170=58,848.\n\nThen 58,848 +490,400:\n\n58,848 + 400,000 =458,848\n\n458,848 +90,400 =549,248.\n\nYes.\n\nAlternatively, to verify, let's compute 613 \u00d7 896.\n\nAlternatively, compute 613 \u00d7 900 = 551,700\n\nThen subtract 613 \u00d74 = 2,452 \u2192 551,700 -2,452 =549,248.\n\nYes, that works. So the answer is 549,248.\n\nWait but I initially thought I messed up the first time, but now after doing it step by step, it seems correct. So the product of 613 and 896 is 549,248.\n\nI think that's correct. Let me check with another method, perhaps using a calculator approximation.\n\n613 \u00d7 900 is 551,700. Since 896 is 4 less than 900, so subtract 613\u00d74 = 2,452 from 551,700 \u2192 551,700 -2,452 =549,248. So that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, 600\u00d7900 =540,000. Then 13\u00d7900=11,700. So total would be 540,000+11,700=551,700. Then subtract 613\u00d74 as before. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps do (600+13)(900-4) = 600\u00d7900 -600\u00d74 +13\u00d7900 -13\u00d74.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n600\u00d7900 =540,000\n\n-600\u00d74= -2,400\n\n+13\u00d7900=+11,700\n\n-13\u00d74= -52\n\nTotal: 540,000 -2,400 =537,600; 537,600 +11,700 =549,300; 549,300 -52 =549,248.\n\nYes, that's another way and it matches. So I think the correct answer is 549,248.\n\nWait, but initially when I tried doing it step by step, I messed up some steps and got confused, but now with different methods, all leading to 549,24